	('c08ad93b-a7a2-451f-ada1-46fbc6b145bd', 'ea155ac4-eb3a-4e24-a4be-84f0143f4348', '111e6b4a-cb10-4969-b64b-8deb59bcd3fa', 'Can I upload a document here?', 'microtranslation', '2025-02-07 00:23:36.367943+00', '2025-02-07 00:23:36.367943+00', NULL, NULL),
	('fff322dd-aefb-4e3f-8abc-8275c3c6c6db', '6ba21501-22c2-4705-850f-d07844f4dffd', '494ef97c-4539-419c-aa65-051ecb851efc', 'This marks my initial engagement.', 'microtranslation', '2025-02-13 19:46:22.930049+00', '2025-02-13 19:46:22.930049+00', NULL, NULL),
	('babd1932-76cb-4f79-a8fc-da3cc48dbeab', '6ff6d5f4-9cc6-4a8e-9c48-608201bb392d', NULL, 'Chase Orton - empowering teachers to take control of their professional growth, Chase Orton - fostering a culture of collaboration and mutual growth among teachers', 'idea', '2025-02-14 22:55:45.641212+00', '2025-02-14 22:55:45.641212+00', NULL, NULL),
	('50851502-1bf4-418b-b117-f1dfa64dca81', '6ba21501-22c2-4705-850f-d07844f4dffd', NULL, 'Diego - hands-on learning and iterative process, Diego - in-person learning and perceiving vibes', 'idea', '2025-02-15 00:35:06.52277+00', '2025-02-15 00:35:06.52277+00', NULL, NULL),
	('f0ccfbdc-d3c1-43a1-b746-422d6464f22d', '6ba21501-22c2-4705-850f-d07844f4dffd', NULL, 'Diego - traditional learning and school system limitations', 'idea', '2025-02-15 00:35:09.500597+00', '2025-02-15 00:35:09.500597+00', NULL, NULL),
	('7a229e4a-e6af-49b8-a0a7-9015bc13439b', '4e8fa647-0aad-4962-a879-826b7edc6dd4', NULL, 'Lorri E.: I think that if learners do not understand the benefit of actually doing the thinking themselves, that it could be detrimental to learners if they use it as a tool to enhance their real learning.', 'idea', '2025-02-18 18:48:49.008172+00', '2025-02-18 18:48:49.008172+00', NULL, NULL),
	('c560c702-c139-436f-a918-5e442094f476', '4e8fa647-0aad-4962-a879-826b7edc6dd4', NULL, 'Lorri E. - Concerns about AI replacing human thinking and learning, Jeff C. - Challenges of segregating students based on ability', 'idea', '2025-02-18 18:48:51.859072+00', '2025-02-18 18:48:51.859072+00', NULL, NULL),
	('71669196-c777-41bc-9b3d-3e9f7df168ac', '4e8fa647-0aad-4962-a879-826b7edc6dd4', NULL, 'Lorri E. - Using AI to enhance thinking and learning, Jeff C. - Creating inclusive learning environments', 'idea', '2025-02-18 18:48:53.440567+00', '2025-02-18 18:48:53.440567+00', NULL, NULL),
	('a76cc68b-57c4-47c6-b8ae-20618d797c00', 'bd47a56c-b275-4972-987f-30b0cd993f17', NULL, 'Tom Thorpe - Student agency and personalized learning, Simone Leech - Impactful projects and mental health education', 'idea', '2025-02-19 16:22:28.890109+00', '2025-02-19 16:22:28.890109+00', NULL, NULL),
	('37a2b4f8-06a0-4e35-8b65-0547e7a2bb1d', 'bd47a56c-b275-4972-987f-30b0cd993f17', NULL, 'Tom Thorpe - Traditional education methods stifling student creativity, Tom Thorpe - Overemphasis on teacher-led storytelling in classrooms', 'idea', '2025-02-19 16:23:02.705614+00', '2025-02-19 16:23:02.705614+00', NULL, NULL),
	('9f81a2fd-f93a-4d12-a444-cbef5dc2ba21', 'bd47a56c-b275-4972-987f-30b0cd993f17', NULL, 'Tom Thorpe: ''Let the kids tell their story, their story isn''t your story, and their story isn''t one story. Let each story shine, let each story be told and be known, and let it inform and be integrated into it.''', 'idea', '2025-02-19 16:23:19.748528+00', '2025-02-19 16:23:19.748528+00', NULL, NULL),
	('b75e288a-fd14-4970-a603-4a7cb8db90db', '44d8b840-888f-4849-9111-b52ada8f4599', NULL, 'Brittany S. - AI tools for special education, particularly for differentiation and personalized learning, Brittany S. - Technology integration to support students with exceptionalities', 'idea', '2025-02-19 17:19:29.605199+00', '2025-02-19 17:19:29.605199+00', NULL, NULL),
	('d666ee10-c661-494d-8f83-70c4d897a0ea', '44d8b840-888f-4849-9111-b52ada8f4599', NULL, 'Brittany S. - Standardized testing, which she believes should be changed, Brittany S. - The need for public schools to adapt more to support students with diverse needs', 'idea', '2025-02-19 17:19:42.691843+00', '2025-02-19 17:19:42.691843+00', NULL, NULL),
	('423f0be9-dd91-4601-ac41-8f89e89c398d', '44d8b840-888f-4849-9111-b52ada8f4599', NULL, 'Brittany S.: ''I think that those tools that help students with exceptionalities can be streamlined to help all students. So taking that box... and maybe changing the shape or even letting some of those walls down.''', 'idea', '2025-02-19 17:19:47.064202+00', '2025-02-19 17:19:47.064202+00', NULL, NULL),
	('36b3a1b8-18ee-4a4d-b509-b6ce959ab2a7', '86f608d8-be4a-47b2-9c8a-b0b3fb52dabb', NULL, 'Michael M. - integrating technology into classrooms to support staff and students, Michael M. - creating learning experiences that empower teachers', 'idea', '2025-02-21 15:27:45.317572+00', '2025-02-21 15:27:45.317572+00', NULL, NULL),
	('e2890f04-32b5-4b06-bdcd-554572556ccc', '86f608d8-be4a-47b2-9c8a-b0b3fb52dabb', NULL, 'Michael M.: My stance on learning and teaching, I would say, is to never stop, always continue learning.', 'idea', '2025-02-21 15:28:22.800476+00', '2025-02-21 15:28:22.800476+00', NULL, NULL),
	('b295737a-5b6b-4c0d-9768-c3967bb88c4c', 'f66f1077-2f65-43f4-95bd-cbf9f328b38b', '8bb32e7a-2026-40c6-8057-b513f1f14441', 'Reader''s writing style example 1: Greetings! Thrilled to be part of this grand venture. Could you kindly enlighten me on the subsequent phases of this journey?

Reader''s writing style example 2: Salutations! It is with great excitement that I find myself amidst such esteemed company. Pray tell, what actions am I to undertake henceforth?

Translation to match the reader''s writing style:

Salutations and felicitations! I find myself at the commencement of this illustrious endeavour. Would you be so kind as to guide me through the ensuing stages of this adventure?', 'microtranslation', '2025-02-22 00:15:26.550622+00', '2025-02-22 00:15:26.550622+00', NULL, NULL),
	('358e4af2-8fdc-4d55-94c6-c967d1e8c2e4', '44d8b840-888f-4849-9111-b52ada8f4599', NULL, 'Brittany S. - AI tools for special education, particularly for differentiation and personalized learning, Brittany S. - Technology integration to support students with exceptionalities', 'idea', '2025-02-25 19:09:49.734346+00', '2025-02-25 19:09:49.734346+00', NULL, NULL),
	('9dd4f360-d705-4231-a84e-00c06dcb203f', '44d8b840-888f-4849-9111-b52ada8f4599', NULL, 'Brittany S. - Standardized testing, which she believes should be changed, Brittany S. - The need for public schools to adapt more to support students with diverse needs', 'idea', '2025-02-25 19:09:51.954073+00', '2025-02-25 19:09:51.954073+00', NULL, NULL),
	('f01578bf-fbfe-4850-be07-3a72d68c7b12', '44d8b840-888f-4849-9111-b52ada8f4599', NULL, 'Brittany S.: ''I think that those tools that help students with exceptionalities can be streamlined to help all students. So taking that box... and maybe changing the shape or even letting some of those walls down.''', 'idea', '2025-02-25 19:09:52.818525+00', '2025-02-25 19:09:52.818525+00', NULL, NULL),
	('42d72386-cfaa-429b-816f-c211a6e8df32', '44d8b840-888f-4849-9111-b52ada8f4599', NULL, 'Brittany S.: ''I think that those tools that help students with exceptionalities can be streamlined to help all students. So taking that box... and maybe changing the shape or even letting some of those walls down.''', 'idea', '2025-03-03 20:54:18.100896+00', '2025-03-03 20:54:18.100896+00', NULL, NULL),
	('1b514ece-7214-4457-b94c-ef459538d0c5', 'ea155ac4-eb3a-4e24-a4be-84f0143f4348', '9b72fd15-d33c-47aa-8e08-c6077b91dbdd', 'Can I upload a file here?', 'microtranslation', '2025-02-07 00:32:44.133272+00', '2025-03-25 00:34:06.81058+00', 3, 1),
	('7ae5aec5-6a82-436c-9085-a7206651e2cc', 'd2928ae9-b58d-4c7a-bc24-53d1567bba0e', NULL, 'You’re not afraid of the messy middle.

Bias, hallucinations, limitations—you’re choosing to name what’s hard, not avoid it. That’s real leadership in this space. We NEED this leadership.', 'idea', '2025-05-09 20:56:10.487228+00', '2025-05-09 20:56:10.487228+00', NULL, NULL),
	('0d7ff7b7-cb46-4c36-aa00-d11a8106565e', '4c3a7dc1-10fb-45d6-a20e-f89f0e73af73', NULL, '### Participant: Allison Ogle

#### Primary Flow Activity
Allison Ogle expresses a wide array of interests and hobbies that contribute to her personal fulfillment and joy. She mentions her love for dance, specifically stating, "I take hip hop and tap dancing classes," which highlights her active engagement with movement and rhythm. Additionally, her passion for the arts is evident through her appreciation for painting, drawing, and coloring. She remarks, "I love doing art," showcasing her creative side. Music also plays a significant role in her leisure time, as she enjoys relaxing and immersing herself in it: "I love just sitting down and listening to music or dancing and all that jazz." Lastly, reading is another cherished activity for her, indicating her love for literature and storytelling.

#### Stance on Teaching and Learning
Allison articulates a progressive and collaborative view of teaching and learning, emphasizing that it is an "ongoing process." She strongly believes in the idea that "teachers are learners and learners can be teachers," advocating for a reciprocal relationship in the educational journey. This perspective suggests a focus on effort and a willingness to embrace "new ideas," which can foster a dynamic learning environment where continuous improvement is prioritized.

#### Professional Roles
In her professional capacity, Allison serves as the MTSS (Multi-Tiered System of Supports) coordinator at an elementary school, overseeing grades pre-K through 4th grade. This role reflects her commitment to supporting the academic and emotional development of young learners. Her enthusiasm for learning about "new AI tools" indicates her dedication to integrating innovative resources into her work, aiming to enhance her effectiveness as an MTSS coordinator.

#### Personal Interests Influencing Professional Philosophy
Allison''s engagement in creative activities like dance, art, and music potentially enriches her educational approach. Her passions for artistic expression may translate into strategies that incorporate creativity into learning, thereby appealing to a diverse range of learners. Furthermore, her love for reading can inform her ability to engage students with stories and literature, creating a more relatable and enriched educational experience.

In summary, Allison Ogle embodies a philosophy of continuous learning and collaborative teaching. Her diverse hobbies not only provide personal enjoyment but also likely enhance her professional practice by fostering creativity and engagement within the classroom.', 'idea', '2025-03-04 04:45:17.559698+00', '2025-03-04 04:45:17.559698+00', NULL, NULL),
	('d363264f-14fb-4abc-8e0b-f951e90fb33b', '44d8b840-888f-4849-9111-b52ada8f4599', NULL, '### Insights on Allison Ogle

**Primary Flow Activities:**  
Allison Ogle finds joy in a variety of creative pursuits that highlight her artistic inclinations. She passionately shares, "A lot of stuff for fun. I love to dance. I take hip hop and tap dancing classes." This indicates a strong appreciation for movement and expression through dance. Additionally, she enjoys various forms of art, stating, "I love painting, I love drawing, I love coloring, all sorts of things." Her love for music is also noteworthy, as she enjoys, "just sitting down and listening to music or dancing." These activities suggest that Allison values artistic expression and physical activity as essential components for her personal well-being.

**Stance on Teaching and Learning:**  
Allison describes her educational philosophy by emphasizing the dynamic relationship between teachers and learners. She notes, "teaching and learning is an ongoing process; teachers are learners, and learners can be teachers." This reflects her belief in the reciprocal nature of education, where everyone can contribute to the learning environment. Her approach indicates an openness to "new ideas" and a commitment to "putting in effort," highlighting the importance of adaptability and continual learning in her teaching philosophy.

**Hats Worn at Work:**  
As an MTSS coordinator for grades pre-K through 4th grade, Allison takes on a significant role in supporting both teachers and students. Her position implies responsibilities related to educational frameworks, student support systems, and collaborative teaching strategies. By facilitating ongoing educational processes, she embodies the role of a learner and leader, fostering an inclusive environment for all stakeholders involved in the education system.

### Insights on Brittany Stevens

**Primary Flow Activities:**  
Brittany Stevens engages in activities that promote her physical and mental well-being. She mentions, "I''m a huge peloton girly so riding my bike right now," indicating a commitment to fitness and a structured workout routine. Additionally, she mentions yoga, journaling, and reading as her "flow activities." Through these practices, Brittany creates a balanced lifestyle that emphasizes mindfulness and physical health, illustrating her understanding of the importance of self-care in maintaining a positive mindset.

**Stance on Teaching and Learning:**  
Brittany expresses a deep commitment to education, believing that the role of teachers is pivotal in shaping students'' lives. She articulates, "we wear so many hats...we are sometimes counselors, we are sometimes parents and friends," underscoring the multifaceted responsibilities of educators. Her view on the role of learners is equally engaged, as she states, "the role of the learner is to show up for their work" while remaining open to feedback and new learning experiences. This philosophy not only champions student agency but also highlights the shared journey of learning between teachers and students.

**Hats Worn at Work:**  
As a special education teacher currently serving students in 2nd and 4th grades, Brittany acknowledges the diverse responsibilities that come with her profession. She mentions having a caseload of 15 students, a significant reduction from her previous 45-student caseload, which reflects her adaptability and commitment to each student’s needs. Her reflections on managing IEP meetings and her desire to create an inclusive and effective educational environment indicate that she takes on multiple roles, functioning as an advocate, mentor, and facilitator of learning within her school community.

In summary, both Allison and Brittany display a strong commitment to education, creative expression, and the importance of a supportive learning environment. Their personal and professional philosophies underscore the interconnectedness of teaching and learning, and their engagement in various activities showcases their holistic approaches to both life and work.', 'idea', '2025-03-04 04:58:22.792641+00', '2025-03-04 04:58:22.792641+00', NULL, NULL),
	('10a29bdb-3e15-4cd9-b234-88e4f8b1b7dd', '86f608d8-be4a-47b2-9c8a-b0b3fb52dabb', NULL, '### Insights from UpDuo Session Transcripts

#### Michael Meehan

**Primary Flow Activity:**  
Michael Meehan enjoys various activities outside of his professional responsibilities. He shares, "I love all Pittsburgh sports," indicating a passion for regional sports teams. Additionally, he expresses a fondness for the arts, saying, "I still love art. I love to paint." Further, he finds joy in being outdoors and states, "I like landscaping. I like plants." This reflects a personal interest in gardening, which he humorously ties to the passing of time, noting, "I guess that''s what happens when you get a little older."

**Stance on Teaching and Learning:**  
Michael emphasizes the importance of continuous learning and growth, stating, "there''s always going to be an opportunity for you to learn something new." He believes that learning is a reciprocal process where "you can learn something new from anyone you''re around," whether as a teacher or a learner. His philosophy centers on empowering others through education, as he aspires to "create learning experiences that empower teachers."

**Professional Roles:**  
In his role as a Digital Learning Coordinator in North Carolina, Michael supports both students and staff from K through 12 in integrating technology into educational practices. He addresses practical needs, helping educators with "learning how to post in their LMS" and exploring "AI" to enhance student engagement, showcasing his commitment to bridging technology with teaching.

---

#### Allison Ogle

**Primary Flow Activity:**  
Allison Ogle has a diverse set of interests that bring her joy beyond her professional life. She reveals her passion for dance, stating, "I love to dance. I take hip hop and tap dancing classes." In addition to dance, she enjoys artistic pursuits like painting and drawing, saying, "I love painting, I love drawing, I love coloring." She also highlights her appreciation for music, mentioning her love for "just sitting down and listening to music or dancing," along with reading, which is another cherished pastime.

**Stance on Teaching and Learning:**  
Allison''s perspective on education is rooted in the belief that "teaching and learning is an ongoing process." She values the idea that "teachers are learners and learners can be teachers," emphasizing the importance of effort and openness to new ideas in the learning journey. This dual role encapsulates her view that collaboration and mutual growth are essential components of effective education.

**Professional Roles:**  
In her capacity as an MTSS Coordinator for grades pre-K through 4th grade, Allison is focused on supporting students in their learning processes. She expresses enthusiasm for exploring "new AI tools" to enhance her role, showcasing her initiative to stay informed about modern educational strategies that can benefit her work at the elementary school level. Her role reflects a commitment to fostering a supportive learning environment for young learners.', 'idea', '2025-03-04 05:01:17.358202+00', '2025-03-04 05:01:17.358202+00', NULL, NULL),
	('65080d05-c7c5-4ea4-995c-b8946ea7e9a8', '86f608d8-be4a-47b2-9c8a-b0b3fb52dabb', NULL, '### Participant: Michael Meehan

#### Primary Flow Activity
Michael, also known as Mike, expressed a variety of interests that reflect his personality outside of his professional role. He mentioned being "a big sports guy" and specifically enjoys watching all Pittsburgh sports teams, including the Pirates, Steelers, and Penguins. Beyond sports, Mike has a creative side, stating, "I still love art. I love to paint." Additionally, he has developed a newfound passion for gardening and landscaping, describing himself as being "in the stage of my life where I become like a gardener, landscaper, just for fun." This blend of activities highlights a connection to both active and creative pursuits.

#### Stance on Teaching, Learning, and Education
Mike''s philosophy on teaching and learning centers around the idea of continuous growth and the importance of seizing learning opportunities. He stated, "My stance on learning and teaching, I would say, is to never stop, always continue learning." He believes that regardless of one''s role—be it teacher, learner, or presenter—there is always something valuable to learn from those around us. He emphasizes the importance of creating empowering learning experiences for teachers, showcasing how his philosophy influences his professional focus: "to create learning experiences that empower teachers and that they can use quickly in their own practice."

#### Professional Roles and Responsibilities
In his professional capacity, Mike serves as a Digital Learning Coordinator in North Carolina. His primary responsibility is to support both staff and students in integrating technology into their classrooms. He mentions specific support activities such as helping teachers learn how to post in their LMS and exploring AI to enhance engagement in technology-centered activities. His commitment to supporting educational professionals and ensuring effective use of technology underlines his dual role as both a facilitator of learning and a technology advocate in the educational landscape.

#### Personal Reflection
Mike''s insights not only reflect his dedication to fostering a positive learning environment but also demonstrate his belief in the potential for growth in all educational contexts. His varied interests and commitment to both learning and teaching indicate a well-rounded individual who values life beyond formal education. He affirms: "There''s always a chance to learn something new, whether it be as a teacher...or as a learner," emphasizing the interconnectedness of roles in the educational journey. This outlook can inspire both colleagues and students to embrace lifelong learning.', 'idea', '2025-03-04 05:03:37.980073+00', '2025-03-04 05:03:37.980073+00', NULL, NULL),
	('399e784f-7d02-449f-a91b-d852c2ffab1a', '713b8455-cc3b-4ab1-bcfb-255f93bf56b0', NULL, '### Participant: Jeff Ream

#### Primary Flow Activity
Jeff Ream expressed a particular passion for cooking, stating, "cooking is my definite activity. I enjoy creativity... it’s something that I do to relax." He describes his approach to cooking as creative and flexible, noting, "I''m not really a recipe follower... I do typically use a recipe for some sort of inspiration and then kind of improvise along the way." This indicates that cooking serves as both a creative outlet and a form of relaxation for him.

#### Stance on Teaching, Learning, and Education
In discussing his views on education, Jeff highlighted the imbalance he perceives in the responsibilities of student success, stating that "the adults often hold too much of the onus." He believes that this focus on the extremes—students who are achieving highly or struggling greatly—leaves "the folks who we can move probably the most in the middle behind." This reflection signifies his desire to explore ways to better support those middle-performing students, showcasing his commitment to a more balanced and inclusive educational approach.

#### Professional Roles and Responsibilities
In his professional life, Jeff identifies as a high school counselor, emphasizing his role in "integrating new technology within my practice as a counselor" and helping other counselors do the same. He expressed enthusiasm for connecting with others who share a passion for innovation in education, particularly with tools like AI, indicating his proactive approach to enhancing his counseling practice. Jeff also acknowledges the unique perspective he brings from his role, asserting that "as I''m not a classroom teacher necessarily," his insights could complement those of traditional educators. 

#### Summary
In summary, Jeff Ream''s insights from the UpDuo session reveal a multifaceted individual who finds joy in cooking while advocating for a more equitable educational landscape. He carries the responsibility of a high school counselor, seeking to leverage technology to enhance educational practices and address the needs of students who often go unnoticed in the traditional learning environment. His balanced view toward learning—encompassing both creativity in personal interests and a desire for systemic improvement in education—reflects a deep engagement with both his profession and personal pursuits.', 'idea', '2025-03-04 05:10:35.919774+00', '2025-03-04 05:10:35.919774+00', NULL, NULL),
	('93d88966-db6a-4efb-a646-a9c48fcac20d', 'bd47a56c-b275-4972-987f-30b0cd993f17', NULL, 'Tom Thorpe’s Vision for Using sideby.ai to Transform Learning & Community Building

### **From “Education” to “Educating”**  
Tom’s goal is to **move beyond the traditional concept of education**—which he describes as rigid and institutional—into **educating**, which is “this basic human core of existence, of curiosity.” He wants to build a **learning ecosystem** that allows students, educators, and the community to **engage in authentic, human-centered interactions** rather than just following prescribed systems.  

> “Education is like a thing. It’s a noun. It means school. It means school closing, school funding, tests. Educating is this… basic human core of existence, of curiosity.”  

### **sideby.ai as a Tool for Building Connected Learning Communities**  
Tom envisions **sideby.ai as a key platform for connecting learners, mentors, and educators** through guided conversations that generate meaningful insights.  

1. **Connecting Students from Different Backgrounds**  
   - Tom wants to **bridge the divide** between students from different socioeconomic and educational backgrounds by fostering **structured conversations** that reveal commonalities.  
   - Through sideby.ai, students from **REDI Lab** and other programs can engage in guided, recorded discussions and see their reflections **analyzed for themes and insights**.  

   > “Right now, it’s a challenge bringing the CA kids, who are like fancy private school kids, together with these urban charter school kids… they look different, they do that high school sizing-each-other-up thing.”  

   > “But what if we could take the conversations they’re having, analyze them, and say: ‘Here are the words you all are saying. Look how similar they are.’”  

2. **Bringing Mentorship into the Learning Process**  
   - He wants to **integrate sideby.ai as a mentorship platform** where REDI Lab alumni and outside experts can easily connect with students through scheduled 15-20 minute conversations.  
   - These conversations would be **recorded, analyzed, and stored** for both students and mentors, making learning **more intentional and cumulative**.  

   > “We want to try to engage some of our alumni as mentors. But what’s the platform, and how do you do it? Well, if we bring them into our closed community, then that’s a really great way to do 15 to 20-minute conversations where kids are getting mentorship, idea generation, transcripts, and data.”  

3. **Making Student Reflection & Check-Ins More Meaningful**  
   - Currently, REDI Lab runs regular **one-on-one check-ins** with students every six to eight days. Tom wants to **use sideby.ai to structure and record** these conversations, turning them into valuable data points.  
   - The **challenge is time**—he wants a way to **keep reflections focused** and **capture insights automatically**, so students and educators can track their growth.  

   > “Right now, we sit down and talk to them, and then they fill out a Google Sheet. But that’s like three steps—first, they have to go do it, then I have to go find the spreadsheet. But if it’s all on a dashboard with distilled insights, that’s huge.”  

4. **Using AI to Provide Actionable Coaching & Feedback**  
   - Tom wants sideby.ai to **help educators reflect on their teaching practices in real time** and ensure that student learning isn’t repetitive or stagnant.  
   - He envisions an AI-driven **feedback loop** that could flag when educators are using the same ineffective strategies, or suggest **new approaches based on student responses**.  

   > “What if we were to wear something that was recording us, and the rocket fuel went on to say: ‘Hey, you’ve already offered this to the kid three times, and they didn’t take it. Maybe don’t offer it again.’”  

   > “AI could be recording all these sessions with kids and say: ‘The reason they’re stuck is because you’re doing the same thing over and over again. Here are three ideas for something new to try.’”  

### **The Future: sideby.ai as a Core Tool for REDI Lab & Beyond**  
Tom sees sideby.ai as a **central tool for making learning more relational, reflective, and community-driven**. He is interested in launching a **closed community version** for REDI Lab, where all student check-ins, mentorship conversations, and learning reflections are stored and analyzed for insights.  

> “While they’re in REDI Lab, this is your tool. You’re capturing all these really rich, valuable conversations.”  

Ultimately, he wants **sideby.ai to empower learners and educators alike**, making reflection, mentorship, and collaboration **seamless and actionable**.  

> “Let’s find a way to use this moment to get rid of these things so that we can love kids.”', 'idea', '2025-03-05 19:46:56.746685+00', '2025-03-05 19:46:56.746685+00', NULL, NULL),
	('2d122af5-ce56-413f-a870-0f021ae662c4', '713b8455-cc3b-4ab1-bcfb-255f93bf56b0', NULL, '#### ### Common Themes and Patterns
The transcripts from the UpDuo sessions reveal a prominent theme centered around the integration of technology in education, particularly within the counseling domain. Jeff, the high school counselor, emphasizes his passion for utilizing AI tools—such as ChatGPT and Claude—to enhance educational practices. A secondary theme reflects the need for collaboration among educators to explore innovative solutions that can address current challenges in student engagement and success. Additionally, there is an undercurrent of self-reflection regarding the balance of responsibility between educators and students and the importance of recognizing diverse student needs, especially those in the middle spectrum of achievement.

#### ### Key Learning Moments
A critical learning moment emerges from Jeff''s reflection on the role of adults in education. He articulates a concern that educators may be shouldering too much responsibility for student success, thereby undermining student agency and accountability. This insight encourages participants to reevaluate their approaches to student engagement and support, fostering a discussion on how to empower students rather than solely focusing on their academic performance. Furthermore, the mention of cooking not only illustrates Jeff’s creative side but also serves as a metaphor for education: blending structure with creativity can lead to more personalized and effective learning experiences.


#### ### Actionable Takeaways for Participants
Participants in the session should consider the following actionable takeaways: Firstly, there is an opportunity to collaboratively develop strategies that empower students by engaging them in their learning processes. Workshops focusing on the use of AI tools in the classroom can be initiated, promoting peer support and knowledge sharing. Secondly, educators might explore methods for addressing the “hidden and forgotten middle” by designing targeted interventions or programs that cater specifically to students who are neither high achievers nor struggling significantly. Engaging in cross-disciplinary brainstorming sessions can further enhance the pool of ideas.


#### ### Overall Engagement and Collaborative Spirit
The session demonstrates a genuine desire for collaboration among educators, aiming to exchange ideas and solutions. Jeff’s focus on community building and learning from peers stands out as a critical element that can position the group as a catalyst for innovation in educational practices. This spirit of collaboration should be fostered in future sessions, perhaps through follow-up meetings or collaborative projects, to ensure ongoing engagement and sustained progress towards integrating technology effectively within their educational frameworks.', 'idea', '2025-03-06 00:50:15.380729+00', '2025-03-06 00:50:15.380729+00', NULL, NULL),
	('b9960046-bd5a-4ac8-be73-4b38ae837b5f', '6ba21501-22c2-4705-850f-d07844f4dffd', '90e843e0-bb52-402c-86d2-61582c212823', 'Salutations! It is with profound exhilaration that I enter this august pursuit. Could you, with your indulgence, illumine the path that lies ahead in this odyssey?', 'microtranslation', '2025-03-06 15:39:32.560738+00', '2025-03-06 15:39:32.560738+00', NULL, NULL),
