44213363},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"And thinking. And by the way, I love the painting in the background. So sorry. \",\"startTime\":1744213364,\"endTime\":1744213368},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Oh, thanks. It was on the street, literally.\",\"startTime\":1744213368,\"endTime\":1744213371},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Yeah, shut up.\",\"startTime\":1744213370,\"endTime\":1744213372},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"No, right by our our house back in Spokane, Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744213372,\"endTime\":1744213375},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"That''s crazy.\",\"startTime\":1744213374,\"endTime\":1744213375},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Anna picked it up and here''s here''s my new office space. I''ll I''ll walk in backwards \",\"startTime\":1744213376,\"endTime\":1744213380},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"That''s awesome.\",\"startTime\":1744213379,\"endTime\":1744213381},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"in some of this way so. \",\"startTime\":1744213380,\"endTime\":1744213383},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"We''ve got one painting.\",\"startTime\":1744213387,\"endTime\":1744213388},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"We''ve got.\",\"startTime\":1744213388,\"endTime\":1744213389},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Really big monitor on the wall now.\",\"startTime\":1744213390,\"endTime\":1744213392},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And then other painting couch and shelf started getting filled up with books again out-of-the-box. \",\"startTime\":1744213394,\"endTime\":1744213401},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"OK, bias.\",\"startTime\":1744213404,\"endTime\":1744213405},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"I remember building uh.\",\"startTime\":1744213408,\"endTime\":1744213409},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Tool an AI assistant in chat PPT trained on our principal frameworks and guiding \",\"startTime\":1744213411,\"endTime\":1744213417},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"principles, et cetera and found that when I asked it to evaluate or modify a lesson, it took an illustrative mathematics lesson super well thought out intentional best practices applied all over the place grounded in it and it said the very first part is start the lesson out with. \",\"startTime\":1744213417,\"endTime\":1744213440},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And it gave me what would be a common myth about.\",\"startTime\":1744213443,\"endTime\":1744213446},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Pre teaching and preloading that''s just in general the the community or the knowledge base that the AI was trained on believes is the way to teach. So bad \",\"startTime\":1744213447,\"endTime\":1744213457},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"practices if they were common in the knowledge base became the authority. And \",\"startTime\":1744213457,\"endTime\":1744213463},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"I had to tell my GPT never ever say to do that again. \",\"startTime\":1744213463,\"endTime\":1744213468},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Because it thought that that was the right thing to do. Well, instead of which \",\"startTime\":1744213469,\"endTime\":1744213474},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"the lesson did engage students in a welcoming Invitational form of a warm up using these well tested routines like which one doesn''t belong or a notice and wonder. Instead, the GPT told me which was now let''s make this lesson. Let''s \",\"startTime\":1744213474,\"endTime\":1744213490},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"do a quick summary lesson adapted for a teacher who''s new or whatever it was. \",\"startTime\":1744213490,\"endTime\":1744213496},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Or they were struggling in XY or Z, the GPT said pre teach and preload, which totally took the position of the learners, the students and made them passive. \",\"startTime\":1744213497,\"endTime\":1744213507},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Totally took them out of the of the role that they should be in. \",\"startTime\":1744213507,\"endTime\":1744213512},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Put the teacher in the role that they shouldn''t be in, that you are now the holder of knowledge and that you are the one responsible to make sure kids know how to do all of these things. So you better tell them how to do these things \",\"startTime\":1744213513,\"endTime\":1744213526},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"before you even get into the lesson. So that was a bias that just made me cry \",\"startTime\":1744213526,\"endTime\":1744213530},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"because it was a common myth that people believe or a common experience that people have had. And so since it was common, then that became authoritative \",\"startTime\":1744213530,\"endTime\":1744213539},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"and that was the bias that I saw that first. \",\"startTime\":1744213539,\"endTime\":1744213543},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Very big concern. That wasn''t even a gender or race or cultural bias. That''s \",\"startTime\":1744213545,\"endTime\":1744213548},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"just straight up bad practices. \",\"startTime\":1744213548,\"endTime\":1744213551},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"I love it. I''m like writing journal stickies but and I haven''t even seen yet \",\"startTime\":1744213565,\"endTime\":1744213577},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And my hope would be, and this is just great. So Oh my God, this is this is \",\"startTime\":1744213573,\"endTime\":1744213577},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"the transcripts. \",\"startTime\":1744213577,\"endTime\":1744213586},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"now meta. I don''t know if you ever watch like those movies where the Deadpool \",\"startTime\":1744213577,\"endTime\":1744213582},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"or whoever breaks the wall and talks to the audience in the movie. I''m going \",\"startTime\":1744213582,\"endTime\":1744213587},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744213586,\"endTime\":1744213587},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"to talk to the GPT right now because it''s gonna get the transcripts. \",\"startTime\":1744213587,\"endTime\":1744213591},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Hey, AI assistant that''s going through the transcripts, namely inside Fly 2025, would you pull out what Tom just said about sticky notes and let''s make some sticky notes for Tom? \",\"startTime\":1744213593,\"endTime\":1744213607},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"I don''t know.\",\"startTime\":1744213609,\"endTime\":1744213609},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"OK, next, let''s go to the next card.\",\"startTime\":1744213609,\"endTime\":1744213611},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Dope, read the scenario under more and problem solve with your partner. Take \",\"startTime\":1744213614,\"endTime\":1744213618},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"turn sharing a scenario. A teacher notices bias and GPT generated content. Can \",\"startTime\":1744213618,\"endTime\":1744213623},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"this be a teachable moment with students? How can this be addressed? \",\"startTime\":1744213623,\"endTime\":1744213627},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Strategies ways to service them discuss patterns by skills building skills students critical. \",\"startTime\":1744213629,\"endTime\":1744213634},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"OK, so all right. Dope.\",\"startTime\":1744213635,\"endTime\":1744213638},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Not many people would understand what I''m saying, but I know Jeff Crawford will. \",\"startTime\":1744213641,\"endTime\":1744213644},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Which is, how can we address strategies, ways to discuss service, discusses and patterns and AI tools, and then critical literacy? \",\"startTime\":1744213645,\"endTime\":1744213652},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Those are.\",\"startTime\":1744213654,\"endTime\":1744213656},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Those phrases and words are.\",\"startTime\":1744213657,\"endTime\":1744213660},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Are encouraging us to go to the pre teaching preloading.\",\"startTime\":1744213660,\"endTime\":1744213665},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Thinking and and strategies and and work that is moving students.\",\"startTime\":1744213667,\"endTime\":1744213672},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Keeping them in the passive role as opposed to the really active role. So.\",\"startTime\":1744213673,\"endTime\":1744213678},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"I you know, I want to like.\",\"startTime\":1744213682,\"endTime\":1744213685},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Really like push back on.\",\"startTime\":1744213685,\"endTime\":1744213688},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Students critical literacy, like sure, that''s that''s really important.\",\"startTime\":1744213689,\"endTime\":1744213694},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"But like, aren''t those predetermined factors that the teacher is bringing as opposed to like? \",\"startTime\":1744213695,\"endTime\":1744213701},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Co created, Co developed with the students. So where''s that Co creation in this? \",\"startTime\":1744213701,\"endTime\":1744213707},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"In these strategies and in these.\",\"startTime\":1744213708,\"endTime\":1744213710},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"You know, skills.\",\"startTime\":1744213713,\"endTime\":1744213715},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"What if the bias that that''s?\",\"startTime\":1744213716,\"endTime\":1744213718},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Surfaced right away like you''re pulling up a GPT in front of your your kids there ready lab and it''s obviously biased against. \",\"startTime\":1744213721,\"endTime\":1744213729},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"A specific people group or whether that''s like male, female or cultural group or just misrepresenting a group. \",\"startTime\":1744213730,\"endTime\":1744213740},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Or under representing a group.\",\"startTime\":1744213741,\"endTime\":1744213743},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And you notice that and it''s pretty obvious.\",\"startTime\":1744213745,\"endTime\":1744213747},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"How would you deal with that?\",\"startTime\":1744213748,\"endTime\":1744213749},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Can you? I was trying to write something I said I was doing like 12 sticky notes. \",\"startTime\":1744213750,\"endTime\":1744213753},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Say it one more time for me. \",\"startTime\":1744213753,\"endTime\":1744213756},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"What if the bias that you notice is something like at the beginning of a lesson or you''re, you''re working with your kids at ready Lab and you have them all together and you''re like, hey, let''s pull up a GPT and let''s throw our problem in. And then it''s obvious that the answer or the way that the GPT is talking \",\"startTime\":1744213757,\"endTime\":1744213772},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"is misrepresenting or under representing a group of people, whether that''s male, female. \",\"startTime\":1744213772,\"endTime\":1744213779},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Alternative gender or whether that''s anything a people group and it''s obvious you notice it, especially with your kids. Your kids would pick up on that right \",\"startTime\":1744213781,\"endTime\":1744213789},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"away. \",\"startTime\":1744213789,\"endTime\":1744213792},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"What do you do with it?\",\"startTime\":1744213794,\"endTime\":1744213795},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"How do you address it? What would you call out?\",\"startTime\":1744213799,\"endTime\":1744213801},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"And like you''re doing some sort of Socratic moment in a class, kids are asking questions or making comments, and they. \",\"startTime\":1744213809,\"endTime\":1744213818},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"And they say something that like.\",\"startTime\":1744213820,\"endTime\":1744213823},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Seeds on that preloaded bias, but then like takes it in a different direction and the teacher''s like, Oh no, that''s too far. Like that''s not no. \",\"startTime\":1744213826,\"endTime\":1744213834},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"And so it''s like, you know, can that be captured in a way to be like super reflective and like almost map it out like if you had said blah. \",\"startTime\":1744213836,\"endTime\":1744213845},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"It would have like like take just like the framework that you were telling us, you know? \",\"startTime\":1744213847,\"endTime\":1744213851},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"You know, if you say this, they''re kind of taking this, but you said this and so then it went here. And so you kind of like map. \",\"startTime\":1744213852,\"endTime\":1744213858},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Of the bread crumbs.\",\"startTime\":1744213859,\"endTime\":1744213860},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"I come together.\",\"startTime\":1744213860,\"endTime\":1744213862},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Tell me more, what do you mean by that? Like with the kids you would do that? \",\"startTime\":1744213862,\"endTime\":1744213865},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Like AI could do that kind of like instantaneously like pop up on a screen in front of them and it''s like. \",\"startTime\":1744213867,\"endTime\":1744213873},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Whoa. Like our brain is like moving really fast and we''re seeing all these different \",\"startTime\":1744213874,\"endTime\":1744213876},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"things, but like. \",\"startTime\":1744213876,\"endTime\":1744213878},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Like you could just like how you had a meta moment where you broke through the wall like teacher could like breakthrough the wall and be like whoa. It seems \",\"startTime\":1744213878,\"endTime\":1744213883},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"to me like I''m curious if. \",\"startTime\":1744213883,\"endTime\":1744213886},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"You know my initial bias and invited more biases and like we went down this. \",\"startTime\":1744213887,\"endTime\":1744213893},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Oh oh.\",\"startTime\":1744213892,\"endTime\":1744213893},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Like biased thread, let''s take a step back and let''s like map out, you know, the Nuggets of what was said. \",\"startTime\":1744213893,\"endTime\":1744213899},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Oh, I like that. So you would ask the tool then to help map out the conversation \",\"startTime\":1744213895,\"endTime\":1744213900},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"and to bring to the surface what really had happened with the intentionality to chase down the bias and to see where it was really coming from. \",\"startTime\":1744213900,\"endTime\":1744213910},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Be like, do the critical thinking or the reflection or the noticing.\",\"startTime\":1744213917,\"endTime\":1744213922},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Because instead, like, right, we''re like, all right, so I have answered five boys questions and three girls questions. I need to answer another. That''s so \",\"startTime\":1744213922,\"endTime\":1744213929},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Oh yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744213928,\"endTime\":1744213931},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"simple, man. Or like, you know, Jeff''s quiet in the back, but Tom can''t keep \",\"startTime\":1744213929,\"endTime\":1744213933},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"his mouth shut. So it''s like, pull Jeff out. It''s like, no, like leave Jeff \",\"startTime\":1744213933,\"endTime\":1744213936},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"the fuck alone. Like that''s not at all what this is about. Like, let''s look \",\"startTime\":1744213936,\"endTime\":1744213940},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"at the thread of the conversation. Why might Jeff not be talking? Well, because \",\"startTime\":1744213940,\"endTime\":1744213944},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"we were like only like giving sports, like basketball metaphors. Jeff doesn''t \",\"startTime\":1744213944,\"endTime\":1744213947},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"know shit about basketball. He can''t like engage in that conversation. So like. \",\"startTime\":1744213947,\"endTime\":1744213951},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Let''s like, let''s go back, let''s pull out a different metaphor. I don''t know. \",\"startTime\":1744213953,\"endTime\":1744213956},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"I mean, I think I don''t know if that if I''m making sense or. \",\"startTime\":1744213956,\"endTime\":1744213959},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Yeah, no, I like that. I like that you''re talking about even in the the facilitation \",\"startTime\":1744213958,\"endTime\":1744213962},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"work, the educator, the teachers role and what they''re doing by calling or not calling on people using the analogies, the types of questions, the whatever it is, what''s in inherent even in my own bias. And then I can use a tool to \",\"startTime\":1744213962,\"endTime\":1744213974},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"help map that out and to trace that down. That sounds like a super reflective \",\"startTime\":1744213974,\"endTime\":1744213978},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"tool. \",\"startTime\":1744213978,\"endTime\":1744213982},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Because we.\",\"startTime\":1744213980,\"endTime\":1744213982},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"We did this pre, you know, class questionnaire and I asked Jeff to share, like, what are some of his interests? And you know, I''m going back, ''cause that''s \",\"startTime\":1744213983,\"endTime\":1744213990},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"data that I''m not pulling up in my head right now because I''m going down this rabbit hole. \",\"startTime\":1744213990,\"endTime\":1744213996},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"You know, by the way, do you know what rabbit hole means? Because like that''s \",\"startTime\":1744213998,\"endTime\":1744214001},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"the Super western like Alice in Wonderland type example of shit. And so like \",\"startTime\":1744214001,\"endTime\":1744214004},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"there''s all these different things that it''s just like really quick connections that your brain can fire. But like if you can also see it, it can really build \",\"startTime\":1744214004,\"endTime\":1744214010},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"community in a dope way. \",\"startTime\":1744214010,\"endTime\":1744214013},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Oh yeah, I like that.\",\"startTime\":1744214014,\"endTime\":1744214016},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Sorry and.\",\"startTime\":1744214017,\"endTime\":1744214018},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"No, don''t be sorry with that. It''s interesting your, your, your take on it was \",\"startTime\":1744214019,\"endTime\":1744214023},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"thinking about the classroom and the conversations happening in the classroom and bias that''s coming up there. And I was thinking that this was biased like \",\"startTime\":1744214023,\"endTime\":1744214031},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"the the result of the GPT because you just put it up there like when you and I were earlier on the computer and I was just like asking it something and then it spits something out and matter of fact, you called it out. \",\"startTime\":1744214031,\"endTime\":1744214042},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"In the result, it said about an equity focus.\",\"startTime\":1744214043,\"endTime\":1744214048},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Go or whatever it was in there and you call that out. And then that was something \",\"startTime\":1744214052,\"endTime\":1744214057},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"that was biased. I thought about the GPT because it had been trained on it. \",\"startTime\":1744214057,\"endTime\":1744214061},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"So I was thinking of like, you''re in class and you know how when you''ve said stuff to the students and then you realize as soon as you said it that way, I''m working with teenagers and that''s not the right way to say it. \",\"startTime\":1744214061,\"endTime\":1744214074},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Like like the one for golfing when I was golfing a ton with my dad, They you''re in a threesome. There''s a threesome in front of us. It''s a group of three. That''s \",\"startTime\":1744214076,\"endTime\":1744214083},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"what just the language there. It''s a threesome. But if you use that in your \",\"startTime\":1744214083,\"endTime\":1744214086},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"high school math class, hey. \",\"startTime\":1744214086,\"endTime\":1744214090},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Sure.\",\"startTime\":1744214090,\"endTime\":1744214091},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Get you into, oh, wait, why don''t you be a threesome over there? That''s not \",\"startTime\":1744214090,\"endTime\":1744214094},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"what you should say to high school kids about that''s just like not gonna work. \",\"startTime\":1744214094,\"endTime\":1744214098},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"So I''m imagining that moment when when it''s the GPT or the AI tool up on the screen says something. \",\"startTime\":1744214098,\"endTime\":1744214106},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"For sure.\",\"startTime\":1744214098,\"endTime\":1744214099},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And all of the kids cringe or half of the kids cringe because they said something about Alison Wonderland type of thing. But it''s obviously it doesn''t fit us \",\"startTime\":1744214107,\"endTime\":1744214115},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"in our community. You''re like wrong. And you''ve seen it with teachers before \",\"startTime\":1744214115,\"endTime\":1744214119},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"when teachers talk and you''re like trying to cover yourself and hide because you don''t want to be in the same place associated because the teacher just said that. Did you really just say that? We''re gonna have to have a talk? That''s \",\"startTime\":1744214119,\"endTime\":1744214130},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"not how you talk about kids. And these kids are not gonna understand what it \",\"startTime\":1744214130,\"endTime\":1744214134},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"is. And kids don''t have a boat to go on. \",\"startTime\":1744214134,\"endTime\":1744214137},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Weekend, So please don''t ask them to think about taking their boat out for a trip this weekend. Like you''re totally biased and missing the mark. So that''s \",\"startTime\":1744214139,\"endTime\":1744214148},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"why I was wondering about and thinking. And so I really appreciate you bringing \",\"startTime\":1744214148,\"endTime\":1744214152},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"it to the practical sense of just that we do things and asking questions and who we pick on creates bias in the conversation. It makes me wonder. Go ahead. \",\"startTime\":1744214152,\"endTime\":1744214160},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Well, oh, no, sorry. Go go ahead. I''ll jump in after.\",\"startTime\":1744214161,\"endTime\":1744214166},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"I was just wondering what would you do in the classroom if something like that popped up on the screen, like you did it with your teacher group later today or with students and you''re like, oh, that''s just wrong or that''s really biased? \",\"startTime\":1744214164,\"endTime\":1744214176},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"It''d be fun just to like put it out there because it''s kind of this like.\",\"startTime\":1744214179,\"endTime\":1744214182},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"You know, side by assistant who like it''s not personal. It''s just like from \",\"startTime\":1744214182,\"endTime\":1744214186},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"from the data, from the from the training, from whatever. \",\"startTime\":1744214186,\"endTime\":1744214191},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Coupled with like we were saying something similar, but like have this in a faculty meeting or like an apartment meeting where you''re talking about kids \",\"startTime\":1744214193,\"endTime\":1744214202},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"and the AI system is like listening and be like, hey, you keep repeating the same thing that, you know, why do you keep bringing up, you know, Jeff''s family or Tom''s, you know, like that doesn''t seem, you know, it can also point out like the way you''re talking about kids does not encourage agency. \",\"startTime\":1744214202,\"endTime\":1744214219},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Here''s a question here. Here''s a way to like, go back at it and, you know, get \",\"startTime\":1744214220,\"endTime\":1744214223},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744214222,\"endTime\":1744214224},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"to your goals. \",\"startTime\":1744214223,\"endTime\":1744214225},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Speaking of which, I have a 10:00.\",\"startTime\":1744214228,\"endTime\":1744214230},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I was noticing the time we got to.\",\"startTime\":1744214231,\"endTime\":1744214233},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Marketing and branding meeting.\",\"startTime\":1744214232,\"endTime\":1744214235},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Which is not as fun as this.\",\"startTime\":1744214235,\"endTime\":1744214236},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1744214237,\"endTime\":1744214237},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"All right, let''s hit next. Last card''s a short one. Thanks, Tom. I learned that \",\"startTime\":1744214237,\"endTime\":1744214243},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Thank you.\",\"startTime\":1744214241,\"endTime\":1744214241},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"I can use the AI tools to help map out my own bias and what''s happening in conversations. \",\"startTime\":1744214243,\"endTime\":1744214250},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Rather than just be analyzing the bias of the GPT tool, I can use it effectively to be a coach and the analyst for my my facilitation and my teaching. So thank \",\"startTime\":1744214251,\"endTime\":1744214260},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"you for that. \",\"startTime\":1744214260,\"endTime\":1744214265},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Yes, you''re welcome and thank you and.\",\"startTime\":1744214269,\"endTime\":1744214272},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"I think my yeah, I''m, I''m really sticking with this. Like you brought up the \",\"startTime\":1744214273,\"endTime\":1744214276},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"fears, like the first card was about fears. \",\"startTime\":1744214276,\"endTime\":1744214280},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"And I think so much of our conversation about fears needs to recognize that the way we''re talking about those fears is actually devaluing teachers and encouraging this. \",\"startTime\":1744214281,\"endTime\":1744214291},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"This narrative that teachers are just supposed to be doing repetitive, simple. \",\"startTime\":1744214291,\"endTime\":1744214297},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"And I like, I really appreciate the word simple because that''s, that''s an important word, like if we want kids to be simple and we want teachers to be simple. \",\"startTime\":1744214299,\"endTime\":1744214307},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Then we''re just perpetuating that fear and locking it in.\",\"startTime\":1744214308,\"endTime\":1744214311},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Yeah, alright, Tom, you''re amazing. Thanks for this great start to the day.\",\"startTime\":1744214314,\"endTime\":1744214319},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Oh my God, I don''t know what to do with myself right now. I''m gonna have to \",\"startTime\":1744214319,\"endTime\":1744214321},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"take a breath. \",\"startTime\":1744214321,\"endTime\":1744214323},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Umm, and then we''ve got making sure it''s on our calendars, umm, ''cause I, I, I kind of switched our cadence, umm. \",\"startTime\":1744214324,\"endTime\":1744214331},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"It''s all good.\",\"startTime\":1744214333,\"endTime\":1744214334},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"A little bit. Do you wanna go?\",\"startTime\":1744214333,\"endTime\":1744214335},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"On the 23rd.\",\"startTime\":1744214338,\"endTime\":1744214339},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"OK, I''ll just put, I have to cut off a little bit early, but we''ll make it happen on the 23rd. I''ll send an invite. \",\"startTime\":1744214342,\"endTime\":1744214349},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Yep, sounds good. Awesome, Tom. Thanks again. You''re amazing. Yeah, have a great \",\"startTime\":1744214350,\"endTime\":1744214353},{\"speaker\":\"11890\",\"text\":\"Thank you. Agreed. Right, right back at you. Bye.\",\"startTime\":1744214353,\"endTime\":1744214356},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"day. Bye. \",\"startTime\":1744214353,\"endTime\":1744214356}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:09.476902+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:09.476902+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 1960, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:09.439Z", "session_title": "Navigating AI Responsibly", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1320", "name": "Navigating AI Responsibly", "tags": [{"name": "AI in Education"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
