w AI was going to help us as teachers. \",\"startTime\":1740421566,\"endTime\":1740421573},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"And what it basically came down to was the the less time we have to spend on planning and administrative tasks. \",\"startTime\":1740421573,\"endTime\":1740421583},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"And differentiating and all that jazz, the more time we''re able to actually spend with students, helping them and letting them grow. So overall, it''s about. \",\"startTime\":1740421583,\"endTime\":1740421593},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Benefiting our students through giving ourselves more time.\",\"startTime\":1740421595,\"endTime\":1740421601},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yes, exactly.\",\"startTime\":1740421603,\"endTime\":1740421604},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It''s really about the students. And if it''s not about them, why are we doing \",\"startTime\":1740421607,\"endTime\":1740421611},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Exactly.\",\"startTime\":1740421611,\"endTime\":1740421612},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it if we can save time so that we can be better for our students? Yeah. Like, \",\"startTime\":1740421611,\"endTime\":1740421615},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I love the the heartbeat that I hear and the passion I hear from educators who are learning AI tools. And they say like what you''re saying. And they they keep \",\"startTime\":1740421615,\"endTime\":1740421622},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"saying it in different words with that, hey, you know what? I need to be like \",\"startTime\":1740421622,\"endTime\":1740421626},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"fresh. And I want to be healthy and I want to go home and spend time with my \",\"startTime\":1740421626,\"endTime\":1740421629},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"family so that tomorrow I can bring my table for my students. And besides that, \",\"startTime\":1740421629,\"endTime\":1740421633},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I want it done so that. \",\"startTime\":1740421633,\"endTime\":1740421637},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740421637,\"endTime\":1740421638},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"All done for them in the right way. And I don''t want me pulling my hair out \",\"startTime\":1740421639,\"endTime\":1740421642},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and I don''t want to be stressed when I go to class or, you know, on the edge. \",\"startTime\":1740421642,\"endTime\":1740421645},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I wanna be sharp for my games. That I can do it, yeah. \",\"startTime\":1740421645,\"endTime\":1740421648},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah, when our district is currently currently has no AI policy. So our school \",\"startTime\":1740421648,\"endTime\":1740421653},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"board''s working on that doing all that jazz. But in the meantime we''re we''ve \",\"startTime\":1740421653,\"endTime\":1740421657},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"been using it to, we''ve been using like ChatGPT. \",\"startTime\":1740421657,\"endTime\":1740421661},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"To unpack standards and create like.\",\"startTime\":1740421662,\"endTime\":1740421666},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Proficiency rubrics. Proficiency scales.\",\"startTime\":1740421668,\"endTime\":1740421670},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"All in.\",\"startTime\":1740421670,\"endTime\":1740421671},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Support of our future place work that we''re just starting to reinvigorate and just trying to help ourselves to ease the burden of the workload. \",\"startTime\":1740421672,\"endTime\":1740421683},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yes, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740421686,\"endTime\":1740421688},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m looking at the interface for script writing and they have a GPT scriptwriter button up there under the script. Oh I was in ChatGPT to do it, that was cool. \",\"startTime\":1740421690,\"endTime\":1740421703},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740421698,\"endTime\":1740421698},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Do you know when you uploaded the script? It''s saying it''s only wants an excel \",\"startTime\":1740421711,\"endTime\":1740421716},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"file for the script. I try to just a text file and it didn''t like it. \",\"startTime\":1740421716,\"endTime\":1740421720},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"I think I ended up just doing.\",\"startTime\":1740421717,\"endTime\":1740421719},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"I think I ended up doing like just copy paste.\",\"startTime\":1740421721,\"endTime\":1740421724},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, into the Oh, that makes sense too.\",\"startTime\":1740421726,\"endTime\":1740421728},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah, ''cause it also there''s a character limit in each script box.\",\"startTime\":1740421728,\"endTime\":1740421734},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"I believe and so I had to like split it up to be.\",\"startTime\":1740421736,\"endTime\":1740421741},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Got it.\",\"startTime\":1740421739,\"endTime\":1740421740},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Smaller chunks.\",\"startTime\":1740421743,\"endTime\":1740421745},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, I''m I''m I''m downloading the sample script that they have to see what it looks like. \",\"startTime\":1740421748,\"endTime\":1740421753},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And then I''m wondering if I could use my script. I have to put it in a format \",\"startTime\":1740421756,\"endTime\":1740421759},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"like this to upload so I don''t have to go copy paste. \",\"startTime\":1740421759,\"endTime\":1740421763},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740421767,\"endTime\":1740421768},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, it just broke it by lines, OK.\",\"startTime\":1740421770,\"endTime\":1740421772},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Playing with the translator at the moment to see.\",\"startTime\":1740421782,\"endTime\":1740421786},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"What all languages they have and what everything? How effective is the translator? \",\"startTime\":1740421789,\"endTime\":1740421795},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Not that I''m particularly fluent at reading many other languages, but.\",\"startTime\":1740421797,\"endTime\":1740421801},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"I do appreciate that they have.\",\"startTime\":1740421811,\"endTime\":1740421813},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Different dialects for different locales.\",\"startTime\":1740421814,\"endTime\":1740421818},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, that''s amazing.\",\"startTime\":1740421818,\"endTime\":1740421824},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Like for Spanish, we have a large, yeah, we have a large Guatemalan population that speaks the Mom language, which is indigenous to Guatemala. And they have, \",\"startTime\":1740421818,\"endTime\":1740421828},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"it''s not named Mum. And I don''t know how it doesn''t sound like Mum, but they \",\"startTime\":1740421828,\"endTime\":1740421833},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740421832,\"endTime\":1740421832},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"have. \",\"startTime\":1740421833,\"endTime\":1740421838},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"The Spanish for the Guatemala region.\",\"startTime\":1740421839,\"endTime\":1740421842},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That''s so cool.\",\"startTime\":1740421843,\"endTime\":1740421844},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I like it. When you go to Costa Rica, for example, we got to go there finally. \",\"startTime\":1740421846,\"endTime\":1740421851},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm.\",\"startTime\":1740421848,\"endTime\":1740421849},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It was wonderful. Or you hear from somebody from a different region and they''re \",\"startTime\":1740421851,\"endTime\":1740421856},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"like, we speak Costa Rican. It''s not Spanish, but it is some Spanish. And like \",\"startTime\":1740421856,\"endTime\":1740421861},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"they have pride in your language. And for somebody who''s not from there, you''re \",\"startTime\":1740421861,\"endTime\":1740421866},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah, Mm-hmm.\",\"startTime\":1740421862,\"endTime\":1740421864},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"like, oh, it''s Spanish. And locals will say, no, it''s not, it''s Costa Rican. \",\"startTime\":1740421866,\"endTime\":1740421871},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It''s just really simple. I guess it would be say like when you''re British or. \",\"startTime\":1740421871,\"endTime\":1740421876},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740421872,\"endTime\":1740421873},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Or US English like they''re different and the words have different meanings.\",\"startTime\":1740421878,\"endTime\":1740421882},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740421883,\"endTime\":1740421884},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Well, there are so many different there''s like how many different forms of English on here 1234? \",\"startTime\":1740421886,\"endTime\":1740421892},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"567891011121314 There''s 14 different English regional dialects.\",\"startTime\":1740421892,\"endTime\":1740421901},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh.\",\"startTime\":1740421895,\"endTime\":1740421896},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"In Hey Jen.\",\"startTime\":1740421905,\"endTime\":1740421908},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Wow.\",\"startTime\":1740421915,\"endTime\":1740421916},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"My bot''s thinking I asked it to put in ''cause on the output it has scene 1, scene 2, scene 3. \",\"startTime\":1740421924,\"endTime\":1740421931},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Umm, all the way to and then closing. But I know that in Hey Jen, it needs to \",\"startTime\":1740421934,\"endTime\":1740421937},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"be a spreadsheet with each row. \",\"startTime\":1740421937,\"endTime\":1740421941},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"The scene or whatever you call it, the dialogue for that scene or frame. So \",\"startTime\":1740421942,\"endTime\":1740421946},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740421943,\"endTime\":1740421947},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m just asking it in ChatGPT to output it like that, see if it can do it, yeah. \",\"startTime\":1740421946,\"endTime\":1740421951},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Nice.\",\"startTime\":1740421952,\"endTime\":1740421953},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"No copy pasting, I''ll spend 20 hours trying to do the correct prompt until I get your superpower. \",\"startTime\":1740421953,\"endTime\":1740421958},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And then I''ll be like, oh, I''m trying to figure it out, but it''s for me. I''m \",\"startTime\":1740421959,\"endTime\":1740421963},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740421960,\"endTime\":1740421960},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"trying to learn the tools, download the script in XLS format, starting downloads, download complete. I''m trying. I''m going to crash hard maybe. \",\"startTime\":1740421963,\"endTime\":1740421971},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm. Oh, love that.\",\"startTime\":1740421968,\"endTime\":1740421970},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Uploading script.\",\"startTime\":1740421975,\"endTime\":1740421976},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"They put it in.\",\"startTime\":1740421983,\"endTime\":1740421984},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Did it work?\",\"startTime\":1740421983,\"endTime\":1740421984},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, it''s kind of funky, though.\",\"startTime\":1740421986,\"endTime\":1740421987},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Nice.\",\"startTime\":1740421986,\"endTime\":1740421986},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"We''ll see what happens.\",\"startTime\":1740421988,\"endTime\":1740421989},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I just want to hit play now and see what it looks like. Script generation, Dang \",\"startTime\":1740421991,\"endTime\":1740421993},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it. \",\"startTime\":1740421993,\"endTime\":1740421995},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"But maybe it''s still working?\",\"startTime\":1740421999,\"endTime\":1740422000},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Can I see it doing things on the side?\",\"startTime\":1740422002,\"endTime\":1740422004},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Voice not found. Voicemail.\",\"startTime\":1740422016,\"endTime\":1740422018},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Did you pick a voice?\",\"startTime\":1740422019,\"endTime\":1740422021},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Hello I am a generated voice you can use. Oh this is fun.\",\"startTime\":1740422022,\"endTime\":1740422025},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Nice.\",\"startTime\":1740422029,\"endTime\":1740422029},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It''s so funny in your brain. You''re like, of course, because you know what a \",\"startTime\":1740422033,\"endTime\":1740422036},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"video looks like on the other end and you think it should be automatic because it''s a powerful tool. But then when you start doing it, you realize, oh, there''s \",\"startTime\":1740422036,\"endTime\":1740422042},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740422040,\"endTime\":1740422040},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"all of this work that has to get done. \",\"startTime\":1740422042,\"endTime\":1740422045},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740422048,\"endTime\":1740422049},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Do you hear this?\",\"startTime\":1740422049,\"endTime\":1740422049},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Professionals connect for real, meaningful conversations. If you''re an educator, \",\"startTime\":1740422056,\"endTime\":1740422060},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"you know that having someone who gets it can make all the difference. But what \",\"startTime\":1740422060,\"endTime\":1740422064},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"if you could instantly connect with a network of verified, insightful educators? \",\"startTime\":1740422064,\"endTime\":1740422068},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Whenever you need a spark of inspiration or practical advice with Side By, you can. Let''s show you how. \",\"startTime\":1740422068,\"endTime\":1740422074},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, it''s the same screen with some girl pose with her marker with a cool background. \",\"startTime\":1740422074,\"endTime\":1740422078},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"That''s awesome.\",\"startTime\":1740422075,\"endTime\":1740422075},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, at least I''m on the right track. This is cool. Alright, how''s yours coming \",\"startTime\":1740422078,\"endTime\":1740422082},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740422081,\"endTime\":1740422081},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"along? \",\"startTime\":1740422082,\"endTime\":1740422086},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"It''s going pretty well, I''m just working on editing my slides and making them or editing the like sections of the video to make them more relevant to what I''m talking about. \",\"startTime\":1740422087,\"endTime\":1740422098},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Which is not hard I have to say.\",\"startTime\":1740422100,\"endTime\":1740422103},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"And then there''s a portion where you can like upload a screen record, I think. \",\"startTime\":1740422104,\"endTime\":1740422108},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"And so I kind of want to try and do that. \",\"startTime\":1740422108,\"endTime\":1740422112},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Rather than have to go take screenshots of a bunch of stuff I did just say like hey. \",\"startTime\":1740422114,\"endTime\":1740422118},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Here''s a video of what I did other thing and have the AI avatar talking over it. \",\"startTime\":1740422119,\"endTime\":1740422125},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, that''s a great idea.\",\"startTime\":1740422126,\"endTime\":1740422127},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, I want to brain with you and help turbocharge your work. Where are you at \",\"startTime\":1740422131,\"endTime\":1740422135},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and and are you stuck on anything? \",\"startTime\":1740422135,\"endTime\":1740422138},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Umm, I don''t think I''m stuck yet. I think it''s mainly gonna be just eventually \",\"startTime\":1740422143,\"endTime\":1740422147},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"going and making that screen recording and seeing. \",\"startTime\":1740422147,\"endTime\":1740422151},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"If that actually works.\",\"startTime\":1740422152,\"endTime\":1740422153},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Which I think it will.\",\"startTime\":1740422156,\"endTime\":1740422157},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Oh, and you can screen record within Hey Gen.\",\"startTime\":1740422164,\"endTime\":1740422167},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah, either specific tabs, windows, entire screen.\",\"startTime\":1740422170,\"endTime\":1740422175},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"That is very cool.\",\"startTime\":1740422177,\"endTime\":1740422179},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"With Nice Oh now I''m playing with all the different templates and backgrounds. \",\"startTime\":1740422184,\"endTime\":1740422189},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think I just need to click all the different tool options that we have. \",\"startTime\":1740422189,\"endTime\":1740422194},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"I think that''s that tends to be the hardest thing for a lot of my colleagues just. \",\"startTime\":1740422205,\"endTime\":1740422209},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Getting out there, clicking buttons and seeing what happens.\",\"startTime\":1740422209,\"endTime\":1740422212},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Because they don''t always, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740422215,\"endTime\":1740422217},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I can see that.\",\"startTime\":1740422215,\"endTime\":1740422216},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"I''m out here like, OK, I know. Generally I know enough Internet safety to get \",\"startTime\":1740422218,\"endTime\":1740422222},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"me through quite a few things. \",\"startTime\":1740422222,\"endTime\":1740422226},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"But I also know that I can go in and click a bunch of things and it probably won''t hurt anything. \",\"startTime\":1740422227,\"endTime\":1740422234},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"And I have plenty of staff members who think they''re going to break something or hurt something just because they clicked it. \",\"startTime\":1740422237,\"endTime\":1740422244},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740422247,\"endTime\":1740422247},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"I guess the IT department has done their job and instilled the fear of of computers in them so they don''t click things. \",\"startTime\":1740422250,\"endTime\":1740422258},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That''s yeah. How true is that? Should we have some stories in each of our districts \",\"startTime\":1740422262,\"endTime\":1740422266},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and places of all the don''t click here and don''t do this? And I better not hand \",\"startTime\":1740422266,\"endTime\":1740422269},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"out the laptops because if I hand out the laptops, you''re all going to be not paying attention to me. So I''m just going to show you how to do it. That was \",\"startTime\":1740422269,\"endTime\":1740422277},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"one of my stories. Oh, seriously? Come on. \",\"startTime\":1740422277,\"endTime\":1740422281},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740422280,\"endTime\":1740422280},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, you can change the person, the avatar, the digital avatar on each of the screens, or it can keep going. Oh, that''s sweet. \",\"startTime\":1740422285,\"endTime\":1740422292},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740422293,\"endTime\":1740422293},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm. And some of them have like different looks or poses or things that you \",\"startTime\":1740422295,\"endTime\":1740422298},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"can click through and find. \",\"startTime\":1740422298,\"endTime\":1740422301},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"So I just made a sample screen recording and then you can upload that directly into the slide deck. \",\"startTime\":1740422305,\"endTime\":1740422314},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Hey there, welcome to.\",\"startTime\":1740422319,\"endTime\":1740422321},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Hey there.\",\"startTime\":1740422323,\"endTime\":1740422324},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Thank you for the.\",\"startTime\":1740422327,\"endTime\":1740422328},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Insight opening scene Hey there, did you hear that opening scene?\",\"startTime\":1740422329,\"endTime\":1740422334},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740422334,\"endTime\":1740422335},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Love it.\",\"startTime\":1740422339,\"endTime\":1740422339},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh.\",\"startTime\":1740422348,\"endTime\":1740422349},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So it takes the script and uses the script that you have to generate voice using one of the models that you have. You can change the model, you can change the \",\"startTime\":1740422350,\"endTime\":1740422359},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"language translating it, you can change the avatar, you can change the script. \",\"startTime\":1740422359,\"endTime\":1740422364},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"You can upload scripts, you can upload screen recordings. All of the cool little \",\"startTime\":1740422364,\"endTime\":1740422369},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"elements of the slide in the video can pop up in and out guessing. You can do \",\"startTime\":1740422369,\"endTime\":1740422374},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"different transitions, but that''s just a guess. \",\"startTime\":1740422374,\"endTime\":1740422379},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"I think so. There''s like an animation button and it has like effects for entering \",\"startTime\":1740422382,\"endTime\":1740422388},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"and effects for leaving. \",\"startTime\":1740422388,\"endTime\":1740422394},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"I wonder if they''re going to add more.\",\"startTime\":1740422399,\"endTime\":1740422402},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"More options for that.\",\"startTime\":1740422405,\"endTime\":1740422407},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I know that it''d be way faster for me to open up the spreadsheet and delete the first couple rows with the thing that says seen or opening, but I''m asking the GPT to do that like let''s do it again better and get rid of the 1st 2 rows. \",\"startTime\":1740422439,\"endTime\":1740422454},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"All right, we''re 40 minutes into the call.\",\"startTime\":1740422473,\"endTime\":1740422476},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m gonna play some more, but I think we should wrap it up soon. So you get \",\"startTime\":1740422476,\"endTime\":1740422480},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"space to do your stuff and we don''t go over limit and I''ll let you finish what you''re doing unless you''re ready to to bring it together. And I kind of wonder \",\"startTime\":1740422480,\"endTime\":1740422487},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"All right.\",\"startTime\":1740422485,\"endTime\":1740422486},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"what''s next on the next card. But this has been really fun. \",\"startTime\":1740422487,\"endTime\":1740422491},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I''m, I''m ready if you are.\",\"startTime\":1740422492,\"endTime\":1740422494},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, OK. Press next.\",\"startTime\":1740422494,\"endTime\":1740422497},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Think Allison and Cher. One thing that I learned about Hey, Jen and a bunch \",\"startTime\":1740422500,\"endTime\":1740422504},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"of things in using. Hey, Jen. So thank you so much. Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1740422504,\"endTime\":1740422509},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"I love that.\",\"startTime\":1740422507,\"endTime\":1740422508},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah, no problem. I love that I got to learn that there are.\",\"startTime\":1740422509,\"endTime\":1740422513},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"A plethora of people out there who I can connect with and.\",\"startTime\":1740422513,\"endTime\":1740422516},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Grow my skills using AI and as a professional that I''m just, I''m excited.\",\"startTime\":1740422517,\"endTime\":1740422522},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yes, yes, awesome. So Allison, I don''t remember what you had except for your \",\"startTime\":1740422524,\"endTime\":1740422528},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"cadence in your dashboard there, but we''re updating how you can connect. We''re \",\"startTime\":1740422528,\"endTime\":1740422532},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"building it ground up and Mike''s using Lovable as a tool to do coding and it''s fun is because we''re using oh, you do Oh, I want to chat with you so much ''cause \",\"startTime\":1740422532,\"endTime\":1740422540},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"I love lovable.\",\"startTime\":1740422539,\"endTime\":1740422540},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"there''s all of these different things, but we''re building it ground up ''cause we want to make it as best as it could be And as you know, in education, we have so many things embedded and baked in the way we. \",\"startTime\":1740422540,\"endTime\":1740422553},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740422542,\"endTime\":1740422542},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Do it like we want to be ground up, starting fresh. And that''s why we did the \",\"startTime\":1740422555,\"endTime\":1740422559},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"the new organization this this February. So we''re at the end of our first month \",\"startTime\":1740422559,\"endTime\":1740422563},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740422561,\"endTime\":1740422562},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"right now. And as we build it out for the dashboard, if you have ideas that \",\"startTime\":1740422563,\"endTime\":1740422567},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"you know, that would work better or things like that, don''t hesitate to reach out and send that to me. However you want to e-mail it to me or we''ll connect \",\"startTime\":1740422567,\"endTime\":1740422574},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"or whatever tool you end up using. You think, hey, Jeff, this will be a fun \",\"startTime\":1740422574,\"endTime\":1740422578},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"tool to use. You definitely are on that cutting edge with using tools. \",\"startTime\":1740422578,\"endTime\":1740422581},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And I like the phrase using appropriate tools strategically.\",\"startTime\":1740422581,\"endTime\":1740422585},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And I think you''re, you''re, you''re doing that and that''s your stance as an educator. \",\"startTime\":1740422586,\"endTime\":1740422590},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"You''re an amazing individual who embraces technology and trying things out. \",\"startTime\":1740422590,\"endTime\":1740422593},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So as you have ideas and you want to communicate them, please do communicate them. And also we want to keep connecting you. So keep looking back at your \",\"startTime\":1740422593,\"endTime\":1740422601},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1740422596,\"endTime\":1740422597},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Absolutely.\",\"startTime\":1740422599,\"endTime\":1740422600},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"dashboard and on your dashboard there, we''ll be connecting you with other people. \",\"startTime\":1740422601,\"endTime\":1740422605},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Right now I have to play because Mike made some new things in there and I''ll meet with him today and I''ll get updates and even share them with you. But I \",\"startTime\":1740422605,\"endTime\":1740422612},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"believe the way that we''re connecting. \",\"startTime\":1740422612,\"endTime\":1740422616},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"In your dashboard, there''s fine time. You can just chat in there and say, hey, \",\"startTime\":1740422616,\"endTime\":1740422621},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"this is when it works for me. And if somebody else is at that same time, then \",\"startTime\":1740422621,\"endTime\":1740422625},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"our robot robot at Scibi will send you both a calendar invite. So it''ll be automated \",\"startTime\":1740422625,\"endTime\":1740422629},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"MMM. Mm-hmm.\",\"startTime\":1740422629,\"endTime\":1740422631},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"for you just like, hey, do you want to meet with Dale on next Monday morning at this time? And then you would be like, yes or no. So we''re trying to make \",\"startTime\":1740422629,\"endTime\":1740422638},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Love it.\",\"startTime\":1740422636,\"endTime\":1740422637},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it seamless and easy for you and also keep your inbox from being cluttered up with too many things. We know there''s too many things in our. \",\"startTime\":1740422638,\"endTime\":1740422646},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, anything else that we could do or I could do, please reach out and I''ll be working on my end to connect you with other educators and keep going back to side by. And then at some point we''ll get it to be an app and we''ll get rid \",\"startTime\":1740422648,\"endTime\":1740422659},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"of the updo logo ''cause that will be all together ours and it''ll all be bye, bye. And it''ll be one app and you can do it off your phone and you get your \",\"startTime\":1740422659,\"endTime\":1740422666},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"notification. Hey, somebody wants to chat right now about AI tools and you''d \",\"startTime\":1740422666,\"endTime\":1740422670},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"be like yes or however it is. Yeah, Alright. Thank you so much Allison, you \",\"startTime\":1740422670,\"endTime\":1740422674},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Love it.\",\"startTime\":1740422673,\"endTime\":1740422674},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"are wonderful. I hope you have a great Monday. This has been. \",\"startTime\":1740422674,\"endTime\":1740422677},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Amazing start for my day, I appreciate it.\",\"startTime\":1740422678,\"endTime\":1740422680},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Thank you. You too. It''s gonna be a great week.\",\"startTime\":1740422681,\"endTime\":1740422684},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Thanks. It is. It really is. Thanks. Bye. Bye.\",\"startTime\":1740422684,\"endTime\":1740422686},{\"speaker\":\"11876\",\"text\":\"Bye.\",\"startTime\":1740422688,\"endTime\":1740422689}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:09.545462+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:09.545462+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 2625, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:09.488Z", "session_title": "Innovation in AI - Recent Updates", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1447", "name": "Innovation in AI - Recent Updates", "tags": [{"name": "AI in Education"}, {"name": "Freemium"}, {"name": "First10"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('031a95f8-0b21-4f33-b6d0-832c9f1bf9dd', '4c3a7dc1-10fb-45d6-a20e-f89f0e73af73', '114747', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:54.590091+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:54.590091+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 18, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:54.528Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('7fe77103-018c-4e74-b822-a7caef3d34cc', 'e5a67ee9-d30e-4f26-bafd-bf20b9ba4ab6', '138522', '"[{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"I teach the basics of AI to educators so that they can.\",\"startTime\":1746473827,\"endTime\":1746473833},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"Teach students for the real world that students will eventually be in. And I \",\"startTime\":1746473834,\"endTime\":1746473837},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"do that through creation of software, connecting them with each other, giving them access to tools that they''re curious about. \",\"startTime\":1746473837,\"endTime\":1746473845},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"I came to that through teaching.\",\"startTime\":1746473848,\"endTime\":1746473849},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"That was early to to be able to learn about what was coming with respect to AI on the back of deep learning in 2017 to 2020. \",\"startTime\":1746473852,\"endTime\":1746473861},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"And I got to talk to people who were building it and then translate what they knew into learning experience for lots and lots of developers and data scientists. \",\"startTime\":1746473861,\"endTime\":1746473869},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"Now that it''s more ubiquitous, I''m focused on.\",\"startTime\":1746473870,\"endTime\":1746473873},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"What this looks like for teachers.\",\"startTime\":1746473873,\"endTime\":1746473875},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"Umm, OK.\",\"startTime\":1746473882,\"endTime\":1746473884},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"Stances forward have a forward stance. I lean forward. Umm, towards the future. \",\"startTime\":1746473895,\"endTime\":1746473900},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"I believe that students are very capable and that we should position them as capable. I really love. \",\"startTime\":1746473902,\"endTime\":1746473909},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"When students do the work.\",\"startTime\":1746473911,\"endTime\":1746473912},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"Versus when teachers do the work.\",\"startTime\":1746473912,\"endTime\":1746473914},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"Big believer in clear learning targets.\",\"startTime\":1746473918,\"endTime\":1746473920},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"Big believer in measurement against those zoning targets.\",\"startTime\":1746473921,\"endTime\":1746473924},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"Not a big believer in lecture even though I''m doing a lot of it right now.\",\"startTime\":1746473932,\"endTime\":1746473936},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"I''m a skier straight downhill.\",\"startTime\":1746473955,\"endTime\":1746473957},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"Umm, I try to go skiing when snow is fresh.\",\"startTime\":1746473958,\"endTime\":1746473961},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"On mountains that are big where there are rocks to jump off of.\",\"startTime\":1746473962,\"endTime\":1746473965},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"And I do it a lot, like 60 plus days here.\",\"startTime\":1746473966,\"endTime\":1746473970},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"Small bursts, 2 hours or less most of the time and I''ve been lucky enough to learn. \",\"startTime\":1746473970,\"endTime\":1746473976},{\"speaker\":\"12032\",\"text\":\"I''m great skiers and snowboarders, but I''m a skier.\",\"startTime\":1746473977,\"endTime\":1746473979}]"', '2025-05-06 18:29:40.89431+00', '2025-05-06 18:29:40.89431+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 137, "created_at": "2025-05-06T18:29:40.688Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('a0f16ea6-b05f-4748-a350-7636064052a8', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '137024', '"[{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"A great question when I think about myself setting the culture cultural thermostat in the school. \",\"startTime\":1739285249,\"endTime\":1739285255},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I guess I I think about it twofold. You know, when I think about a thermostat. \",\"startTime\":1739285255,\"endTime\":1739285259},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And you want that that consistent temperature that happens all the time.\",\"startTime\":1739285259,\"endTime\":1739285263},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And to me, that''s that, that that''s the culture. That''s the the feeling of of \",\"startTime\":1739285264,\"endTime\":1739285266},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"warmth. \",\"startTime\":1739285266,\"endTime\":1739285268},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That''s the feeling of security.\",\"startTime\":1739285269,\"endTime\":1739285272},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And then as the temperature drops, I mean, that''s the climate to me. So when \",\"startTime\":1739285272,\"endTime\":1739285275},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I think about the thermostat. \",\"startTime\":1739285275,\"endTime\":1739285277},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You know when the temperature drops? Or maybe it it rises above what the temperature \",\"startTime\":1739285278,\"endTime\":1739285281},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"is supposed to be. \",\"startTime\":1739285281,\"endTime\":1739285284},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And but the climate is the day-to-day stuff where the where the culture is that thermostat is set at 68 or 69 or 72 and just like a thermostat. \",\"startTime\":1739285284,\"endTime\":1739285294},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I think your reading gauges, umm, throughout your whole school, I''ve shared it this way before, like a NASA command dashboard. You have all of these gauges \",\"startTime\":1739285295,\"endTime\":1739285302},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"that you''re looking at and you''re receiving all of these inputs just like a thermometer does. \",\"startTime\":1739285302,\"endTime\":1739285308},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"To try and determine what the actual temperature is.\",\"startTime\":1739285308,\"endTime\":1739285311},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And you as the leader, as you, as you gather that information from all those different gauges that you''re looking at. \",\"startTime\":1739285312,\"endTime\":1739285318},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You try to make decisions.\",\"startTime\":1739285318,\"endTime\":1739285320},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"How are things today? What are What are the gauge is telling me? What''s the \",\"startTime\":1739285320,\"endTime\":1739285322},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"thermostat telling me? \",\"startTime\":1739285322,\"endTime\":1739285324},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Is the temperature really as hot as it is? Because sometimes it feels hotter \",\"startTime\":1739285325,\"endTime\":1739285328},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"or colder than than what it shows on the thermostat. So. \",\"startTime\":1739285328,\"endTime\":1739285331},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You have to really be in tune with the context of your building. You have to \",\"startTime\":1739285331,\"endTime\":1739285334},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"be in tune with the context of your staff, the kids and so many other things to really get a true. \",\"startTime\":1739285334,\"endTime\":1739285340},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Thermostat measurement around culture.\",\"startTime\":1739285341,\"endTime\":1739285344},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, I think that one piece comes to mind when I think about influencing the school''s culture. \",\"startTime\":1739285374,\"endTime\":1739285380},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I was working really hard in elementary school to uplift student strengths.\",\"startTime\":1739285380,\"endTime\":1739285386},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And looking at that from a student centered lens.\",\"startTime\":1739285387,\"endTime\":1739285391},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And and knowing that every student had something inherently in them.\",\"startTime\":1739285392,\"endTime\":1739285397},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That they felt comfortable and confident about in themselves. It could be whatever. \",\"startTime\":1739285397,\"endTime\":1739285401},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And I I I stole an idea from a couple of principles up in in Canada years ago. \",\"startTime\":1739285402,\"endTime\":1739285409},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And it was called Identity Day.\",\"startTime\":1739285410,\"endTime\":1739285412},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And what we ended up doing was all of our fifth graders, and it eventually spread to other grade levels, but. \",\"startTime\":1739285412,\"endTime\":1739285419},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"The very first year, all of the 5th graders produced something that they identified with, that they thought they were comfortable and confident. \",\"startTime\":1739285419,\"endTime\":1739285426},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And strings based, umm and they.\",\"startTime\":1739285427,\"endTime\":1739285429},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Put on a display and they brought in whatever it was and on our one of our last days of school where we have this. \",\"startTime\":1739285429,\"endTime\":1739285436},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Giant assembly and parents command and community members come in.\",\"startTime\":1739285436,\"endTime\":1739285439},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"We had the gym all set up with tables and whatnot and all of our fifth graders. \",\"startTime\":1739285439,\"endTime\":1739285444},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Set up their displays, their their identity day displays and kids in the entire building from kindergarten all the way through and. \",\"startTime\":1739285444,\"endTime\":1739285451},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Parents and community members just kind of.\",\"startTime\":1739285451,\"endTime\":1739285453},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Walked from table to table and listened to the kids talk.\",\"startTime\":1739285454,\"endTime\":1739285456},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And to hear the stories of the students and why they loved rocks.\",\"startTime\":1739285458,\"endTime\":1739285464},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Why they loved wakeboarding, why they loved reading, why they loved whatever BMX biking. \",\"startTime\":1739285465,\"endTime\":1739285471},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Didn''t matter, it was something that the students.\",\"startTime\":1739285471,\"endTime\":1739285474},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Saw themselves as confident in and and.\",\"startTime\":1739285475,\"endTime\":1739285478},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I think that really helped shape the culture of the building.\",\"startTime\":1739285478,\"endTime\":1739285482},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"To identifying individual strengths of kids and uplifting those and and being a student centered, focused school. \",\"startTime\":1739285483,\"endTime\":1739285490},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Man, there''s a great question that hits home.\",\"startTime\":1739285519,\"endTime\":1739285521},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"When we think about moving to Tier 1 instruction and MTSS strategies and PBIS and and a variety of different things with that and social emotional learning. \",\"startTime\":1739285521,\"endTime\":1739285529},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"SEL pieces restorative justice initiatives are a big part of that allows.\",\"startTime\":1739285530,\"endTime\":1739285534},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Students to talk things out and figure things out and, and it is a, it is a little bit of a, well, it is a big change for a lot of just veteran teachers, but teachers in general. \",\"startTime\":1739285536,\"endTime\":1739285545},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Depending on how they''ve been been brought up through and learned and.\",\"startTime\":1739285545,\"endTime\":1739285550},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Through their own educational experiences.\",\"startTime\":1739285551,\"endTime\":1739285553},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I think it''s extremely important that as a leader, anytime you''re making systemic change. \",\"startTime\":1739285554,\"endTime\":1739285561},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And in this case, the district has mandated something that the staff doesn''t want. \",\"startTime\":1739285562,\"endTime\":1739285565},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You may want it as the leader, but the majority of your staff may not want it. \",\"startTime\":1739285566,\"endTime\":1739285569},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"But anytime you run into circumstances like that, it''s to me, it''s extremely important the leader leans into the context of the building. \",\"startTime\":1739285569,\"endTime\":1739285576},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"What is the school context around restorative practices? How do people what \",\"startTime\":1739285578,\"endTime\":1739285581},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"what do? What does our school believe around that? What do the kids feel? What \",\"startTime\":1739285581,\"endTime\":1739285584},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"does the staff feel? \",\"startTime\":1739285584,\"endTime\":1739285586},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"What do they think? Umm, and then you dwindle that down into individual context. \",\"startTime\":1739285586,\"endTime\":1739285591},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Is the the teacher that''s resistant? Is the resistance coming from a stance \",\"startTime\":1739285592,\"endTime\":1739285596},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"of I don''t know the skill set to to do this and I just need assistance in learning what to do? Is there reticence to do this because they firmly believe that this \",\"startTime\":1739285596,\"endTime\":1739285604},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"is not the right way to approach student discipline, student management, student behaviors? \",\"startTime\":1739285604,\"endTime\":1739285612},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And so again when we.\",\"startTime\":1739285613,\"endTime\":1739285616},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Sometimes when we hear the.\",\"startTime\":1739285616,\"endTime\":1739285617},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"The workload concerns and the skepticism and the misalignment and some and the resistance that comes with that. \",\"startTime\":1739285618,\"endTime\":1739285623},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It''s not necessarily because somebody doesn''t want to, it''s because they''re scared of their skill set or they''re fearful they don''t have the skills in order to do it effectively. \",\"startTime\":1739285624,\"endTime\":1739285634},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And umm, I think it''s, it''s really important for the leader to.\",\"startTime\":1739285634,\"endTime\":1739285639},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Convey stories of success.\",\"startTime\":1739285640,\"endTime\":1739285644},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And and.\",\"startTime\":1739285645,\"endTime\":1739285646},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You don''t have to say the district is mandating. This is why we''re doing it. \",\"startTime\":1739285646,\"endTime\":1739285649},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"''Cause as the leader, the, the, the umm, the delicacy, Well, the delicacy, I don''t know that''s the right word or not, but this art and science of, of leadership is something that that. \",\"startTime\":1739285650,\"endTime\":1739285661},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Have thought about a lot. You know, there''s there''s a science to what we do. \",\"startTime\":1739285662,\"endTime\":1739285667},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"But there''s an also an art about how things get done and knowing.\",\"startTime\":1739285667,\"endTime\":1739285671},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Who you are as a leader and who I need to be with individual groups and within a building. \",\"startTime\":1739285671,\"endTime\":1739285676},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Is important too, because the way I the way I talk with a teacher that that is. \",\"startTime\":1739285677,\"endTime\":1739285682},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Resistant because of workload concerns might be very different than a teacher that has skepticism. Will this really work? \",\"startTime\":1739285683,\"endTime\":1739285690},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And and so the planning part of of.\",\"startTime\":1739285691,\"endTime\":1739285693},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Navigating this, I think would be. Is not not I think. I mean, I know it is, \",\"startTime\":1739285694,\"endTime\":1739285697},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"haven''t been there before. Is extremely important. \",\"startTime\":1739285697,\"endTime\":1739285701},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And then at a certain point, it''s just like we''re going.\",\"startTime\":1739285704,\"endTime\":1739285707},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Because we''re not gonna get buy in from every single person.\",\"startTime\":1739285708,\"endTime\":1739285712},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"But when they see their success, hopefully everybody else comes along.\",\"startTime\":1739285712,\"endTime\":1739285715}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:27.880957+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:27.880957+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 430, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:27.809Z", "session_title": "From Reflective to Transformative: Leading with Purpose in Challenging Climates", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1435", "name": "From Reflective to Transformative: Leading with Purpose in Challenging Climates", "tags": [{"name": "BEL"}, {"name": "LSL"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('6a640d88-be87-4ada-8204-baf68d23ad70', '713b8455-cc3b-4ab1-bcfb-255f93bf56b0', '137070', '"[{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Good. Thank you.\",\"startTime\":1739483374,\"endTime\":1739483375},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Just testing, testing some tech out.\",\"startTime\":1739483375,\"endTime\":1739483378},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Good, good.\",\"startTime\":1739483375,\"endTime\":1739483376},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"The hot chocolate, by the way, is money.\",\"startTime\":1739483380,\"endTime\":1739483382},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Icebreaker.\",\"startTime\":1739483380,\"endTime\":1739483381},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yes, yes, put it. Put up my coffee each day and I have the poor guys mocha.\",\"startTime\":1739483383,\"endTime\":1739483388},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"All right, Greet your partner. Hi, Jeff. Good to see you.\",\"startTime\":1739483392,\"endTime\":1739483395},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Hi, Mike. I mean Scott.\",\"startTime\":1739483396,\"endTime\":1739483398},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Thank you. There you go.\",\"startTime\":1739483397,\"endTime\":1739483399},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Umm, let''s see here. Share your first experience. Do we have to go through this \",\"startTime\":1739483399,\"endTime\":1739483402},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"all the way or are we good now or? \",\"startTime\":1739483402,\"endTime\":1739483405},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Let''s try it out. It''s the data. Yeah, Well, I''m also curious, what''s your, \",\"startTime\":1739483405,\"endTime\":1739483408},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Let''s go through it, OK?\",\"startTime\":1739483406,\"endTime\":1739483407},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"what''s your first? \",\"startTime\":1739483408,\"endTime\":1739483411},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh jeez, first experience using that. First I remember it was. I''ll never forget \",\"startTime\":1739483409,\"endTime\":1739483412},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"it. \",\"startTime\":1739483412,\"endTime\":1739483414},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Is up at 4 points Sheraton in the Seatac area and I was screwing around and I made songs out of the. \",\"startTime\":1739483415,\"endTime\":1739483421},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Snoop Dogg genre and then I would change the song up into a cowboy style. Then \",\"startTime\":1739483421,\"endTime\":1739483425},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I did some poems and and and. \",\"startTime\":1739483425,\"endTime\":1739483428},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Used my friend''s dog''s name and his and he was just a puppy being a pain in the ass. So I made some. I just, I was, I was creating songs. \",\"startTime\":1739483430,\"endTime\":1739483437},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And changing the changing the genre up, up. And it was so damn funny. This all \",\"startTime\":1739483438,\"endTime\":1739483441},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"the differences, it was so funny. \",\"startTime\":1739483441,\"endTime\":1739483444},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah. That was like March or April a couple years ago actually.\",\"startTime\":1739483444,\"endTime\":1739483449},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That''s awesome. That''s awesome.\",\"startTime\":1739483446,\"endTime\":1739483447},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh I like it, I had some similar experience doing like generating some music but I don''t know how AI was built or just some programming so I''m not going to use that as my first one. \",\"startTime\":1739483451,\"endTime\":1739483462},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I remember some things along the way, but the one that really got me was.\",\"startTime\":1739483462,\"endTime\":1739483466},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I was so excited because I''ve been reading and and listening to and watching podcasts and videos about AI and what it can do and then finally Chat CBT comes out and I, I''m like OK ChatGPT. \",\"startTime\":1739483467,\"endTime\":1739483477},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739483473,\"endTime\":1739483475},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''ve been organizing my Google Drive with all of this cool stuff and I''ve had all of these parts and pieces and I know it needs better organized and I want to synthesize it all together. Here we go. \",\"startTime\":1739483478,\"endTime\":1739483489},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And it wasn''t ready at all to do that today. I could do that ''cause I can connect \",\"startTime\":1739483489,\"endTime\":1739483493},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it. And then even in Google Drive, you can summarize that it''s built in, summarize \",\"startTime\":1739483493,\"endTime\":1739483497},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, right.\",\"startTime\":1739483494,\"endTime\":1739483495},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"this folder. Or I''m like, I''ve been wanting. I''ve tried to do that before. I \",\"startTime\":1739483497,\"endTime\":1739483501},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"saw that on my Google Drive page, by the way, look on yours, like just pause for a second next time, like up in the top of my ass book. \",\"startTime\":1739483501,\"endTime\":1739483508},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, eat it.\",\"startTime\":1739483504,\"endTime\":1739483505},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I''m, I''m writing. Really. I''m writing that down. OK, good. Yeah, ''cause my Google \",\"startTime\":1739483508,\"endTime\":1739483511},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Drive''s a mess. \",\"startTime\":1739483511,\"endTime\":1739483514},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So I, I asked, and then there was another one like, hey, here are some sample lessons. And here''s a sample structure with a teacher guide. Let''s make some \",\"startTime\":1739483512,\"endTime\":1739483520},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"more ones for this. And I was like, I wanted to spit out a whole unit and it \",\"startTime\":1739483520,\"endTime\":1739483524},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"was no, it wasn''t ready for it. No, no. \",\"startTime\":1739483524,\"endTime\":1739483528},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"What was ready for that? Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739483526,\"endTime\":1739483528},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So I was I was reading too much and had been in theory headspace too much and didn''t meet. \",\"startTime\":1739483529,\"endTime\":1739483535},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Where the tools were functional, yet it was like, I want to drive a car 80,000 miles an hour. Well, Jeff, we can''t. Yeah, yes. \",\"startTime\":1739483536,\"endTime\":1739483543},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right. Got it.\",\"startTime\":1739483539,\"endTime\":1739483541},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Here here ya.\",\"startTime\":1739483546,\"endTime\":1739483550},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"All right.\",\"startTime\":1739483548,\"endTime\":1739483549},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, share your thoughts on real fears versus misplaced fears about using AI tools in education. Then ask your partner to add to your answer. Does yours \",\"startTime\":1739483550,\"endTime\":1739483558},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"say share or does it say listen to Jeff or something? \",\"startTime\":1739483558,\"endTime\":1739483562},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Mine says ask your partner.\",\"startTime\":1739483563,\"endTime\":1739483565},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1739483565,\"endTime\":1739483565},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So what do you think are some fears, real fears versus misplaced fears about using AI tools in education? \",\"startTime\":1739483566,\"endTime\":1739483571},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think one, that it''s going to replace us. There''s we''re just going to have \",\"startTime\":1739483573,\"endTime\":1739483577},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"a bunch of robots in the classroom. \",\"startTime\":1739483577,\"endTime\":1739483580},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739483579,\"endTime\":1739483580},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I won''t. I won''t have a job.\",\"startTime\":1739483582,\"endTime\":1739483584},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It''s going to take over the world.\",\"startTime\":1739483585,\"endTime\":1739483586},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1739483587,\"endTime\":1739483588},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Gonna read all of my thoughts.\",\"startTime\":1739483588,\"endTime\":1739483590},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, all of those kind of things. Those are my first ones.\",\"startTime\":1739483592,\"endTime\":1739483594},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"About versus thoughts on real fears versus misplaced fears, I think real fears are. \",\"startTime\":1739483595,\"endTime\":1739483602},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Versus misplaced fears.\",\"startTime\":1739483599,\"endTime\":1739483601},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Will I use the tool effectively in the way that I want to and still keep my own identity and use it to create my own identity the way I want to craft my the way I see myself and who I want to be? Or will I just get inundated with \",\"startTime\":1739483604,\"endTime\":1739483619},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"so much information and so many I could use this tools that I no longer have my own? \",\"startTime\":1739483619,\"endTime\":1739483629},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1739483621,\"endTime\":1739483621},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Identity and agency in it, but I''m more reacting to all of the.\",\"startTime\":1739483631,\"endTime\":1739483635},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Pop ups and the bells and whistles and the Jeff do this and Jeff do that and answer the e-mail and do this thing because I''m responding and I''m a reactionary individual rather than the one at the control of my life and and using the tools. \",\"startTime\":1739483635,\"endTime\":1739483649},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, right.\",\"startTime\":1739483642,\"endTime\":1739483644},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So I guess in the one way to say it. \",\"startTime\":1739483649,\"endTime\":1739483654},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739483650,\"endTime\":1739483650},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Stealing this from Matthew Green, who''s doing the programming? Am I programming \",\"startTime\":1739483654,\"endTime\":1739483658},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it or is it programming me? Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1739483658,\"endTime\":1739483662},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Programming you yeah, yeah, You know, I was just thinking about that as you were talking like some of the the real fears of. \",\"startTime\":1739483661,\"endTime\":1739483667},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Priority see massive isolation among kids and teenagers and depression and anxiety and diminished mental health and. \",\"startTime\":1739483669,\"endTime\":1739483676},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And is this.\",\"startTime\":1739483677,\"endTime\":1739483679},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think your phone''s ringing or something. I can''t hear you.\",\"startTime\":1739483688,\"endTime\":1739483691},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I still can''t hear you. I lost your your audio.\",\"startTime\":1739483700,\"endTime\":1739483703},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Can you hear my audio?\",\"startTime\":1739483704,\"endTime\":1739483705},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"OK, still there.\",\"startTime\":1739483727,\"endTime\":1739483727},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m here. That was really interesting just for feedback when it started ringing \",\"startTime\":1739483728,\"endTime\":1739483731},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"your phone, I it cut out your audio so you were saying something so I didn''t catch that and then. \",\"startTime\":1739483731,\"endTime\":1739483737},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"When you''re done with the call. I''m guessing now, now that I can hear you.\",\"startTime\":1739483738,\"endTime\":1739483741},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Then it came back so it it shut my audio off to you.\",\"startTime\":1739483741,\"endTime\":1739483744},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"OK. And there there is like the the.\",\"startTime\":1739483745,\"endTime\":1739483747},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I call it the hamburger, like up top where it says guts and fear and AI.\",\"startTime\":1739483747,\"endTime\":1739483750},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm. Yeah. Oh yeah. Yeah. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739483751,\"endTime\":1739483753},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"The hamburger there, you press that and it has something there. Restart audio \",\"startTime\":1739483751,\"endTime\":1739483753},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"and video. \",\"startTime\":1739483753,\"endTime\":1739483756},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So like, if I, if we''re missing something, we could do that. But anyway, so \",\"startTime\":1739483757,\"endTime\":1739483761},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"the let''s talk about just just that that, that that isolation is going to lead to more lack of lack of communication among people, lack of, of whatever it is, you know, is, is AI gonna replace and not replace friends or anything like that, but maybe. \",\"startTime\":1739483761,\"endTime\":1739483774},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh cool.\",\"startTime\":1739483763,\"endTime\":1739483764},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, tell me more. Your depression? No.\",\"startTime\":1739483764,\"endTime\":1739483767},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You know, do I, do I really need to engage in, in community and society as a whole as a, as a kid? \",\"startTime\":1739483775,\"endTime\":1739483781},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And then how does that lead to education, you know, Anyway, just a few things around that and and. \",\"startTime\":1739483781,\"endTime\":1739483786},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You know some of the fears.\",\"startTime\":1739483787,\"endTime\":1739483789},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Whether placed reality or misplaced fears is.\",\"startTime\":1739483790,\"endTime\":1739483794},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"The authenticity of learning you know how how are how are how are kids.\",\"startTime\":1739483794,\"endTime\":1739483799},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Going to build learning pathways in their minds.\",\"startTime\":1739483800,\"endTime\":1739483804},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"If if they''re like are the Synapse is going to get connected? I don''t know if \",\"startTime\":1739483804,\"endTime\":1739483807},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"they''re supposed to or however that all that works, but are are are those going to get connected? \",\"startTime\":1739483807,\"endTime\":1739483813},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"In a manner that will allow them to.\",\"startTime\":1739483813,\"endTime\":1739483816},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Think in the future or they''ll be misfires. I don''t know if I''m explaining it \",\"startTime\":1739483816,\"endTime\":1739483819},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"very well, but it''s just a wondering about if I''m just reading all this stuff on AI and I''m not I''m not wrestling with you know how learning is just just not to be difficult and confusing, but. \",\"startTime\":1739483819,\"endTime\":1739483829},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"If you don''t have some of that struggle.\",\"startTime\":1739483830,\"endTime\":1739483832},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Are you are you, are you creating a brain that''s going to be have the capacity for you to? \",\"startTime\":1739483833,\"endTime\":1739483839},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Problem solve and think in the future.\",\"startTime\":1739483840,\"endTime\":1739483842},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, Yeah, I think that''s right along. What I was trying to say is that if \",\"startTime\":1739483842,\"endTime\":1739483846},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m not the one who is using AI as a tool. \",\"startTime\":1739483846,\"endTime\":1739483850},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Thinking about brain growth and habits of mind use appropriate tools strategically. \",\"startTime\":1739483851,\"endTime\":1739483855},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"If I''m not even being mindful of that and I''m not the problem solver, then I''m not going to be growing my neural pathways strong the way that I should be as a human, which will be adaptable. And then if I amend the flip flop of that, \",\"startTime\":1739483855,\"endTime\":1739483868},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739483863,\"endTime\":1739483865},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"reacting to things, getting the dopamine hit, just getting rid of the buttons on my screen, I''m not really growing my my brain for a healthy future, Jeff. \",\"startTime\":1739483868,\"endTime\":1739483877},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right, right.\",\"startTime\":1739483874,\"endTime\":1739483875},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I just am A and same with our kids. \",\"startTime\":1739483877,\"endTime\":1739483881},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"We''re going to be, as we see students today in our world and culture today.\",\"startTime\":1739483881,\"endTime\":1739483885},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Imbalanced chemically in their brains on a dopamine addiction trail and they''re not growing the neural pathways strong to be the problem solvers, the effective communicators. Once you can choose what tools to use at the right time. Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1739483886,\"endTime\":1739483902},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"No. Great.\",\"startTime\":1739483890,\"endTime\":1739483892},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739483898,\"endTime\":1739483899},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I mean, we all go to, we all tend to go to that path of least resistance from time to time. And and does this elevate that even more where like you''re saying \",\"startTime\":1739483901,\"endTime\":1739483907},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"the the. \",\"startTime\":1739483907,\"endTime\":1739483910},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"The neural pathways don''t get developed because I''m just taking the first thing and moving on and getting done, yeah. \",\"startTime\":1739483910,\"endTime\":1739483916},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Take turns sharing. What research have you come across regarding biases in GPT \",\"startTime\":1739483919,\"endTime\":1739483921},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"models? \",\"startTime\":1739483921,\"endTime\":1739483924},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I mean the I don''t know if it''s been researched but just reading about just the implicit bias conscious stuff and relationship to race, ethnicity, being male dominated, male centered. \",\"startTime\":1739483924,\"endTime\":1739483934},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It''s gotten better, but you know, unless you''re explicit about telling it, I want 3. \",\"startTime\":1739483936,\"endTime\":1739483941},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Black and brown authors or whatever the case may be, or I''ve noticed some of the educational stuff I''ve put in there, it''s really trended toward. \",\"startTime\":1739483941,\"endTime\":1739483948},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Umm, a white.\",\"startTime\":1739483950,\"endTime\":1739483950},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Centric kind of solution and.\",\"startTime\":1739483951,\"endTime\":1739483955},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And if you''re not aware of that or you''re, you have the inability to recognize that, which I don''t. I''m sure I''ve missed some. \",\"startTime\":1739483955,\"endTime\":1739483963},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"But those are some of the things I''ve I''ve I''ve seen.\",\"startTime\":1739483964,\"endTime\":1739483966},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yep, same. It''s it''s all in that knowledge base that''s used being used to train \",\"startTime\":1739483967,\"endTime\":1739483972},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"or has been used to train the the the these assistants or these GPT models. \",\"startTime\":1739483972,\"endTime\":1739483978},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739483978,\"endTime\":1739483979},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And other right along the lines of that same thing for research around bias, ethnicity, fields of study, age groups. \",\"startTime\":1739483979,\"endTime\":1739483987},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It dispositions for learning or culture even even what the value is around struggle for example. \",\"startTime\":1739483989,\"endTime\":1739483996},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Like how, how do we value struggle? And is that based upon good scientific evidence? \",\"startTime\":1739483996,\"endTime\":1739484001},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Or is it just a general common knowledge? And then anecdotally asking GPT to \",\"startTime\":1739484001,\"endTime\":1739484006},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"to give me a quick summary or adapt this teacher guide and it would give me really bad first things. Hey, what you could do to start the math lesson is \",\"startTime\":1739484006,\"endTime\":1739484016},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right, right.\",\"startTime\":1739484013,\"endTime\":1739484015},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and I''m like, no, don''t, don''t ever do that. \",\"startTime\":1739484016,\"endTime\":1739484021},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"No, no, no. Not good, Not good.\",\"startTime\":1739484021,\"endTime\":1739484023},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Then because it''s because it comes from popular knowledge or a common myth that''s trained into it because if it''s coming from the basis of this is just what people are saying. So I can learn how to chat as a GPT because I just want to have \",\"startTime\":1739484022,\"endTime\":1739484035},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"chat doesn''t mean it''s well informed in these other things. And that''s another \",\"startTime\":1739484035,\"endTime\":1739484039},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484036,\"endTime\":1739484038},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"one that I''ve read in an articles as well, just to give you more clarity to it. But practically same thing is if you don''t have. \",\"startTime\":1739484039,\"endTime\":1739484048},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Specificity when you''re training out your model.\",\"startTime\":1739484049,\"endTime\":1739484052},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And it''s really challenging to make sure you have the knowledge base in the right place. Like we want to be really clear about this is a ChatGPT or is this \",\"startTime\":1739484053,\"endTime\":1739484063},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"a, a GPT assistant for the Washington State school principals? \",\"startTime\":1739484063,\"endTime\":1739484068},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484066,\"endTime\":1739484068},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So that they''re aligned to their framework, they''re aligned to Ospi''s menus of best practices, and then take the language around that. But what''s the model \",\"startTime\":1739484068,\"endTime\":1739484076},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"built around and, and what''s it focused on ''cause if it''s just for chat, it can chat, but just know it''s gonna chat like anybody can chat and it''s trained on all this general thing. Yeah, I''m with you too. Very much so. Biased Bias, \",\"startTime\":1739484076,\"endTime\":1739484088},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right, it can chat.\",\"startTime\":1739484082,\"endTime\":1739484084},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484085,\"endTime\":1739484086},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"bias. It''s there. It''s just built around, Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1739484088,\"endTime\":1739484092},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, recognize it.\",\"startTime\":1739484092,\"endTime\":1739484094},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Read the scenario.\",\"startTime\":1739484098,\"endTime\":1739484099},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Teacher finds that chat cheapy tea.\",\"startTime\":1739484101,\"endTime\":1739484103},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Degenerated or that GPT generated content is biased? How should they address \",\"startTime\":1739484104,\"endTime\":1739484108},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"this with their students? \",\"startTime\":1739484108,\"endTime\":1739484111},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think first letting every student and user know that every GPT is biased. \",\"startTime\":1739484114,\"endTime\":1739484119},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I am biased meaning that it''s from my perspective, it''s from my construct, it''s from the way that my brain and my experiences have given me my my well of knowledge. \",\"startTime\":1739484119,\"endTime\":1739484129},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484124,\"endTime\":1739484124},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m culturally biased with what I have from my cultural inheritance and from experiences in life and the way that I learn even to express words and to even in the language that I have, it''s, it''s biasing me just that''s what it is. So. \",\"startTime\":1739484129,\"endTime\":1739484143},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484134,\"endTime\":1739484134},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Telling the students that everybody''s biased, GPTS are biased around their knowledge bases. And then second, you can help your GPT assistant or your GPT by giving \",\"startTime\":1739484144,\"endTime\":1739484153},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484150,\"endTime\":1739484151},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it knowledge based documents. Add this to the document. We want to include this, \",\"startTime\":1739484153,\"endTime\":1739484158},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and as you said, include this kind of author or include this type of person''s perspective. We want to make sure it''s well-rounded. \",\"startTime\":1739484158,\"endTime\":1739484167},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I was, I was seeing this maybe just a little bit different in terms of if I generated an assignment and I give it to the people in the class using ChatGPT or something like that. \",\"startTime\":1739484167,\"endTime\":1739484175},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Umm, but the content that I''ve shared with, with the kids is, is biased and maybe somebody points that out or whatever it is. And so how, how should you \",\"startTime\":1739484176,\"endTime\":1739484182},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"address that with the students? I mean, I think it''s a, you turn it into a learning \",\"startTime\":1739484182,\"endTime\":1739484186},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"situation. What we investigate what, what''s biased about it? What''s, what''s \",\"startTime\":1739484186,\"endTime\":1739484189},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"this, what''s that, you know? \",\"startTime\":1739484189,\"endTime\":1739484192},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"How do you see that showing up? How do you think critically and analytically \",\"startTime\":1739484193,\"endTime\":1739484196},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"about this? What are the what are the structures that you''re gonna put in place \",\"startTime\":1739484196,\"endTime\":1739484199},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"as a as a learner or as a teacher to? \",\"startTime\":1739484199,\"endTime\":1739484202},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Ensure that you''re reducing as much bias as possible. How are you going to grow \",\"startTime\":1739484203,\"endTime\":1739484206},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"your lens around bias? Maybe you compare and contrast. Now you you generate \",\"startTime\":1739484206,\"endTime\":1739484210},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"another lesson. \",\"startTime\":1739484210,\"endTime\":1739484213},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That that says remove all bias of Indigenous languages, what I don''t know, whatever you know, and then do another one that has bias all through it. And so you''re \",\"startTime\":1739484213,\"endTime\":1739484222},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"growing that. So you''re comparing and contrasting growing the knowledge. \",\"startTime\":1739484222,\"endTime\":1739484226},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So kids are becoming more able to recognize that as the product is being being produced and and sent out to them. \",\"startTime\":1739484226,\"endTime\":1739484234},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So that was what I was just thinking about, about that learning, learning piece. \",\"startTime\":1739484236,\"endTime\":1739484240},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah. I really appreciate that you got that. Yeah, I think.\",\"startTime\":1739484236,\"endTime\":1739484238},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I appreciate you got that back to the student in the classroom and what that would look like in in engaging them in discourse around what do you think? What \",\"startTime\":1739484240,\"endTime\":1739484246},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and what could we do about this and where do you be the bias? Yeah, I really \",\"startTime\":1739484246,\"endTime\":1739484249},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"appreciate that. \",\"startTime\":1739484249,\"endTime\":1739484251},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484249,\"endTime\":1739484250},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Really. Tell me more. Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739484251,\"endTime\":1739484253},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Thanks, Scott. Appreciate you.\",\"startTime\":1739484258,\"endTime\":1739484260},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I''ll be right back. See you soon.\",\"startTime\":1739484261,\"endTime\":1739484263},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, I''ll see you in a second. Bye.\",\"startTime\":1739484262,\"endTime\":1739484263}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.394743+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.394743+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 896, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:28.186Z", "session_title": "Navigating AI Responsibly", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1320", "name": "Navigating AI Responsibly", "tags": [{"name": "AI in Education"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('9c50390f-c4ca-4e51-b328-15aceca7704c', 'd8e9db8f-f716-4f11-9fb9-c204d951fd7d', '134653', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"So a current problem of practice or school improvement plan that we are working on is actually riding the school improvement plan. We just completed a strategic \",\"startTime\":1732055101,\"endTime\":1732055114},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"plan that ends in 20-30, so six years. And so we are aligning our. \",\"startTime\":1732055114,\"endTime\":1732055121},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"SIP plan, our school improvement plans with the strategic plan. So that''s kind \",\"startTime\":1732055122,\"endTime\":1732055126},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"of an area that we''re currently working on. And a problem of practice right \",\"startTime\":1732055126,\"endTime\":1732055130},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"now that I''m focused on is intervention in our building. \",\"startTime\":1732055130,\"endTime\":1732055134},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"What that looks like, how we operate, how to best fit intervention time and instead of doing pull out models, doing push insurance. So looking at data and \",\"startTime\":1732055134,\"endTime\":1732055141},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"analyzing that. \",\"startTime\":1732055141,\"endTime\":1732055145},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"So to discuss the progress with my school improvement plan, we''re at the very beginning of the school improvement plan mostly because we have a new format. \",\"startTime\":1732055172,\"endTime\":1732055181},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"We worked on it as a district leadership team about a week ago. We have a meeting \",\"startTime\":1732055181,\"endTime\":1732055186},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"actually this week to discuss future ready and its ability to fit within our school improvement plan at the secondary level middle school. \",\"startTime\":1732055186,\"endTime\":1732055195},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"So progress is at the beginning stages and hopefully have it written here shortly. \",\"startTime\":1732055195,\"endTime\":1732055201},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"Challenges that I anticipate in the coming months, umm, include possibly, umm, staff being out due to illness, uh, and so having to cover staff absences. Umm, \",\"startTime\":1732055221,\"endTime\":1732055234},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"also just kind of that stretch of time where behaviors, uh, tend to increase, uh, as students look forward to breaks and how do we continue to. \",\"startTime\":1732055234,\"endTime\":1732055247},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"Impress upon them the importance of causes of behavior.\",\"startTime\":1732055248,\"endTime\":1732055251},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"Increasing our our incentives and rewards and making sure that students kind of finish strong as we move towards the end of the semester. \",\"startTime\":1732055251,\"endTime\":1732055261}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.097633+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.097633+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 131, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:40.036Z", "session_title": "School Leadership: Describing the Work(BEL LSL)", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1416", "name": "School Leadership: Describing the Work(BEL LSL)", "tags": [{"name": "BEL"}, {"name": "LSL"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('b6ad603e-ab82-4da2-9df8-d6777e030c02', '4f2c17d9-95b8-4de7-8b97-ea6e0874f465', '134626', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11351\",\"text\":\"My name is A.J. Brown, Principal Sacagawea. Hoping to just connect with people \",\"startTime\":1732054516,\"endTime\":1732054520},{\"speaker\":\"11351\",\"text\":\"around the state. Other administrators pick their brains. \",\"startTime\":1732054520,\"endTime\":1732054524}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.267241+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.267241+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 15, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:40.202Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('85717ab3-a722-41b5-af04-0a2d0ccfbb57', 'd8e9db8f-f716-4f11-9fb9-c204d951fd7d', '134630', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"Hi, my name is Katie Hamrick and I''m the principal at East Valley Middle School in Spokane, WA. I''m a first year principal and I hope to learn about a lot of \",\"startTime\":1732054600,\"endTime\":1732054610},{\"speaker\":\"11332\",\"text\":\"things that will help me be successful, run a strong successful building, and work with amazing students and staff. \",\"startTime\":1732054610,\"endTime\":1732054620}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.460052+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.460052+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 25, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:40.255Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('08bf61ce-1e08-4beb-80cd-406a66ebd915', 'cd985910-e971-4907-988f-d311b2adb4d1', '110566', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:55.021299+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:55.021299+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 137, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:54.960Z", "session_title": "Understanding and Utilizing GPT and AI Threads", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "197", "name": "Understanding and Utilizing GPT and AI Threads", "tags": [{"name": "Dream Camp"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "AI in Education"}, {"name": "Freemium"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('372c54a2-73e7-4b6f-9c3d-6c425c95799c', 'e5a67ee9-d30e-4f26-bafd-bf20b9ba4ab6', '138556', '"[{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Name is Michael and I hope to learn about.\",\"startTime\":1746632506,\"endTime\":1746632509},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Better ways to increase the to and through college rate across the state of Washington because I hear it''s struggling. \",\"startTime\":1746632509,\"endTime\":1746632515},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"I know it''s important.\",\"startTime\":1746632516,\"endTime\":1746632517},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"And.\",\"startTime\":1746632518,\"endTime\":1746632519},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I''m here to learn about how people are using.\",\"startTime\":1746632521,\"endTime\":1746632524},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Modern tools.\",\"startTime\":1746632525,\"endTime\":1746632526},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Encouraging the FAFSA, etc.\",\"startTime\":1746632528,\"endTime\":1746632530},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Aggressive, straight downhill, fast.\",\"startTime\":1746632548,\"endTime\":1746632550},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"I tend to lead.\",\"startTime\":1746632553,\"endTime\":1746632554},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Through helping people do things that they think they''re scared of.\",\"startTime\":1746632557,\"endTime\":1746632561},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Kind of like a ski instructor would, or a whitewater kayaking instructor.\",\"startTime\":1746632563,\"endTime\":1746632568},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"I think the people are very capable and.\",\"startTime\":1746632571,\"endTime\":1746632574},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Helping them understand how capable they are is really effective.\",\"startTime\":1746632574,\"endTime\":1746632577},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Hop like a Bunny everywhere I go. Just hippity hop, Hippity hippity hop, hop. \",\"startTime\":1746632595,\"endTime\":1746632598},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Hippity, hippity hop hop like a Bunny.\",\"startTime\":1746632598,\"endTime\":1746632600},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"Not like a deer, not like a kangaroo. I like to hop like a Bunny. It''s so fun. \",\"startTime\":1746632602,\"endTime\":1746632605},{\"speaker\":\"12037\",\"text\":\"At least track of time. I love to hop like a Bunny. \",\"startTime\":1746632605,\"endTime\":1746632609}]"', '2025-05-07 17:02:33.508682+00', '2025-05-07 17:02:33.508682+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 82, "created_at": "2025-05-07T17:02:33.313Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('e79dadb0-1b9d-4dd4-a507-b27db365350d', '8fb45423-222c-4ae3-b697-6e1187167e6e', '137047', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Hey, guys.\",\"startTime\":1739476252,\"endTime\":1739476252},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"This is Diego.\",\"startTime\":1739476252,\"endTime\":1739476253},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"About scientists, software developer and STEAM educator.\",\"startTime\":1739476254,\"endTime\":1739476259},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Nice to meet you all.\",\"startTime\":1739476259,\"endTime\":1739476260},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Here to give it a try and to collaborate.\",\"startTime\":1739476261,\"endTime\":1739476264},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Thank you very much.\",\"startTime\":1739476266,\"endTime\":1739476267},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Hey guys, this is Diego.\",\"startTime\":1739476288,\"endTime\":1739476290},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I''m a math scientist, software developer, STEAM educator and I love being here and can''t wait to meet you virtually. \",\"startTime\":1739476290,\"endTime\":1739476298},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Oh well, I believe in hands on.\",\"startTime\":1739476384,\"endTime\":1739476387},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Learning. I believe in science as a tool.\",\"startTime\":1739476387,\"endTime\":1739476390},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"To explore.\",\"startTime\":1739476392,\"endTime\":1739476393},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I think that the role of the teacher is to facilitate processes. The role of \",\"startTime\":1739476394,\"endTime\":1739476399},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"the learner is to learn whatever they feel. \",\"startTime\":1739476399,\"endTime\":1739476403},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Emotionally connected to.\",\"startTime\":1739476405,\"endTime\":1739476407},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"We we always learn what what we want to learn what you change, I think.\",\"startTime\":1739476409,\"endTime\":1739476414},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Indoor teaching.\",\"startTime\":1739476418,\"endTime\":1739476419},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Things we spent too much time inside and what you stay the same having groups of diverse students all together in. \",\"startTime\":1739476420,\"endTime\":1739476429},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Person in one place? Yeah, that''s it.\",\"startTime\":1739476432,\"endTime\":1739476436},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I''m thinking about kids.\",\"startTime\":1739476437,\"endTime\":1739476438},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Hey, so my stance about learning is that we learned first of all hands on something. \",\"startTime\":1739476458,\"endTime\":1739476465},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"We learned through.\",\"startTime\":1739476465,\"endTime\":1739476466},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Uh, iterative process.\",\"startTime\":1739476468,\"endTime\":1739476469},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Where we go from an idea to something.\",\"startTime\":1739476470,\"endTime\":1739476473},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Concrete materialization.\",\"startTime\":1739476474,\"endTime\":1739476476},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"This realm.\",\"startTime\":1739476477,\"endTime\":1739476478},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"We use science as an exploratory tool.\",\"startTime\":1739476480,\"endTime\":1739476483},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"What''s the role of the teacher is to facilitate the learning?\",\"startTime\":1739476485,\"endTime\":1739476488},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Learning is to actively pursue whatever they want to learn what you change. \",\"startTime\":1739476490,\"endTime\":1739476495},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I think I''m thinking in terms of traditional learning. \",\"startTime\":1739476495,\"endTime\":1739476500},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"And I''m thinking about the school system in particular. I think we should.\",\"startTime\":1739476502,\"endTime\":1739476507},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Less time inside the classroom and what choose?\",\"startTime\":1739476510,\"endTime\":1739476514},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I mean, yeah, in in what you stay the same is that in person learning is.\",\"startTime\":1739476515,\"endTime\":1739476520},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Is better because we perceive other people''s vibes and we can resonate with them. Sometimes that''s a different. \",\"startTime\":1739476521,\"endTime\":1739476529},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"That''s a little different when we connect to virtually, but.\",\"startTime\":1739476530,\"endTime\":1739476533},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I think uh.\",\"startTime\":1739476534,\"endTime\":1739476534},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I can I can perceive the vibes of somebody through.\",\"startTime\":1739476536,\"endTime\":1739476540},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Mediums like this so.\",\"startTime\":1739476541,\"endTime\":1739476542},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Oh well, what do they do for slow activity? I love training jujitsu.\",\"startTime\":1739476570,\"endTime\":1739476574},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I''m a round built. I''ve been training for almost 10 years. It helps me develop \",\"startTime\":1739476575,\"endTime\":1739476578},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"my creativity and my resilience. \",\"startTime\":1739476578,\"endTime\":1739476582},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"And when you''re slow rolling or rolling against another.\",\"startTime\":1739476584,\"endTime\":1739476587},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Person, sometimes you get into this flow mental state where your body moves. \",\"startTime\":1739476589,\"endTime\":1739476594},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Umm, myself.\",\"startTime\":1739476595,\"endTime\":1739476596},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"I also love playing guitar, making music, I love improvising with other musicians. \",\"startTime\":1739476597,\"endTime\":1739476603},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"That''s really cool for me and.\",\"startTime\":1739476604,\"endTime\":1739476606},{\"speaker\":\"11874\",\"text\":\"Yeah, there''s two things I do for fun, Jiu jitsu and music.\",\"startTime\":1739476607,\"endTime\":1739476610}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:27.880696+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:27.880696+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 156, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:27.828Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('c12da6aa-e9a3-4b94-a177-5398ba10818a', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '135678', '"[{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"A. What are the chances?\",\"startTime\":1734048046,\"endTime\":1734048047},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I was like, hey, I know that guy.\",\"startTime\":1734048047,\"endTime\":1734048049},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I''m like, I know I get so excited when I know people that''s like, I''m not, I don''t know who I''m getting, but it''s just so fun. It''s like, we did this the \",\"startTime\":1734048050,\"endTime\":1734048055},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"other day. So, so. \",\"startTime\":1734048055,\"endTime\":1734048057},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Well, I like your e-mail that you you like talking to yourself.\",\"startTime\":1734048055,\"endTime\":1734048059},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Well, I might have lied a little bit, but it''s actually, it''s not bad. It feels \",\"startTime\":1734048062,\"endTime\":1734048065},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"strange at first and then you''re like, oh gosh, I should take this seriously. \",\"startTime\":1734048065,\"endTime\":1734048069},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm, mm-hmm. I know I was like one of one of the first ones that I did. I \",\"startTime\":1734048071,\"endTime\":1734048075},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048074,\"endTime\":1734048074},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"was like, oh, was that thorough enough? I don''t know if I like really expanded \",\"startTime\":1734048075,\"endTime\":1734048079},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"on that answer enough or that it got enough of the words that I wanted it to get so. \",\"startTime\":1734048079,\"endTime\":1734048086},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Well, cool.\",\"startTime\":1734048087,\"endTime\":1734048088},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Absolutely love it. So yeah. Yeah. So let me see. Let''s press more. Icebreaker. \",\"startTime\":1734048088,\"endTime\":1734048091},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Fun fact, something involved in during a high school that helped pay that. Whatever. \",\"startTime\":1734048091,\"endTime\":1734048095},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Let''s go to the next question. That''s right. Yeah. No, no, you''re good. No, \",\"startTime\":1734048095,\"endTime\":1734048099},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh, I''m sorry, yeah, I totally pressed the wrong OK.\",\"startTime\":1734048098,\"endTime\":1734048101},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"no, we''re good. We''re good. \",\"startTime\":1734048099,\"endTime\":1734048102},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1734048103,\"endTime\":1734048103},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So yeah, you''ve got question two there. Yeah, OK, gotcha. OK.\",\"startTime\":1734048107,\"endTime\":1734048114},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Oh, and I should tell you, the last two times that I''ve done this, and \",\"startTime\":1734048110,\"endTime\":1734048113},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''ve only done it twice. The first time like I lost connection and it kicked \",\"startTime\":1734048113,\"endTime\":1734048117},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"me out of the conversation. And then the second time, like it kind of froze \",\"startTime\":1734048117,\"endTime\":1734048121},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"on me. So like I''ve had two technical things. So hopefully that doesn''t happen, \",\"startTime\":1734048121,\"endTime\":1734048124},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"but. \",\"startTime\":1734048124,\"endTime\":1734048128},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Well, we''ll see. We''ll see. Yeah, Yeah. No worries. No worries.\",\"startTime\":1734048130,\"endTime\":1734048133},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK, sure. So I still feel relatively new to high school, but I think some of \",\"startTime\":1734048133,\"endTime\":1734048138},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"But, uh, so why don''t you answer this question and then I''ll tell you what what what we did or what I remember doing, Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1734048135,\"endTime\":1734048141},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"the things that we have in place is like the high school and beyond planned, which is that requirement that students are kind of thinking about. \",\"startTime\":1734048138,\"endTime\":1734048147},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"You know what, what they''re gonna pursue afterwards and then, you know, since I''ve been a student, they kinda have these different pathway options to graduation to really start students thinking about, you know, are they gonna go to a trade school afterwards? Are they thinking no school, like are they just gonna go \",\"startTime\":1734048153,\"endTime\":1734048171},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"into the workforce and you know, I mean, are they gonna pursue college or whatever military? So that''s part of it. You know, a lot of that''s in our counseling \",\"startTime\":1734048171,\"endTime\":1734048179},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1734048179,\"endTime\":1734048180},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"center. And then we also have just different. \",\"startTime\":1734048179,\"endTime\":1734048183},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Informational nights for families that want to learn more about the different plans kind of after senior year and options. And we start presenting those students \",\"startTime\":1734048184,\"endTime\":1734048194},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"junior years. So we call it a soon to be senior night and invite a lot of different \",\"startTime\":1734048194,\"endTime\":1734048198},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1734048197,\"endTime\":1734048198},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"resources from the community to come talk about everything from the FAFSA to, you know, military branches. \",\"startTime\":1734048198,\"endTime\":1734048208},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, so and then all of our people in the Career Center are available all day long and that we''re lucky to have them staffed as full time employees. \",\"startTime\":1734048209,\"endTime\":1734048219},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yes, Good, good. Well, this is what thanks for sharing all that helps \",\"startTime\":1734048209,\"endTime\":1734048214},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"me remember what what what I did with the help of a lot of other people. And \",\"startTime\":1734048214,\"endTime\":1734048218},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"it really started with the creation of, I''ll call them pathways that kids were interested in that that were based upon what would have been the previous high school and beyond plan. So with a student coming up from the from the middle \",\"startTime\":1734048218,\"endTime\":1734048231},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"So.\",\"startTime\":1734048223,\"endTime\":1734048224},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"school was like. \",\"startTime\":1734048231,\"endTime\":1734048235},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Science. A technology track, A STEM track. We had we had created like 7 different \",\"startTime\":1734048249,\"endTime\":1734048251},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"pathways. \",\"startTime\":1734048251,\"endTime\":1734048254},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That already pre slugged a lot of classes that kids had to take that were required, but the pre slugging of coursework actually allowed them to meet every single cater requirement for a four year school if that''s what they wanted to do. The \",\"startTime\":1734048257,\"endTime\":1734048270},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.\",\"startTime\":1734048260,\"endTime\":1734048264},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"kids didn''t know that, the families didn''t know that, but we knew that because the goal was to leave is to have to allow the student to have as many opportunities possible on the other side. \",\"startTime\":1734048270,\"endTime\":1734048283},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That they could have. And so we had. They would literally, literally get sheets \",\"startTime\":1734048285,\"endTime\":1734048290},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm.\",\"startTime\":1734048288,\"endTime\":1734048288},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"of paper with courses already filled in over a four year plan. \",\"startTime\":1734048290,\"endTime\":1734048294},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And they''d have room for electives in their freshman year, sophomore year, junior year, senior year. And then after those will get filled out again. That would \",\"startTime\":1734048295,\"endTime\":1734048302},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"set them up as academic press. And we want to take challenging coursework. We \",\"startTime\":1734048302,\"endTime\":1734048306},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"would have one-on-one meetings with kids, call them down after all the schedules came in and said, you know what, your test, your assessments. Three years have \",\"startTime\":1734048306,\"endTime\":1734048314},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"shown that you can succeed at this level. So we''re going to move you to this \",\"startTime\":1734048314,\"endTime\":1734048317},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"dishonest course or this AP course. And they''re like, what? \",\"startTime\":1734048317,\"endTime\":1734048321},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And then we work in conjunction with the counseling center to make that happen. \",\"startTime\":1734048323,\"endTime\":1734048326},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And we did all the other things with FAFSA and, and and pieces like that and then our advisory program. \",\"startTime\":1734048326,\"endTime\":1734048331},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"From the freshman year through the senior year has really created and developed, particularly around the freshman year was was transition high school and study habits and all those kinds of fees. And sophomore year was was really diving \",\"startTime\":1734048333,\"endTime\":1734048344},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"into your what would be now the high school and beyond plan and figuring out next steps. And and then the junior year was like, OK, college applications. \",\"startTime\":1734048344,\"endTime\":1734048352},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"What''s that look like fast that we had invited junior parents to come to fast tonight is to get an understanding and then that that''s and the military and we brought everybody in like follow people. \",\"startTime\":1734048352,\"endTime\":1734048363},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1734048355,\"endTime\":1734048355},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And that that senior year was you''re filling out application and doing resumes and I''ll discuss. But the basic underpin was that course work that that the \",\"startTime\":1734048364,\"endTime\":1734048371},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"kids didn''t even know we had kids like surprise. Well, I don''t know if I''ve \",\"startTime\":1734048371,\"endTime\":1734048374},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1734048372,\"endTime\":1734048372},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"taken, I don''t know if I''ve taken the right classes to go to four year school. \",\"startTime\":1734048374,\"endTime\":1734048377},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And that''s not the end all be all. But we looked at like all the community colleges \",\"startTime\":1734048377,\"endTime\":1734048380},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"around Spokane and every single one of them, the certification required like an Algebra 2 level of math. So we just required every kid to take Algebra 2. \",\"startTime\":1734048380,\"endTime\":1734048387},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"They didn''t know. They don''t know. You just tell them what to take and they \",\"startTime\":1734048387,\"endTime\":1734048390},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"take it. \",\"startTime\":1734048390,\"endTime\":1734048393},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right, right. Well, I will say it was really one of the things that''s really \",\"startTime\":1734048396,\"endTime\":1734048401},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So anyway, that''s.\",\"startTime\":1734048397,\"endTime\":1734048398},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"gained popularity in our school is the college and the high school classes so that they can get that that credit before they go. And so that''s been really \",\"startTime\":1734048401,\"endTime\":1734048410},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Yep, Yep.\",\"startTime\":1734048406,\"endTime\":1734048407},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"helpful for, you know, the students. And then eventually hopefully we have enough \",\"startTime\":1734048410,\"endTime\":1734048414},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"classes that it can relieve some financial burden from them too. So. \",\"startTime\":1734048414,\"endTime\":1734048418},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"One of the things Matt would like to pursue is like a dual credit kind of, you know, like, let''s see how we can get most of their prereqs done so that when they go to college, they really have to do the required, you know, other stuff. \",\"startTime\":1734048418,\"endTime\":1734048429},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048419,\"endTime\":1734048420},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"So yeah. \",\"startTime\":1734048429,\"endTime\":1734048433},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, yeah, no. And you that''s come in since I''ve left high school, you \",\"startTime\":1734048434,\"endTime\":1734048438},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"know all those pieces and that''s been integrated in but anyway, so yeah, yeah, it''s cool. And a better two year, 4 year trades will tech school. And I mean \",\"startTime\":1734048438,\"endTime\":1734048445},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048440,\"endTime\":1734048442},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"the basic piece is just a foundational of of educated foundation of education. \",\"startTime\":1734048445,\"endTime\":1734048449},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So you can succeed and can get through like that ERDC data we share share with you like, you know, 50% of the kids after eight years have some certification. \",\"startTime\":1734048449,\"endTime\":1734048457},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I mean that needs to change so. \",\"startTime\":1734048457,\"endTime\":1734048460},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048460,\"endTime\":1734048462},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You know, but cool, cool. And I appreciate you saying like, yeah, middle school \",\"startTime\":1734048462,\"endTime\":1734048465},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"to high school. I''m not sure yet, but I''ll figure it out. \",\"startTime\":1734048465,\"endTime\":1734048469},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048469,\"endTime\":1734048469},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It''s awesome, It''s awesome.\",\"startTime\":1734048471,\"endTime\":1734048473},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK, so you so my thing is like it''s like flashing on me. It''s kind of bugging \",\"startTime\":1734048473,\"endTime\":1734048476},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"out. So I can''t see what the question says and I bet you I won''t be able to \",\"startTime\":1734048476,\"endTime\":1734048479},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"move on after that. \",\"startTime\":1734048479,\"endTime\":1734048482},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Well, we''ll see, we''ll see. What challenges do you face in assisting your students \",\"startTime\":1734048484,\"endTime\":1734048489},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK, OK.\",\"startTime\":1734048485,\"endTime\":1734048486},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"with post secondary goals? What challenges do you face with assisting students \",\"startTime\":1734048489,\"endTime\":1734048494},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"in their post secondary goals? And I''ll, I''ll start while you think about it. \",\"startTime\":1734048494,\"endTime\":1734048499},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, oh, I would, I would say that it''s, it''s the lack of, even though you have college and career counselors, it''s really the lack of. \",\"startTime\":1734048499,\"endTime\":1734048508},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I feel like actually.\",\"startTime\":1734048499,\"endTime\":1734048500},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, go ahead.\",\"startTime\":1734048502,\"endTime\":1734048503},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Hand holding a bunch of different well it comes from two things. I would say \",\"startTime\":1734048515,\"endTime\":1734048517},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"the systemic nature. \",\"startTime\":1734048517,\"endTime\":1734048520},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Not necessarily just resources and council, but it''s really a belief system and A and A and a systemic process that happens in the middle school that is, \",\"startTime\":1734048521,\"endTime\":1734048529},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"is ongoing and, and has multiple touch points through the middle school years on going through the high school years where students are seeing what''s possible and seeing their potential. And it''s also engaging the parents in a much younger, \",\"startTime\":1734048529,\"endTime\":1734048542},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"younger piece. \",\"startTime\":1734048542,\"endTime\":1734048546},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"To dispel some of the myths around financial assistance, like everybody looks at sticker shock. \",\"startTime\":1734048547,\"endTime\":1734048552},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And, and the bottom line, and that''s not the reality. You know when, when I''ll \",\"startTime\":1734048554,\"endTime\":1734048559},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"just use my two kids as an example, they both chose independent schools or private schools where we got an enormous amount of financial aid and they got Zippo at the state schools. We actually went to private schools at a less cost out \",\"startTime\":1734048559,\"endTime\":1734048573},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"of pocket than the state schools that were only offering loan money. And, and \",\"startTime\":1734048573,\"endTime\":1734048578},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"people don''t understand that. So the messaging early on to do that for. \",\"startTime\":1734048578,\"endTime\":1734048583},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"The fact that you can use FAFSA or the Washington State Financial Aid Grant to go to an apprenticeship school, people don''t know that either. So there''s \",\"startTime\":1734048586,\"endTime\":1734048594},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"some pieces that have to happen early on. Systemically, it doesn''t. It can''t \",\"startTime\":1734048594,\"endTime\":1734048597},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048596,\"endTime\":1734048597},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"start in 9th grade. So I would say that''s the biggest piece. It''s not. Yes, \",\"startTime\":1734048597,\"endTime\":1734048601},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"those resources are counselors inside Bing. And really it''s a systemic piece \",\"startTime\":1734048601,\"endTime\":1734048605},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"of this has to dig into the beliefs and install some of the myths at a much, much, much, much, much, much earlier grade level than high school. \",\"startTime\":1734048605,\"endTime\":1734048612},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I, I completely agree with you. I think that also we see, you know, it''s \",\"startTime\":1734048615,\"endTime\":1734048619},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"like last year was the first year I was on kind of the scholarship committee of distributing money back to students. And it was the same students that applied \",\"startTime\":1734048619,\"endTime\":1734048627},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"for kind of all the scholarships. And it''s just, it''s a small amount of kids. \",\"startTime\":1734048627,\"endTime\":1734048632},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh yeah, yes.\",\"startTime\":1734048630,\"endTime\":1734048631},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Like we were able to give them all at least one of the scholarships, but it was just like, man, like we are missing huge amounts of kids on here. I thought \",\"startTime\":1734048632,\"endTime\":1734048640},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"it was going to be like hundreds and hundreds of kids that we were kind of. \",\"startTime\":1734048640,\"endTime\":1734048644},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1734048645,\"endTime\":1734048646},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Choosing from and it wasn''t it was kind of like we were looking at the same, you know, 40 kids and they had applied for all of them and it was like, OK, So what is like the best fit for this kid? And then and so it''s great that they \",\"startTime\":1734048647,\"endTime\":1734048659},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yes, right, right. Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048657,\"endTime\":1734048661},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"all got something, but it really doesn''t feel like it''s like this competitive, you know, thing that that many kids know about. And then yeah, I I completely \",\"startTime\":1734048659,\"endTime\":1734048668},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"agree with you. I think that a lot of families in particular don''t really know \",\"startTime\":1734048668,\"endTime\":1734048672},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"what the options are to. \",\"startTime\":1734048672,\"endTime\":1734048677},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Their students and so they''re kind of learning at the same time that the kids are learning. You know, it could be junior or senior year. And it''s like, man, \",\"startTime\":1734048677,\"endTime\":1734048684},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048683,\"endTime\":1734048684},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"you like wish I had known this a few years ago so I could have started on some of this stuff. So same thing. \",\"startTime\":1734048684,\"endTime\":1734048691},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Well, and yeah, and, and I don''t know about you, but it''s, it''s, I was in the system and you''re in the system and, and I had a hard time navigating it with my kids, regardless of what they wanted to do, you know. So it''s just to start \",\"startTime\":1734048691,\"endTime\":1734048703},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Sure. Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048702,\"endTime\":1734048704},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"earlier. So you understand, just the process of it of a trade school, a tech \",\"startTime\":1734048703,\"endTime\":1734048707},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"school, of an apprenticeship program, you know, and, and a four year school. \",\"startTime\":1734048707,\"endTime\":1734048711},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It doesn''t matter. Just post secondary, just go. It''s all about some way. \",\"startTime\":1734048711,\"endTime\":1734048715},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So yeah, they have a big piece of there. All right #4 get out. I can. Yeah, \",\"startTime\":1734048716,\"endTime\":1734048721},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"yeah, no, I''m waiting for you to go to #4 so no, I can''t. \",\"startTime\":1734048721,\"endTime\":1734048725},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK, can you see #4 without me pressing it? OK, so if I hang up on you, I''m sorry, \",\"startTime\":1734048722,\"endTime\":1734048728},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"but this is what happened last time when I pressed next, so I''ll try. \",\"startTime\":1734048728,\"endTime\":1734048733},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I''m going to, I''m going to take it personally, Mallory. I''m going to take it \",\"startTime\":1734048736,\"endTime\":1734048738},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"personally, OK? \",\"startTime\":1734048738,\"endTime\":1734048740},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Did that work? Oh OK, well it''s still glitchy on my end and I''m frozen on your \",\"startTime\":1734048744,\"endTime\":1734048747},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Hey, you did it. You made it perfect. It did it did. So what do you? Yeah, that''s \",\"startTime\":1734048744,\"endTime\":1734048749},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"screen so. \",\"startTime\":1734048747,\"endTime\":1734048750},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"OK. What do you, what do you what? As long as you can hear me, we''re good. So \",\"startTime\":1734048749,\"endTime\":1734048753},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"what do you hear from students as the greatest reason they are not pursuing or thinking about enrolling in a post secondary school or program? That that \",\"startTime\":1734048753,\"endTime\":1734048763},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"they that they are not pursuing or thinking about enrolling in a post secondary program. The greatest, the biggest reason you hear for students? \",\"startTime\":1734048763,\"endTime\":1734048772},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"That they that they are thinking about it or aren''t.\",\"startTime\":1734048767,\"endTime\":1734048769},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Not pursuing or thinking about enrolling in a post secondary program.\",\"startTime\":1734048782,\"endTime\":1734048786},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I would say, you know, I work on the day-to-day, I''m working with students that have a lot of discipline issues. So I feel like when I hear that from students, \",\"startTime\":1734048788,\"endTime\":1734048798},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''m hearing it from a small number of kids at Olympia High School, but that are just sick of school, you know, like school hasn''t worked in their favor and they''re they''re just wanting to get out and get a job and, you know, just start making money and that school hasn''t really. \",\"startTime\":1734048798,\"endTime\":1734048817},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048804,\"endTime\":1734048804},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1734048806,\"endTime\":1734048807},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048816,\"endTime\":1734048817},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"For them, so, you know, for other students that are kind of middle of the road or higher achieving, that''s not really the norm here at Olympia High School. \",\"startTime\":1734048818,\"endTime\":1734048826},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048823,\"endTime\":1734048823},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"So I don''t hear it too often, but there''s definitely a population of kids that it applies to, right? \",\"startTime\":1734048826,\"endTime\":1734048834},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, and I, I appreciate you saying like school didn''t work for me. Now, why \",\"startTime\":1734048835,\"endTime\":1734048838},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"is it going to work if I go somewhere else? What''s going to be different about \",\"startTime\":1734048838,\"endTime\":1734048840},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"going somewhere else? What''s going to be different about enrolling in in a Community \",\"startTime\":1734048840,\"endTime\":1734048843},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"College or in a trade school, which I just can''t go to work and call it good, you know? \",\"startTime\":1734048843,\"endTime\":1734048849},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah. My, my hope is that we can catch some of those kids earlier, but then \",\"startTime\":1734048850,\"endTime\":1734048854},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"they''re, you know, junior, senior year. Like we, you know, we''ve got a great, \",\"startTime\":1734048854,\"endTime\":1734048858},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I would say care team or SST process where we really start talking about like. \",\"startTime\":1734048858,\"endTime\":1734048863},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK, what about the farm? Or what about this kid for New Market? Or what about \",\"startTime\":1734048863,\"endTime\":1734048867},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"this kid for, you know, and try to brainstorm these things really early on in their high school so that it''s like, OK, like maybe this is something that they can work towards and that they''d be excited about instead of just seeing like four more years of something that''s not fun and that''s not working for them. \",\"startTime\":1734048867,\"endTime\":1734048882},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048869,\"endTime\":1734048873},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm, mm-hmm, mm-hmm. \",\"startTime\":1734048882,\"endTime\":1734048885},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right, Yeah, yeah, it was four years, two years or just a year, you know, like I can''t even think about doing. I''m so tired of school. All I can think about \",\"startTime\":1734048884,\"endTime\":1734048892},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"is June and getting done the you know, as as I think back and the stuff I''ve heard from a lot of other people across the state is, is cost. It''s not about \",\"startTime\":1734048892,\"endTime\":1734048900},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"it''s not about applying. It''s not about this. It''s not about that. It''s just \",\"startTime\":1734048900,\"endTime\":1734048905},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"cost. How how, how my family going to afford this. \",\"startTime\":1734048905,\"endTime\":1734048909},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You know, and then other kids.\",\"startTime\":1734048911,\"endTime\":1734048914},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"They don''t see that as being a possible out for them. And unfortunately, I''ve \",\"startTime\":1734048916,\"endTime\":1734048921},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734048920,\"endTime\":1734048921},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"heard a number of stories and seen some like student voice interviews across our state where kids have been counseled away from doing that. Like they come \",\"startTime\":1734048921,\"endTime\":1734048931},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"in as fresh, they come in as freshmen. And, and if you ask kids, 98% of them \",\"startTime\":1734048931,\"endTime\":1734048935},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"are, are like, yes, I''m going to do something after high school. And then by \",\"startTime\":1734048935,\"endTime\":1734048940},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"the time of juniors, it''s like 60%. And you ask them why and you ask them why. \",\"startTime\":1734048940,\"endTime\":1734048945},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"MMM. Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm. Yeah. No kidding. My hope for those kids is that they''re \",\"startTime\":1734048945,\"endTime\":1734048950},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And, and they''ll flat out tell you and part of the the research that''s been done in the student voice surveys that have been done all up and down the iPad corridor and the road map community is an adult told me I was not a good match to do that, which just crushes me. \",\"startTime\":1734048949,\"endTime\":1734048963},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"like, right. Right. \",\"startTime\":1734048950,\"endTime\":1734048955},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Who, who, who are we to say that this kid can''t do Well, you know, they, they, they put the middle finger up. I don''t know if I can say that in this, but I \",\"startTime\":1734048968,\"endTime\":1734048977},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"just did. So it doesn''t matter. Like, like, you know, like, yeah, one of those \",\"startTime\":1734048977,\"endTime\":1734048982},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I can''t wait for that to be one of the things that pops up as a.\",\"startTime\":1734048979,\"endTime\":1734048983},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"things that Mike Pitbulls said, Scott Scott Friedman said, well, I, I hope the kid gives the middle finger to that adult that said they couldn''t go to school. \",\"startTime\":1734048982,\"endTime\":1734048991},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I agree with that, right. Like I hope that those kids prove that person \",\"startTime\":1734048996,\"endTime\":1734049001},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"wrong. Like you hear those great stories, right? Of Yeah, agree. \",\"startTime\":1734049001,\"endTime\":1734049005},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Who, who, but but it''s like, who, who, who are we? Who are we to put limiters? \",\"startTime\":1734049001,\"endTime\":1734049005},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It''s just pisses me off to no end. Who are we to put limiters on kids? That''s \",\"startTime\":1734049005,\"endTime\":1734049009},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"just so wrong. We should be pushing them to aspire to a notch higher, you know, \",\"startTime\":1734049009,\"endTime\":1734049012},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And because they can do it, they can do it anyway. So all right, question #5 \",\"startTime\":1734049012,\"endTime\":1734049016},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Are you ready? I, I shade out, you''re ready. \",\"startTime\":1734049016,\"endTime\":1734049020},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734049018,\"endTime\":1734049018},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I hear the noise.\",\"startTime\":1734049021,\"endTime\":1734049022},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"All right.\",\"startTime\":1734049024,\"endTime\":1734049025},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"This one''s easy, this one''s easy. It''s thank your partner and share one thing \",\"startTime\":1734049029,\"endTime\":1734049032},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"you learned from them. \",\"startTime\":1734049032,\"endTime\":1734049035},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Thanks for oh, OK.\",\"startTime\":1734049035,\"endTime\":1734049037},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Well, I thank you. I I did not think about just the systemic piece of having \",\"startTime\":1734049040,\"endTime\":1734049045},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"the need to have these conversations earlier. And, you know, we I think we just \",\"startTime\":1734049045,\"endTime\":1734049050},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So.\",\"startTime\":1734049046,\"endTime\":1734049046},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"need to do a better job of whatever that outreach looks like. You know, in terms \",\"startTime\":1734049050,\"endTime\":1734049055},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734049054,\"endTime\":1734049054},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"of listening to what parents say, like, oh, I wish, you know, this would have been something that we covered in middle school or like, yeah, that was like A1 information night a year kind of thing. And just. \",\"startTime\":1734049055,\"endTime\":1734049070},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"How could we support and, you know, opening up that invitation to, you know, that soon to be senior night, Like, hey, if you''re a sophomore or a freshman \",\"startTime\":1734049070,\"endTime\":1734049077},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"and you want to learn about this stuff before you''re a senior, like come, you know, like that, that''s not a bad thing to just have it be an invitation for all Olympia High School families. So I didn''t really think about that, but I \",\"startTime\":1734049077,\"endTime\":1734049088},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"appreciate it. \",\"startTime\":1734049088,\"endTime\":1734049092},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Good. No, thank you. And I and I appreciate you being here today. So I even \",\"startTime\":1734049096,\"endTime\":1734049099},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"though I like an individual reflection, it''s like it''s always better to talk so funny from time to time. \",\"startTime\":1734049099,\"endTime\":1734049105},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You know, I when I think about what I learned from you, I think it it reinforced and really blamed it. What''s that? Oh. \",\"startTime\":1734049108,\"endTime\":1734049116},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"These have been really cool.\",\"startTime\":1734049108,\"endTime\":1734049110},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh, sorry, like there''s a little bit of a delay. I said these have been really \",\"startTime\":1734049117,\"endTime\":1734049120},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"cool just to talk to people from different areas. \",\"startTime\":1734049120,\"endTime\":1734049123},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Isn''t it, I just, I love it. I just, I think it''s yeah, I love it. I, I do a \",\"startTime\":1734049126,\"endTime\":1734049130},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734049128,\"endTime\":1734049130},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"couple of other groups like this with some different things and, and 15 minutes. \",\"startTime\":1734049130,\"endTime\":1734049134},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It''s just, it''s awesome, you know, to be quick. But when I, when I think about \",\"startTime\":1734049134,\"endTime\":1734049137},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"what I learned from you today, I think it, I think I learned the the importance, just as you said of it re ingrained in me just that deep seated belief that it can''t, it can''t begin in 9th and 10th or 11th grade. It it''s got to be a \",\"startTime\":1734049137,\"endTime\":1734049148},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"systemic piece and hearing you talk about coming from the middle school and, and the experience. \",\"startTime\":1734049148,\"endTime\":1734049156},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"There and and and and coming up it it just anyway enforced in my mind on that that that aspect. So I appreciate that you''re still there right. OK yeah, yeah, \",\"startTime\":1734049158,\"endTime\":1734049169},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"yeah, OK. \",\"startTime\":1734049169,\"endTime\":1734049174},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I think coming from the middle school, we Yep. Can you, can you hear me? \",\"startTime\":1734049170,\"endTime\":1734049175},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK, so I was gonna say, coming from the middle school, I just really feel like what we did was try to prepare kids for high school and nothing really beyond high school. So yeah, we gotta change our mindset, you know, because once you''re \",\"startTime\":1734049180,\"endTime\":1734049192},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734049183,\"endTime\":1734049184},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1734049191,\"endTime\":1734049191},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"in high school, you''re just preparing them for after high school. So yeah, yeah. \",\"startTime\":1734049192,\"endTime\":1734049197},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Good conversation. \",\"startTime\":1734049197,\"endTime\":1734049201},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"What a yeah. What a what a perspective. When we when we''re in middle school, \",\"startTime\":1734049200,\"endTime\":1734049204},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"we prepare kids for the high school, when in reality we''re setting some foundational skills to prepare them for life. And we don''t see it that way. \",\"startTime\":1734049204,\"endTime\":1734049212},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right, right.\",\"startTime\":1734049213,\"endTime\":1734049214},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Nugget right there. Drop it Nugget. I love it. I love it so well. I know we \",\"startTime\":1734049216,\"endTime\":1734049220},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"got one more week, but if I don''t get paired up with you again, Merry Christmas and a happy holiday however it is. Choose to celebrate this time period with \",\"startTime\":1734049220,\"endTime\":1734049227},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"a couple weeks off. \",\"startTime\":1734049227,\"endTime\":1734049231},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah. Thank you. Same to you. And I enjoyed speaking with you today and \",\"startTime\":1734049227,\"endTime\":1734049231},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''m actually going to head out and go meet my mentee for dinner tonight. So \",\"startTime\":1734049231,\"endTime\":1734049235},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It''s awesome. I''m happy for you and your family to be able to get a chance to \",\"startTime\":1734049233,\"endTime\":1734049234},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"do that. \",\"startTime\":1734049234,\"endTime\":1734049236},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"lots of AWSP things today. \",\"startTime\":1734049235,\"endTime\":1734049239},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Where you get going on tomorrow, OK.\",\"startTime\":1734049251,\"endTime\":1734049254},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"We''re going to go to Ramirez, a Mexican restaurant in Tumwater. So we''re kind \",\"startTime\":1734049252,\"endTime\":1734049257},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"of meeting closer on my end. And I was happy to drive to 10. I know where she \",\"startTime\":1734049257,\"endTime\":1734049262},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"is, but yeah, she''s she''s like familiar with this area. And, you know, she picked. \",\"startTime\":1734049262,\"endTime\":1734049267},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh good.\",\"startTime\":1734049267,\"endTime\":1734049267},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Isn''t it so good? Yes, it''s that place is delicious. \",\"startTime\":1734049267,\"endTime\":1734049272},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Is it Valentino''s Downtown Olympia? I think it''s Valentino''s.\",\"startTime\":1734049272,\"endTime\":1734049275},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I got the name right, didn''t I?\",\"startTime\":1734049282,\"endTime\":1734049285},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yep, you did.\",\"startTime\":1734049284,\"endTime\":1734049285},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, it is. It was Bueno, Louis. Bueno, Louis bueno. Michi Somo will have your \",\"startTime\":1734049287,\"endTime\":1734049291},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It was awesome. Yeah, been there a couple of times. 6 So, yeah, it was great. \",\"startTime\":1734049291,\"endTime\":1734049295},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It was great. But yeah. Enjoy. Valerie and I so, so appreciate the chance to \",\"startTime\":1734049295,\"endTime\":1734049299},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"connect with you today. OK. \",\"startTime\":1734049299,\"endTime\":1734049303},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, all right. Have a good night, Scott.\",\"startTime\":1734049304,\"endTime\":1734049306}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.38687+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.38687+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 1269, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:28.288Z", "session_title": "Uncovering Student Post-Secondary Access Realities", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1323", "name": "Uncovering Student Post-Secondary Access Realities", "tags": [{"name": "HSLC"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('45df20ef-7163-4fdf-a4f7-6c27c0649052', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '135455', '"[{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yes, Brenda Thompson, Scott Friedman. What are the chances?\",\"startTime\":1733237233,\"endTime\":1733237237},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Hi, Siri. I know right? I''m driving so.\",\"startTime\":1733237236,\"endTime\":1733237240},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I love it. You are fine. Put that camera off and we''ll get it. Get it going, \",\"startTime\":1733237238,\"endTime\":1733237241},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"OK? \",\"startTime\":1733237241,\"endTime\":1733237243},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I just set it down OK.\",\"startTime\":1733237245,\"endTime\":1733237246},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh how cool. Oh my gosh, I biggest smile I''ve had all week. Well, it''s only \",\"startTime\":1733237247,\"endTime\":1733237251},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"been one day long, but you know. \",\"startTime\":1733237251,\"endTime\":1733237254},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh man, so I''m good. I I had a long day yesterday. I flew over to Olympian back \",\"startTime\":1733237259,\"endTime\":1733237264},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"How are you doing?\",\"startTime\":1733237260,\"endTime\":1733237261},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"and my flight got delayed and whatnot. So but we''re all good this morning. So \",\"startTime\":1733237264,\"endTime\":1733237268},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"all good this morning. But and yourself. Yeah, Thanksgiving was good. Thanksgiving \",\"startTime\":1733237268,\"endTime\":1733237273},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I''m doing good, doing good, just trying to get to work. Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah, \",\"startTime\":1733237272,\"endTime\":1733237276},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"was good. Awesome. \",\"startTime\":1733237273,\"endTime\":1733237278},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"yeah. You know, immediate family, mom, dad, you know, it was, it was nice just \",\"startTime\":1733237276,\"endTime\":1733237280},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"not having to go nowhere. So we hosted. \",\"startTime\":1733237280,\"endTime\":1733237284},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Love, love to hear it. Did you Good. Yeah. Love to hear, Love to hear it. So \",\"startTime\":1733237287,\"endTime\":1733237292},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"we''ll click on that next down below and let''s let''s roll, yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733237292,\"endTime\":1733237296},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"OK, there we go. I think I clicked on it.\",\"startTime\":1733237296,\"endTime\":1733237299},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So it''s asking me to how did I end up becoming an educator and then ask you for your story. And really, I, I fought it forever. \",\"startTime\":1733237302,\"endTime\":1733237309},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And I just didn''t realize that after watching my dad for he was a long time educator for 41 or 42 years. And after growing up in that environment and seeing \",\"startTime\":1733237311,\"endTime\":1733237319},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"how happy he was every day he came home and how he took care of my mom and us and never had a bad day, it seemed like I was like, I guess there is something this teaching thing. So that''s kind of how it ended up after my first year of \",\"startTime\":1733237319,\"endTime\":1733237331},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"college. I I fought it the first year and then I just dove right in. So yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733237331,\"endTime\":1733237335},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yourself.\",\"startTime\":1733237337,\"endTime\":1733237337},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1733237337,\"endTime\":1733237338},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I, I knew I wanted to be a teacher since like 2nd, 4th grade. I had the same \",\"startTime\":1733237339,\"endTime\":1733237343},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"teacher and I ever since then, I knew that''s what I wanted to do. And it took \",\"startTime\":1733237343,\"endTime\":1733237347},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"me a little bit longer being a military wife and having kids prior to, you know, right out of right before I got out of high school and stuff like that. And \",\"startTime\":1733237347,\"endTime\":1733237354},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237353,\"endTime\":1733237355},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"then, and then I just, that''s what I dove into. My husband''s like, OK, that''s \",\"startTime\":1733237354,\"endTime\":1733237357},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"what you want to do, Let''s do it again. It just, like I said, took a little \",\"startTime\":1733237357,\"endTime\":1733237361},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"bit longer with him being in Iraq three times, being a single mom those times and just trying to raise our kids. \",\"startTime\":1733237361,\"endTime\":1733237368},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237370,\"endTime\":1733237370},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Go to school and work. But then I was finally able to do that, and that''s what \",\"startTime\":1733237370,\"endTime\":1733237374},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I''ve been doing since 2000. Well, I was a pair of two for over 19 years. So \",\"startTime\":1733237374,\"endTime\":1733237379},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah. No, I knew that. I knew that.\",\"startTime\":1733237377,\"endTime\":1733237379},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"and then in 2014, somebody gave me an opportunity in Tacoma. So I left my husband \",\"startTime\":1733237379,\"endTime\":1733237383},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"in Indiana and came back home. \",\"startTime\":1733237383,\"endTime\":1733237388},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Wow. What an awesome, awesome story. Awesome story. He came back from Indiana \",\"startTime\":1733237390,\"endTime\":1733237393},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I''ve been doing it ever since. Yeah, yeah, yeah. He came back in 2015, he retired \",\"startTime\":1733237390,\"endTime\":1733237394},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"though, right? Yeah. Yeah, I know, I know. \",\"startTime\":1733237393,\"endTime\":1733237396},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"and now he''s in the school system. \",\"startTime\":1733237394,\"endTime\":1733237398},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Oh, awesome. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237400,\"endTime\":1733237403},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"But he he does check, he doesn''t do, he says I wouldn''t be able to do what you do, Brenda, not being in the military and then. \",\"startTime\":1733237403,\"endTime\":1733237409},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"No, Yeah, yeah. So.\",\"startTime\":1733237409,\"endTime\":1733237412},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I was like, OK, oh.\",\"startTime\":1733237413,\"endTime\":1733237414},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Well, let''s go to the. Go to the next one.\",\"startTime\":1733237414,\"endTime\":1733237417},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Right, I think I clicked it. Did I click it OK?\",\"startTime\":1733237420,\"endTime\":1733237424},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, you did. You did. Yeah, Yeah. In the I''ll, I''ll read the question for \",\"startTime\":1733237422,\"endTime\":1733237425},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"you and we''ll take turns sharing this is what do you hope to learn or achieve through these sessions? \",\"startTime\":1733237425,\"endTime\":1733237431},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Go ahead.\",\"startTime\":1733237435,\"endTime\":1733237435},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, no, go ahead. I was going to say you can. You can go first if you want. \",\"startTime\":1733237436,\"endTime\":1733237439},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"OK. I am just hoping to connect with other people and just different strategies \",\"startTime\":1733237438,\"endTime\":1733237442},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, Yeah. You know, And mine, mine''s probably similar, even though it''s I \",\"startTime\":1733237439,\"endTime\":1733237443},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"that I can use for different things. And then how did you know like some organization \",\"startTime\":1733237442,\"endTime\":1733237446},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I do it from afar. And my hope is that this platform provides leaders like yourself \",\"startTime\":1733237443,\"endTime\":1733237447},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"systems for discipline and just things like that. So just to connect with people \",\"startTime\":1733237446,\"endTime\":1733237451},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"the ability to connect with colleagues that have similar challenges, similar problems of practice, similar. \",\"startTime\":1733237447,\"endTime\":1733237454},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"and build my capacity. \",\"startTime\":1733237451,\"endTime\":1733237455},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Similar barriers and celebrations and, and that it reduces isolation so you feel like there''s somebody some way you can turn to every Tuesday morning at 6:45 or Thursday at 4:00. And, and that consistency of conversation, I think \",\"startTime\":1733237471,\"endTime\":1733237486},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"is something that my hope is that it provides a reduction of maybe a little bit of anxiety or stress knowing that you can just hop on and, and just talk and, and will they answer the. \",\"startTime\":1733237486,\"endTime\":1733237501},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Questions or not is OK, you know, but but just just just talk with somebody and ''cause it can be isolating as as as you know. So anyway, that''s my hope. \",\"startTime\":1733237501,\"endTime\":1733237512},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1733237504,\"endTime\":1733237504},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"All right, head to the next one here. I should wait for a good. I should probably \",\"startTime\":1733237515,\"endTime\":1733237517},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"wait till you get to a stop light, huh? \",\"startTime\":1733237517,\"endTime\":1733237520},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"OK, well actually they''re not even usually I get stop lights all the time.\",\"startTime\":1733237520,\"endTime\":1733237525},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"See you leave. See you leave. You leave. 5 minutes sooner. You get there 15 \",\"startTime\":1733237526,\"endTime\":1733237528},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"minutes earlier. You don''t have any stop lights. Oh, you did. Oh, Oh well, even \",\"startTime\":1733237528,\"endTime\":1733237530},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"better. \",\"startTime\":1733237530,\"endTime\":1733237533},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Actually, I love later today.\",\"startTime\":1733237532,\"endTime\":1733237533},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I''m usually I''m usually at work between 6:30 and 6:45 but I wanted to make sure my husband was that before I left. Does anyone have to be late for his doctor''s \",\"startTime\":1733237535,\"endTime\":1733237542},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"OK, OK.\",\"startTime\":1733237539,\"endTime\":1733237540},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"appointment? \",\"startTime\":1733237542,\"endTime\":1733237545},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, gotcha. Perfect. Well, here''s the here''s the scenario that we''re asked to \",\"startTime\":1733237546,\"endTime\":1733237550},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"ask to kind of think about. You''ve been asked to ensure teachers across the \",\"startTime\":1733237550,\"endTime\":1733237554},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"district become good at one thing you''re great at what is that thing and how much you structure that learning experience so it can be impactful and and spreads to others. \",\"startTime\":1733237554,\"endTime\":1733237566},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So I will, yeah, go ahead, go ahead. 01 thing, one thing that you''re great at, \",\"startTime\":1733237569,\"endTime\":1733237576},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Panti Showay.\",\"startTime\":1733237569,\"endTime\":1733237570},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"No, I was just one thing who''s great at I I wanted just to get the question clarified. OK, OK, you can go ahead and answer first. I just, I didn''t, I wasn''t \",\"startTime\":1733237572,\"endTime\":1733237579},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I would say, I would say the ability to connect with all kids. \",\"startTime\":1733237576,\"endTime\":1733237583},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"sure if it was their grade at or. \",\"startTime\":1733237579,\"endTime\":1733237582},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That would, for whatever reason, that was something that I that I had been told through my career. And as I looked back on it, I''m able to kind of reflect and \",\"startTime\":1733237592,\"endTime\":1733237599},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"say, yeah, I was pretty good at at creating relationships and connections and making kids feel welcome in a classroom. \",\"startTime\":1733237599,\"endTime\":1733237605},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Umm and I tried to do that same thing with staff as well in terms of structuring that learning experience for, for people, you know, I''m thinking about modeling it on a daily basis with, with others tips and tricks that way skills here. \",\"startTime\":1733237607,\"endTime\":1733237623},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"The the best book I''ve ever read was Harry Wong, the first days of school about relationships with kids and, and so I would embed some of those pieces, I guess. \",\"startTime\":1733237623,\"endTime\":1733237634},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And working with others.\",\"startTime\":1733237634,\"endTime\":1733237635},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Yeah, that''s kind of what I was going to say just because I always would have said can I come back? Can I come back? Even though I was, I would think it''d \",\"startTime\":1733237638,\"endTime\":1733237645},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"be like firm, but kind of you want to, if you want to describe that, just being very firm with with students, but also kind and loving because you confess the kid out. But then at the very end of the day, the last sentence you say is I \",\"startTime\":1733237645,\"endTime\":1733237656},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237650,\"endTime\":1733237650},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237650,\"endTime\":1733237651},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"love you. \",\"startTime\":1733237656,\"endTime\":1733237660},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I love you, you''re important. You just got to get rid of those behaviors, you \",\"startTime\":1733237661,\"endTime\":1733237665},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237662,\"endTime\":1733237663},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"know, so but it''s the same thing just and I, I think I create the same thing with staff is that I''m firm, but I care about you. I''ll learn about you. I''ll \",\"startTime\":1733237665,\"endTime\":1733237673},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237666,\"endTime\":1733237669},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"do you know, I''ll send you cards. I will do the happy card. I want you to feel \",\"startTime\":1733237673,\"endTime\":1733237677},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"appreciated just like kids. And again, that structure, like you were saying, \",\"startTime\":1733237677,\"endTime\":1733237681},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"is just modeling that, just being vulnerable and modeling that and showing people that it happens that. \",\"startTime\":1733237681,\"endTime\":1733237689},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"That just being that firm and kind, but being firm, you have to be firm. You \",\"startTime\":1733237692,\"endTime\":1733237694},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"can''t just be Willy nilly. \",\"startTime\":1733237694,\"endTime\":1733237696},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Umm, with kids or adults, you know, and just in that openness and honesty.\",\"startTime\":1733237698,\"endTime\":1733237705},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, exactly. And it, it reminds me of the quote by Brené Brown that you''ve \",\"startTime\":1733237705,\"endTime\":1733237709},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"probably heard Jack use a million times and myself as clear, as kind. And, and \",\"startTime\":1733237709,\"endTime\":1733237713},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"when you say firm, I conjure up that notion of, of being clear with the expectations \",\"startTime\":1733237713,\"endTime\":1733237717},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"and guidelines and, and reinforcing those for students and for students and adults, because that''s the kind thing to do when we can remove confusion about how I have to act and behave and be with others. \",\"startTime\":1733237717,\"endTime\":1733237729},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237721,\"endTime\":1733237721},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237728,\"endTime\":1733237728},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It''s but it''s tough to do for a lot of people.\",\"startTime\":1733237731,\"endTime\":1733237733},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Yeah, for some people, but yeah, it''s that. It''s just that they want to be. \",\"startTime\":1733237734,\"endTime\":1733237738},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Thank you.\",\"startTime\":1733237737,\"endTime\":1733237738},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I''m sorry. We''re not friends here. I mean, we are, but we aren''t, you know, \",\"startTime\":1733237738,\"endTime\":1733237742},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"it''s just like your kids. I''m not your friend. I love you. I''m not your friend. \",\"startTime\":1733237742,\"endTime\":1733237746},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1733237742,\"endTime\":1733237742},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"And we don''t have to get along, but we do have to show respect to each other. \",\"startTime\":1733237746,\"endTime\":1733237749},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237747,\"endTime\":1733237749},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"So. Or be respectful. Be respectful. So. \",\"startTime\":1733237749,\"endTime\":1733237753},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I love it. Love it. Perfect, perfect. Let''s slide over to the next one here. \",\"startTime\":1733237752,\"endTime\":1733237758},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, spend 3 open-ended minutes with Brenda. Well, look at that. Isn''t that nice? \",\"startTime\":1733237758,\"endTime\":1733237764},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Alright, try not to lose you.\",\"startTime\":1733237761,\"endTime\":1733237762},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Isn''t that nice? So remind me, what Rd. are you going down right now? Like this \",\"startTime\":1733237764,\"endTime\":1733237770},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"is our open-ended time? Yeah. Gotcha. Oh, gotcha. OK, OK. \",\"startTime\":1733237770,\"endTime\":1733237776},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I right now I''m going down 176. I actually went down the long way because there''s \",\"startTime\":1733237782,\"endTime\":1733237786},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"like four or five roads that I could go down to get to my my job. I was going \",\"startTime\":1733237786,\"endTime\":1733237791},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"all the way down towards Pacific so that I didn''t get cut off with the, the sometimes when I enter, my service is not really good around here. So, so I \",\"startTime\":1733237791,\"endTime\":1733237800},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"was trying to go down a road that I knew I would have service. \",\"startTime\":1733237800,\"endTime\":1733237804},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Well, good, good thinking as you as.\",\"startTime\":1733237803,\"endTime\":1733237807},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"But.\",\"startTime\":1733237806,\"endTime\":1733237807},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"As you call out the road names, I''m, I''m remembering my days at at PLU and all around Parkland and Spanaway and all that stuff. And I''m like, Oh yeah, I think \",\"startTime\":1733237810,\"endTime\":1733237816},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"But yeah, no, I just passed district office, so I''m going to go down B Street and get to my building, so. \",\"startTime\":1733237810,\"endTime\":1733237816},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I ran down that road a few times during wrestling season. I know I''ve gone down \",\"startTime\":1733237816,\"endTime\":1733237819},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"that road. So yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733237819,\"endTime\":1733237822},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Awesome.\",\"startTime\":1733237828,\"endTime\":1733237828},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Awesome. Well, we can go to the next there. And, and and I, I kid you not, Brenda, \",\"startTime\":1733237831,\"endTime\":1733237836},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"when when, when I saw when I saw the match with Brenda show up, I was like Brenda, Brenda, Brenda, Brenda. Oh, my gosh, it''s Brenda Thompson. I''m so happy. It''s \",\"startTime\":1733237836,\"endTime\":1733237848},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"just put a big smile on my face this morning. So I appreciate you. Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733237848,\"endTime\":1733237854},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Well, you guys always, you guys always do that for me and I appreciate you guys. \",\"startTime\":1733237851,\"endTime\":1733237855},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"So I was like going to the meetings or just talking to you guys or just listening to you guys. Sometimes. Sometimes I don''t talk and I try to give other people \",\"startTime\":1733237855,\"endTime\":1733237863},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237863,\"endTime\":1733237863},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"space, but some people like it''s quite OK. Let me go ahead and say something. \",\"startTime\":1733237863,\"endTime\":1733237867},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, that''s perfect, It''s perfect. And I don''t know if we''ll see each other \",\"startTime\":1733237868,\"endTime\":1733237872},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"''cause we may not get connected again through this, but if, if or if we''re there. \",\"startTime\":1733237872,\"endTime\":1733237876},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"But happy holidays to you and your family. Yeah, hopefully get get the kids \",\"startTime\":1733237876,\"endTime\":1733237880},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"all around again and, and get some smiles and some laughter. I know you''ll laugh, \",\"startTime\":1733237880,\"endTime\":1733237884},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"YouTube.\",\"startTime\":1733237882,\"endTime\":1733237882},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"there''s no question about that. So. \",\"startTime\":1733237884,\"endTime\":1733237888},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"That''s all we do, tell stories. Horror stories.\",\"startTime\":1733237890,\"endTime\":1733237892},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That''s a that''s a given. Oh, yeah. Well, I got a story for you. Let me let me \",\"startTime\":1733237893,\"endTime\":1733237896},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"one up that one, you know, so, you know, you know how that goes. So. \",\"startTime\":1733237896,\"endTime\":1733237899},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"But it''s like we we compare education and military stories.\",\"startTime\":1733237900,\"endTime\":1733237903},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733237904,\"endTime\":1733237905},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"Because my dad was military, too. So my husband and my dad have those stories. \",\"startTime\":1733237906,\"endTime\":1733237910},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, was he OK? Oh wow. Yeah, cool.\",\"startTime\":1733237909,\"endTime\":1733237913},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"And then my mom works in Spanaway Lake High School as their program nurse and one of the special Ed programs. So she has stories. But you know, just, yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733237910,\"endTime\":1733237918},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"So it''s always story, story, stories. \",\"startTime\":1733237918,\"endTime\":1733237922},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Always, always. Well, I don''t know about you, but I guarantee you this is the \",\"startTime\":1733237924,\"endTime\":1733237928},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"best 15 minutes of my day. So thank you. All right. OK. OK. Make it a great \",\"startTime\":1733237928,\"endTime\":1733237931},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"I appreciate it. I mine too right now. We''ll have to see what I get with kiddos. \",\"startTime\":1733237930,\"endTime\":1733237934},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"day, Brenda. Thanks. Bye. \",\"startTime\":1733237931,\"endTime\":1733237935},{\"speaker\":\"11346\",\"text\":\"YouTube Bye bye sweetie.\",\"startTime\":1733237938,\"endTime\":1733237939}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.405415+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.405415+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 718, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:28.190Z", "session_title": "#learning_to_human", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "33", "name": "#learning_to_human", "tags": [{"name": "Dream Camp"}, {"name": "Inclusion"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('c6be590f-15e5-4f9c-8601-daf0f0333e7c', '903382e8-a889-4f58-85bc-6ec0178aa685', '134647', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"I''m good. How are you?\",\"startTime\":1732054765,\"endTime\":1732054767},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Hey, how are you?\",\"startTime\":1732054766,\"endTime\":1732054767},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Good. I''m supposed to share a fun fact about myself. I grew up in New York City \",\"startTime\":1732054768,\"endTime\":1732054774},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"and my wife grew up in a town of 500 in rural Eastern Oregon. \",\"startTime\":1732054774,\"endTime\":1732054781},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1732054781,\"endTime\":1732054782},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"I guess fun fact for me is I used to own a custom sugar cookie business. Yeah, \",\"startTime\":1732054783,\"endTime\":1732054788},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"What makes you an effective leader? That''s a leader. Well, that''s pretty cool. \",\"startTime\":1732054787,\"endTime\":1732054791},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"that''s pretty cool. \",\"startTime\":1732054788,\"endTime\":1732054793},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"What caused you to pivot to education? \",\"startTime\":1732054791,\"endTime\":1732054795},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Well, I did it while I was in education. It was at the same time and I decided \",\"startTime\":1732054800,\"endTime\":1732054804},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"to end that because time. \",\"startTime\":1732054804,\"endTime\":1732054807},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732054808,\"endTime\":1732054808},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"All right, what makes you an effective leader?\",\"startTime\":1732054811,\"endTime\":1732054814},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Umm.\",\"startTime\":1732054813,\"endTime\":1732054813},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"I''ve been told one of the reasons is I''m present and I''m willing to jump in and do anything and I lead by example. How about you? \",\"startTime\":1732054817,\"endTime\":1732054827},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Kind of similarly, I''ve been told that I am really present in buildings. I''m \",\"startTime\":1732054829,\"endTime\":1732054834},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"not somebody that''s usually like in my office a lot. I like to be in classrooms \",\"startTime\":1732054834,\"endTime\":1732054838},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"and out at recess. So I think just being around and listening to people would \",\"startTime\":1732054838,\"endTime\":1732054843},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"be a strength. \",\"startTime\":1732054843,\"endTime\":1732054847},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"What''s the next? Yeah, my, my supervisors like your office. Looks like you barely \",\"startTime\":1732054847,\"endTime\":1732054850},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"moved in. I said. I have ''cause I don''t like spending time here. My my office \",\"startTime\":1732054850,\"endTime\":1732054853},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"is the school. And she goes, that''s perfect. \",\"startTime\":1732054853,\"endTime\":1732054857},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732054858,\"endTime\":1732054859},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Next What''s your next goal in your leadership journey?\",\"startTime\":1732054865,\"endTime\":1732054868},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"I would say that mine is. This is my fourth year in administration and 4th year \",\"startTime\":1732054869,\"endTime\":1732054875},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"as an API. Took a year off last year to go in the classroom and finish my dissertation \",\"startTime\":1732054875,\"endTime\":1732054880},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"and then I decided to go back into the AP role this year. But I would like to \",\"startTime\":1732054880,\"endTime\":1732054886},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"move into principle eventually. I just have two young children so I''m not. \",\"startTime\":1732054886,\"endTime\":1732054892},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"5:00 and 7:00.\",\"startTime\":1732054893,\"endTime\":1732054894},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah. How old are your kids? Nice. Yeah. We have an 11 year old who just started \",\"startTime\":1732054895,\"endTime\":1732054899},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"middle school, so I understand that part. Oh, yeah. You know, it''s a good question \",\"startTime\":1732054899,\"endTime\":1732054904},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"about my next goal and my leadership journey because I the previous 10 years I was a principal at self-contained behavior schools. \",\"startTime\":1732054904,\"endTime\":1732054913},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732054904,\"endTime\":1732054905},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"The last seven in my current district and so.\",\"startTime\":1732054916,\"endTime\":1732054919},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"I''m enjoying the transition to a comprehensive school, but there''s moments where \",\"startTime\":1732054921,\"endTime\":1732054925},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"I''m like, you know, I think I could do this for maybe five years and then I may just leave education just because some days that the trends don''t seem as as wanting to do it for a while. But we''ve got folks at my district who think \",\"startTime\":1732054925,\"endTime\":1732054937},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"what I''m doing is, is pretty solid. And so I think I could grow in the district, \",\"startTime\":1732054937,\"endTime\":1732054941},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Absolutely.\",\"startTime\":1732054940,\"endTime\":1732054941},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"but I don''t think at this point I would want to leave a building, go to central office to do something like that. \",\"startTime\":1732054941,\"endTime\":1732054949},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Umm, to me the kid action is where it is. It''s more fun than the adult. Actually, \",\"startTime\":1732054950,\"endTime\":1732054954},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"the adults cause me way more stress than than than the kids. \",\"startTime\":1732054954,\"endTime\":1732054957},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"OK. Strength of our schools culture. I would say that we have very strong staff \",\"startTime\":1732054963,\"endTime\":1732054968},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"to staff relationships. \",\"startTime\":1732054968,\"endTime\":1732054972},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732054974,\"endTime\":1732054974},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"It''s a community that really values community because it''s a small neighborhood school, so everyone kind of knows each other and their families and staff have been there for a really long time, so they know the families. There''s a really \",\"startTime\":1732054975,\"endTime\":1732054986},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"strong sense of community, especially among teachers and then like teachers to families. \",\"startTime\":1732054986,\"endTime\":1732054994},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732054993,\"endTime\":1732054994},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah, Yeah, we have a, we have a similar feeling. We''ve got, I''ve got two teachers \",\"startTime\":1732054996,\"endTime\":1732055001},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"who''ve been teaching in our building for 3132 years and teaching kindergarten the whole time. And like they kind of are like Mary Poppins personified. And \",\"startTime\":1732055001,\"endTime\":1732055010},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"we got some folks that are like kind of 2829, have a couple more years and then and then we''ve got other folks that are kind of new. But everyone is really \",\"startTime\":1732055010,\"endTime\":1732055019},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"proud that we work, that they work at our school. \",\"startTime\":1732055019,\"endTime\":1732055023},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"You know that we work with our community and we''re champions and advocates for for that. So I think there''s a lot of. \",\"startTime\":1732055024,\"endTime\":1732055029},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Lot of lot of love strengthen that identity. It doesn''t always translate into \",\"startTime\":1732055030,\"endTime\":1732055034},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"then like putting in the effort for that identity ''cause we have a lot of folks who, you know, when at the moment the, the clock hits the end of contract time, they''re walking out the door and, and then they''re like, so you guys fix everything and we''ll be back tomorrow. It''s like, well, it doesn''t quite always work that \",\"startTime\":1732055034,\"endTime\":1732055051},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055048,\"endTime\":1732055048},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"way. So one of one of my goals with RAP is, is how do we keep shifting that \",\"startTime\":1732055051,\"endTime\":1732055056},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"to make it to get. \",\"startTime\":1732055056,\"endTime\":1732055060},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"More ownership. And it''s hard because the previous principal just kind of was \",\"startTime\":1732055061,\"endTime\":1732055065},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"fairly checked out and let people kind of do whatever they want. So kind of \",\"startTime\":1732055065,\"endTime\":1732055070},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"getting, getting back in trenches going to take a little bit of time. So let''s \",\"startTime\":1732055070,\"endTime\":1732055074},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"see where it goes. Yeah, sure. Yeah. There''ve been a couple days and, you know, \",\"startTime\":1732055074,\"endTime\":1732055078},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah, OK. Yeah, I I would say yeah, we''re we''re pretty similar in that like \",\"startTime\":1732055074,\"endTime\":1732055078},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"I''m, I''m still building, you know, relationships with, you know, everyone in the school. But there''s been moments where I kind of wanted to say, so you say \",\"startTime\":1732055078,\"endTime\":1732055087},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"idea of here you handle it, I''m clocked out type of thing, which I mean I get for. \",\"startTime\":1732055078,\"endTime\":1732055086},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"you''re all about kids. \",\"startTime\":1732055087,\"endTime\":1732055091},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"CBA and personal like mental health, but I would you know, love to see a little bit more. \",\"startTime\":1732055088,\"endTime\":1732055094},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Of that investment.\",\"startTime\":1732055096,\"endTime\":1732055098},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"You say you''re all about our kids, but I don''t see it in your actions and help. \",\"startTime\":1732055110,\"endTime\":1732055113},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Can you help me understand the disconnect, but I don''t think that will help the relationship building and the work quite yet to say that, but it''s I think it a lot so. \",\"startTime\":1732055113,\"endTime\":1732055123},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, absolutely. OK.\",\"startTime\":1732055123,\"endTime\":1732055126},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"OK. Feel like we kind of already transitioned to this one a little bit, but \",\"startTime\":1732055130,\"endTime\":1732055137},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055134,\"endTime\":1732055137},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"I do also think that we have a pretty general mistrust among staff towards admin. \",\"startTime\":1732055137,\"endTime\":1732055143},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"The the kind of like impression the last couple of years has been that they just stay in their office. So trying to break that narrative. I''ve gotten good \",\"startTime\":1732055144,\"endTime\":1732055153},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055152,\"endTime\":1732055153},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"feedback on it so far, so that''s good. \",\"startTime\":1732055153,\"endTime\":1732055158},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"But I think in general, like the relationship between staff and admin, and then we''re still working really hard on student to student relationships too. I think \",\"startTime\":1732055160,\"endTime\":1732055170},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"conflict resolution is not always a strength for us. \",\"startTime\":1732055170,\"endTime\":1732055175},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055170,\"endTime\":1732055170},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"No, no, I, I I see similar stuff.\",\"startTime\":1732055175,\"endTime\":1732055177},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"You know, in our building as you know, the work in, in regards to, you know, kind of where we''re going. It was interesting. I had a thought it had vanished \",\"startTime\":1732055180,\"endTime\":1732055188},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"and it''ll come back in a minute. But you know, this is, is one of the things \",\"startTime\":1732055188,\"endTime\":1732055192},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"that I walked into. \",\"startTime\":1732055192,\"endTime\":1732055196},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Which kind of speaks to my strengths is the person before me was in their office a lot. And so we had a couple first grade teachers who told me like the second \",\"startTime\":1732055199,\"endTime\":1732055208},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"week, I''ve seen you more in my classroom already than I saw the entire principle the previous year. And so to me, that was a comment that we''re doing the right \",\"startTime\":1732055208,\"endTime\":1732055216},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"thing. And you know, when we had some issues in fifth grade at like lunch and \",\"startTime\":1732055216,\"endTime\":1732055220},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055216,\"endTime\":1732055217},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"recess, you know, my AP and I were, you know, we''re like, OK, so we will be at every recess and every lunch is being visible and just being visible. \",\"startTime\":1732055220,\"endTime\":1732055228},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Coming up to us, helping us, you know, asking us to help solve the problem. \",\"startTime\":1732055228,\"endTime\":1732055232},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"So it''s like that visibility piece is so key. And I think, you know, that''s \",\"startTime\":1732055232,\"endTime\":1732055236},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"how we change that culture is by having our teachers see us solving the problems \",\"startTime\":1732055236,\"endTime\":1732055240},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"that we''re communicating with them about the problems that we''re solving and bringing them into the problem solving process so that they have more tools and capacity. And really trying to be like, I will cover your classroom while \",\"startTime\":1732055240,\"endTime\":1732055251},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"you step out and have that conversation with the student rather than me have that conversation with the student be that''s going to. \",\"startTime\":1732055251,\"endTime\":1732055258},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"And it''s going to keep their power. But some of our teachers don''t want the \",\"startTime\":1732055258,\"endTime\":1732055263},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"power. They want us just to solve it and the kids to listen to them. And it \",\"startTime\":1732055263,\"endTime\":1732055267},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"doesn''t really work these days like that. So. Right. Yeah. Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1732055267,\"endTime\":1732055271},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah, more, more the compliance piece, right. Just just get him to do it. Whatever, \",\"startTime\":1732055268,\"endTime\":1732055271},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1732055271,\"endTime\":1732055274},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"Well, thank you.\",\"startTime\":1732055280,\"endTime\":1732055280},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055282,\"endTime\":1732055283},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"I, well, this kind of doesn''t really count. This was a great conversation too, \",\"startTime\":1732055284,\"endTime\":1732055287},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"but I really enjoyed our conversation around discipline earlier today and like the resources you shared. So like, that''s the first thing that popped into my \",\"startTime\":1732055287,\"endTime\":1732055292},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"mind. \",\"startTime\":1732055292,\"endTime\":1732055295},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"Oh, awesome. Cool. Well, I appreciate our chat both earlier and now. What I \",\"startTime\":1732055296,\"endTime\":1732055300},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"think is always good about these connections is that doesn''t matter what part of the state that we''re in, some of the challenges we''re dealing with are identical. \",\"startTime\":1732055300,\"endTime\":1732055309},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"And you know, so it doesn''t, it doesn''t matter if we''re in Vancouver or Seattle, Spokane or anywhere in between, which helped remind me last week since I''ve had a couple teachers taking some like kind of personal digs. \",\"startTime\":1732055309,\"endTime\":1732055322},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"And I remind I had to like with the conversation with my AP kind of pulled me out of they''re angry at the principal position. They''re not angry at me personally. \",\"startTime\":1732055323,\"endTime\":1732055332},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"And so that that part is helpful. And I think these conversations and the connections \",\"startTime\":1732055332,\"endTime\":1732055336},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"really help in that. Like it''s a, you know, the anger is not at us personal. \",\"startTime\":1732055336,\"endTime\":1732055340},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"It just feels personal because we have so much investment in what we''re doing. \",\"startTime\":1732055340,\"endTime\":1732055345},{\"speaker\":\"11339\",\"text\":\"And so it''s, you know, kind of that professional personal balance of kind of investing, but not to the point where we''re taking the feedback personally. \",\"startTime\":1732055345,\"endTime\":1732055353},{\"speaker\":\"11321\",\"text\":\"I love that. That''s good. That''s a nice little nugget.\",\"startTime\":1732055356,\"endTime\":1732055358}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.45409+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.45409+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 605, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:40.374Z", "session_title": "School Leadership: Describing the Work(BEL LSL)", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1416", "name": "School Leadership: Describing the Work(BEL LSL)", "tags": [{"name": "BEL"}, {"name": "LSL"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('87fa442c-5a23-4806-ba99-6fba0e12533c', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '86134', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:40:27.104347+00', '2025-05-06 19:40:27.104347+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 183, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:40:27.041Z", "session_title": "Preparing for Committee Leads Meeting - Action Plan", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "336", "name": "Preparing for Committee Leads Meeting - Action Plan", "tags": [{"name": "Pathfinder"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('fc7f9032-8cbf-4edf-8eab-73d86138bced', '72c8622a-73ad-405b-9f71-d437a1193d3d', '74392', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:40:26.985288+00', '2025-05-06 19:40:26.985288+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 694, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:40:26.927Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('fcf4e9d6-09cc-4a06-b742-bc22ea99d0b3', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '78021', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:40:27.118937+00', '2025-05-06 19:40:27.118937+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 429, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:40:26.907Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('37e69fdd-9e3c-4e32-b5cc-8544b1960af6', 'f75f7f16-84b9-41ce-b842-2a77a9dd70b8', '136250', '"[{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"This prompter is about what are the real and misplaced fears that educators might have when using AI tools in education. \",\"startTime\":1736971759,\"endTime\":1736971765},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"The real fears are, I think around the world atrophy that like if you don''t use it, you lose it. And so they start to lean on these tools to do parts of \",\"startTime\":1736971767,\"endTime\":1736971775},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"our life for us. Will we still be able to? What will we lose? \",\"startTime\":1736971775,\"endTime\":1736971780},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"A self driving car is a good that kind of physical analogy of this in that like if a kid never learns how to drive, a kid couldn''t drive. Like the fact that \",\"startTime\":1736971783,\"endTime\":1736971791},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"us adults have been driving for 10/20/30 years. \",\"startTime\":1736971791,\"endTime\":1736971796},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Means like for example we can drive in the snow or when the conditions are bad. \",\"startTime\":1736971798,\"endTime\":1736971801},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"So when needed to drive, we can drive where if you were never, never needed to drive, you would never become a competent driver. I''m sure there are other \",\"startTime\":1736971804,\"endTime\":1736971813},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"examples of that in the rest of the things that we do like writing, choosing words, calculating. So. So that''s a real fear. \",\"startTime\":1736971813,\"endTime\":1736971822},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"I think the misplaced fear is that we''ll end up somewhere worse because of that, because. \",\"startTime\":1736971829,\"endTime\":1736971834},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"From my perspective, we''ve been.\",\"startTime\":1736971836,\"endTime\":1736971839},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"We''ve been doing things differently for our entire like, history of the people. \",\"startTime\":1736971843,\"endTime\":1736971848},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Is the story I like to tell about when like that the Donner party had to eat each other when walking over Donner Pass and now I can drive up and over twice a week I during snowstorms, etcetera, because we''ve invented the snow plow and we''ve invented the automobile and we''ve paved roads. Like there are things that \",\"startTime\":1736971851,\"endTime\":1736971870},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"I don''t need to know how to do, I don''t get to know how to do. \",\"startTime\":1736971870,\"endTime\":1736971875},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"But it''s kind of made life bigger and better.\",\"startTime\":1736971880,\"endTime\":1736971884},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"So when we talk about bias in AI models.\",\"startTime\":1736971921,\"endTime\":1736971925},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"We get to explore bias against the status quo, like is it less biased or more biased in our current systems? And, and it''s so good that we''re aware of this. \",\"startTime\":1736971927,\"endTime\":1736971939},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"So for example, we know that AI is trained on existing writing things that have already been written down or pictures that have already been posted. \",\"startTime\":1736971939,\"endTime\":1736971950},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"So it''s like our our lives until this point become like bait in and that we have historically had bias. So and that the people who''ve had more voice, for \",\"startTime\":1736971955,\"endTime\":1736971965},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"example, are the are people who are in power. They say history was written by \",\"startTime\":1736971965,\"endTime\":1736971969},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"the winners. And so the like the intelligence is trained in our our culture, \",\"startTime\":1736971969,\"endTime\":1736971974},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"but our written culture, as we go into video and image, it becomes into the culture of the. \",\"startTime\":1736971974,\"endTime\":1736971983},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Cruise groups of people who''ve been able to speak in that language, in the language of video and the language of of imagery. So it''s not everybody. \",\"startTime\":1736971987,\"endTime\":1736971992},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"We''re not, it''s not it''s really not everybody''s voice or everybody''s perspective. \",\"startTime\":1736971994,\"endTime\":1736971998},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Umm, but it''s measurable and correctable at the system level instead of the individual level. So for that reason, it''s maybe probably better than the status \",\"startTime\":1736971998,\"endTime\":1736972007},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"quo. And I guess that''s a through line in both of both of these cards for me \",\"startTime\":1736972007,\"endTime\":1736972012},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"so far is that it seems of course, this is true, but it''s better. But but with \",\"startTime\":1736972012,\"endTime\":1736972016},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"it is better than without. So let''s keep going. \",\"startTime\":1736972016,\"endTime\":1736972021},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"There are large organizations working on bias correcting and.\",\"startTime\":1736972027,\"endTime\":1736972031},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"And getting it right is properly incentivized. So. So I''m faithful that we as \",\"startTime\":1736972033,\"endTime\":1736972036},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"humanity will get that part right. \",\"startTime\":1736972036,\"endTime\":1736972040},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"In the offering of opportunity, there''s this like if you take the idea of AI was gonna decide who gets a loan and who does not. And it looks like who has \",\"startTime\":1736972043,\"endTime\":1736972051},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"historically given a loan, who historically is not. And we''re getting different \",\"startTime\":1736972051,\"endTime\":1736972055},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"opportunities to different people based on based on this bias. \",\"startTime\":1736972055,\"endTime\":1736972059},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"It''s a fun question. So it''s flipping now instead of a learner or a user, I''m \",\"startTime\":1736972087,\"endTime\":1736972091},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"I''m engaged as a teacher. So if I''m demonstrating the impact of artificial intelligence \",\"startTime\":1736972091,\"endTime\":1736972096},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"and there''s bias and I''m showing that to learners and it''s their first time encountering these systems, the work would be to acknowledge it. Make sure that \",\"startTime\":1736972096,\"endTime\":1736972104},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"for generations we don''t forget to check our bias, especially at the system level. So acknowledge it, teach it, and trust. \",\"startTime\":1736972104,\"endTime\":1736972113},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"That over generations will get better and better.\",\"startTime\":1736972113,\"endTime\":1736972115}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:27.913934+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:27.913934+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 334, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:27.845Z", "session_title": "Navigating AI Responsibly", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1320", "name": "Navigating AI Responsibly", "tags": [{"name": "AI in Education"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('fe48ea0d-b969-4e68-a404-cbdafd94a813', '4c3a7dc1-10fb-45d6-a20e-f89f0e73af73', '135679', '"[{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Hi, this is Allison Larson. I''m doing a reflective session. How can schools \",\"startTime\":1734048171,\"endTime\":1734048176},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"bridge the knowledge gap for families unfamiliar with the high school to college and trade pipeline? We do a lot of trying to do family engagement activities. \",\"startTime\":1734048176,\"endTime\":1734048186},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"We do. \",\"startTime\":1734048186,\"endTime\":1734048191},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Zoom sessions and also in person sessions for families. We are trying to engage \",\"startTime\":1734048192,\"endTime\":1734048196},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"our natural leaders group to be more knowledgeable because Edmonds the way we have. \",\"startTime\":1734048196,\"endTime\":1734048205},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Families who did not grow up in the United States, and so their understanding of schooling is completely different, and we have some cultural differences that we need to bridge. So we tried to find a variety of ways to provide resources, \",\"startTime\":1734048205,\"endTime\":1734048222},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"and we''re always looking for more opportunities to engage families further. \",\"startTime\":1734048222,\"endTime\":1734048227},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"We try to do things.\",\"startTime\":1734048229,\"endTime\":1734048230},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Multiple times during the school year and try to provide information in a bunch of different ways for families. \",\"startTime\":1734048232,\"endTime\":1734048238},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Card talks about umm, what we can do more specifically for families and provides. \",\"startTime\":1734048297,\"endTime\":1734048304},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Some good suggestions like parent teacher meetings about explaining post secondary options. \",\"startTime\":1734048304,\"endTime\":1734048310},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Umm, we do we? I haven''t thought of that, so that might be a really interesting. \",\"startTime\":1734048311,\"endTime\":1734048316},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Strategy for parents. We do do a lot of workshops about financial planning. \",\"startTime\":1734048317,\"endTime\":1734048322},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"This year we are partnering with some community partners to come in and help families with filling out FAFSA and WAFSA, and we have some we partnered with some community organizations as well as just volunteers that can help families navigate through that process for financial planning. \",\"startTime\":1734048322,\"endTime\":1734048343},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"And then of course, we also have a college and Career Center specialist who helps and answer those kinds of questions. \",\"startTime\":1734048344,\"endTime\":1734048351},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"And I had not thought of creating a mentorship program connecting our parents and alumni. And that is a really interesting idea. And one thing that our parent \",\"startTime\":1734048353,\"endTime\":1734048365},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"group is wanting to do is establish an alumni organization for our school. So \",\"startTime\":1734048365,\"endTime\":1734048372},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"that would be interesting then to help create partnerships among that alumni. \",\"startTime\":1734048372,\"endTime\":1734048378},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"So in this question about parents feeling really overwhelmed by all the post secondary options and the financial aid. I think one thing that we are really \",\"startTime\":1734048442,\"endTime\":1734048454},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"trying to do in our school and trying to Foster and grow a natural leaders program where we are helping families that did not grow up in the United States and families of our multilingual students to connect with each other and then hopefully. \",\"startTime\":1734048454,\"endTime\":1734048471},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"They learn information that then they can pass along and connect to their cultural groups. And we do talk about in those meetings what are the ways students can \",\"startTime\":1734048471,\"endTime\":1734048480},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"graduate from high school and then also what are the post secondary options, I think sometimes. \",\"startTime\":1734048480,\"endTime\":1734048489},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"We approach our families of multilingual students from a deficit lens and I think we sometimes forget that those families have some pretty big goals for their students to achieve and want to see their students do well and so. \",\"startTime\":1734048491,\"endTime\":1734048507},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"It I think it''s really important that we try to do that outreach. Of course \",\"startTime\":1734048509,\"endTime\":1734048514},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"we do have resources where we have a counselor for our multilingual program and we have two pair educators that support that program along with our teachers \",\"startTime\":1734048514,\"endTime\":1734048523},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"and the counselor and the para educators and our family resource advocate meet regularly to, to reach out to family specifically and build relationships with them. \",\"startTime\":1734048523,\"endTime\":1734048537},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"And then invite them into the school so that we can have meetings and have those conversations with them. So it''s not a huge program yet, but the people who \",\"startTime\":1734048537,\"endTime\":1734048547},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"are participating in the program do so regularly because I think they''re finding connections at the school. So it''s exciting and I think it''s just going to take \",\"startTime\":1734048547,\"endTime\":1734048557},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"a few years to really get it going. But we really. \",\"startTime\":1734048557,\"endTime\":1734048562},{\"speaker\":\"10900\",\"text\":\"Appreciate those efforts for our Natural leaders families to learn more about post secondary options. \",\"startTime\":1734048564,\"endTime\":1734048570}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.269408+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.269408+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 323, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:27.997Z", "session_title": "Family/Parental Involvement in Post-Secondary Access", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1428", "name": "Family/Parental Involvement in Post-Secondary Access", "tags": [{"name": "HSLC"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('913d471f-73b4-4adc-aaed-3d2d37250565', 'f75f7f16-84b9-41ce-b842-2a77a9dd70b8', '132332', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.465465+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.465465+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 303, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:40.388Z", "session_title": "Standards vs. Curriculum", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "250", "name": "Standards vs. Curriculum", "tags": [{"name": "Cothinking Classrooms"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('c348ff40-0044-4a02-a697-253331585914', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '135458', '"[{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, let''s see what is what is GPT and what is their main function? GPT is a \",\"startTime\":1733238167,\"endTime\":1733238170},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"generative. \",\"startTime\":1733238170,\"endTime\":1733238173},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Pre trained something with text training stuff and it''s really for just understanding human generated messages and and information to make life a little bit simpler and easier for you in many different ways. \",\"startTime\":1733238174,\"endTime\":1733238189},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"GPT is a generative.\",\"startTime\":1733238212,\"endTime\":1733238214},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Pre trained text analyzer.\",\"startTime\":1733238215,\"endTime\":1733238217},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"And the main functions are really just analyzing massive amounts of information and and answering questions and. \",\"startTime\":1733238220,\"endTime\":1733238225},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Providing information to you in a in a fashion that makes sense for you, and distilling of information to make things easier. \",\"startTime\":1733238227,\"endTime\":1733238236},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I should probably begin a new engagement with an AI versus remaining the same one. You''re not getting the information that you''re you''re looking for or you \",\"startTime\":1733238274,\"endTime\":1733238280},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"need to tweak something up. \",\"startTime\":1733238280,\"endTime\":1733238284},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I think we, we, we look at human inquiry as the generator of the idea that we want to try and solve, we''re trying to work with and as we, as we do that human inquiry, then we utilize AI to make that happen with our prompt. And then we \",\"startTime\":1733238286,\"endTime\":1733238299},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"have to engage with that to make sure that it''s what we''re looking for. \",\"startTime\":1733238299,\"endTime\":1733238303},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"If it''s not what we''re looking for, then we might have to begin a new engagement or tweak the current engagement that we''re in. It''s really about being clear \",\"startTime\":1733238304,\"endTime\":1733238312},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"in terms of what you''re you''re looking for. But if we want to maintain continuity \",\"startTime\":1733238312,\"endTime\":1733238316},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"and an understanding of the same conversation, then we''re going to we''re going to continue that unless something on the outside or something changes that we need to address in a different manner or different fashion. \",\"startTime\":1733238316,\"endTime\":1733238328},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"In terms of utilizing AI, it was really about.\",\"startTime\":1733238355,\"endTime\":1733238357},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Just attaching documents and, and diving deep into them and creating action plans as a result of school improvement plans and goals that people want to accomplish as I''ve worked with with staff. The other thing is utilizing that \",\"startTime\":1733238362,\"endTime\":1733238374},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"to utilizing AI to write observation reports and other stuff. What I''d really \",\"startTime\":1733238374,\"endTime\":1733238379},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"like to do is better understand how to utilize it with data and how to crunch data and, and, and turn things out. \",\"startTime\":1733238379,\"endTime\":1733238387}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.284497+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.284497+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 155, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:28.075Z", "session_title": "Understanding and Utilizing GPT and AI Threads", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "197", "name": "Understanding and Utilizing GPT and AI Threads", "tags": [{"name": "Dream Camp"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "AI in Education"}, {"name": "Freemium"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('651c13b1-c874-4247-a428-17f050858843', '31f25266-25f6-40c6-b809-30b6e6bc2301', '135553', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Hello.\",\"startTime\":1733443371,\"endTime\":1733443371},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Shoot my.\",\"startTime\":1733443374,\"endTime\":1733443376},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I can hear you. Can you hear me? OK, Perfect.\",\"startTime\":1733443377,\"endTime\":1733443380},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Can you hear me OK?\",\"startTime\":1733443378,\"endTime\":1733443379},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733443380,\"endTime\":1733443380},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I was like, oh gosh, a new platform I don''t know how to use.\",\"startTime\":1733443382,\"endTime\":1733443385},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"OK. This is my I mean, were you doing it the bell? Did you practice at bell \",\"startTime\":1733443387,\"endTime\":1733443390},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"to do it? \",\"startTime\":1733443390,\"endTime\":1733443392},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"No, I actually, I this is my first time like on here. I did like the couple \",\"startTime\":1733443393,\"endTime\":1733443398},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"of ones you do by yourself. So yeah, I''ve never done this before. \",\"startTime\":1733443398,\"endTime\":1733443402},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh, Oh my gosh. OK. And it says I''m not supposed to drive, but I was gonna, \",\"startTime\":1733443402,\"endTime\":1733443406},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"I was gonna drive home and then do it at the same time. How do you feel about \",\"startTime\":1733443406,\"endTime\":1733443410},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"that? I''m OK with it. You might have to read the questions, though, if that''s \",\"startTime\":1733443410,\"endTime\":1733443414},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Well, if you feel OK about it, I''m fine with it.\",\"startTime\":1733443412,\"endTime\":1733443415},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"OK. OK, awesome. \",\"startTime\":1733443414,\"endTime\":1733443418},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK, absolutely Fine. So my name is Mallory Wilson. I''m an assistant principal \",\"startTime\":1733443419,\"endTime\":1733443425},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"at Olympia High School, and this is my second year here. Oh, cool. \",\"startTime\":1733443425,\"endTime\":1733443430},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"I''m Annie Parker. I am a principal in Renton School District. This is also my \",\"startTime\":1733443431,\"endTime\":1733443433},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"second year at my school. Before that I was an AP for five years in Seattle \",\"startTime\":1733443433,\"endTime\":1733443436},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"School District. \",\"startTime\":1733443436,\"endTime\":1733443439},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh, nice. What school in Seattle? Oh, OK. I''m like, not from Seattle, but I \",\"startTime\":1733443439,\"endTime\":1733443443},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh, gosh. I did two years at Salmon Bay K and then three years at Nova High \",\"startTime\":1733443441,\"endTime\":1733443446},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"lived there for a number of years and worked so like, I was a teacher there and everything. So yeah, that''s why I was wondering, but OK. \",\"startTime\":1733443443,\"endTime\":1733443452},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"School. Yeah. Where did you teach? In Seattle. Oh, wow. Yeah, I know. Right \",\"startTime\":1733443446,\"endTime\":1733443452},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"there. Yeah, absolutely. That little old facility. Wow. \",\"startTime\":1733443452,\"endTime\":1733443457},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"So I taught at a residential treatment facility, but it was served by Seattle Public Schools, and it''s called Ryder, which is up in like Lake City Way. Yeah, \",\"startTime\":1733443459,\"endTime\":1733443469},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"yeah, Yep, exactly. So I worked at the school on that site. \",\"startTime\":1733443469,\"endTime\":1733443474},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"And we only like taught the students that lived there. Yeah, exactly. OK, well, \",\"startTime\":1733443478,\"endTime\":1733443483},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yeah. I kind of remember that program, like it was kind of an inclusive, like \",\"startTime\":1733443483,\"endTime\":1733443486},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"let me I just click ahead to the next card then. OK. OK. So discuss the benefits \",\"startTime\":1733443483,\"endTime\":1733443489},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"you would go and that''s where you were. Yeah, Yeah, OK. Yep, just hit next and \",\"startTime\":1733443486,\"endTime\":1733443490},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"of Co teaching for inclusion. Would you like to go first? \",\"startTime\":1733443489,\"endTime\":1733443494},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"then it''s going to do a yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733443490,\"endTime\":1733443494},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Discuss the benefits of Co teaching for inclusion. Well, I mean, I think something \",\"startTime\":1733443505,\"endTime\":1733443510},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"that is really unfortunate at the elementary level, it''s much trickier to Co teach. And I remember when I worked at Nova, there were millions of opportunities. \",\"startTime\":1733443510,\"endTime\":1733443521},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"That our paras would Co teach, our speed teachers would Co teach and they would just build the curriculum together around that. It''s it''s quite different in \",\"startTime\":1733443526,\"endTime\":1733443533},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"elementary where there''s a lot of pull out for special education. There are \",\"startTime\":1733443533,\"endTime\":1733443537},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"push in models that often times it''s like 20-30 minute quick hits and then, you know, it''s not really that coaching style. But I do think there''s a huge \",\"startTime\":1733443537,\"endTime\":1733443545},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"benefit if, if it''s doable, can we talk great results when special education teachers and Jenna teachers work together to go teach kids. And then it was \",\"startTime\":1733443545,\"endTime\":1733443552},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733443545,\"endTime\":1733443546},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"really seamless. \",\"startTime\":1733443552,\"endTime\":1733443556},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Going into the lessons and differentiating the lessons and then also like meeting with all the learners at the same time. Yeah. What about you? Yeah, yeah, yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733443558,\"endTime\":1733443566},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"So this is actually a great discussion prompt. We didn''t have many classes that \",\"startTime\":1733443566,\"endTime\":1733443572},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"were Co taught last year and we definitely saw a need for it this year and so. \",\"startTime\":1733443572,\"endTime\":1733443577},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"We started kind of with the willing. I think that there was definitely willingness \",\"startTime\":1733443578,\"endTime\":1733443583},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"from our special Ed teachers to Co teach, but just there wasn''t enough training. \",\"startTime\":1733443583,\"endTime\":1733443588},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"And so we partnered with C home and did some like intensive targeted training around a Co Top Model. And we''ve been really trying to mirror what what they''ve \",\"startTime\":1733443588,\"endTime\":1733443598},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"been doing for the past few years and so. \",\"startTime\":1733443598,\"endTime\":1733443602},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"We''re seeing huge benefits to it. I would say that like just selfishly, like \",\"startTime\":1733443603,\"endTime\":1733443607},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"the morale with staff is better and there''s like just trust being built there that these are our kids like. \",\"startTime\":1733443607,\"endTime\":1733443614},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, maybe I''m not the expert in math, but I am an expert in special education, you know, or that vice versa. But our students have no idea which ones are served \",\"startTime\":1733443615,\"endTime\":1733443624},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"in special education in those spaces. Ones aren''t. And I think our parents are \",\"startTime\":1733443624,\"endTime\":1733443628},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"definitely like, please tell me there''s going to be a Co taught math next year for my kid. You know, please tell me there''s going to be a Co taught English. \",\"startTime\":1733443628,\"endTime\":1733443636},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"And so we''re seeing some really huge successes and. \",\"startTime\":1733443636,\"endTime\":1733443641},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I think our teachers are just kind of pleasantly surprised by it so.\",\"startTime\":1733443642,\"endTime\":1733443646},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"It''s been really great. And yeah, I hope that we shift, we can shift more that \",\"startTime\":1733443647,\"endTime\":1733443651},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"direction with more and more teachers. Last year there was a lot of, they were \",\"startTime\":1733443651,\"endTime\":1733443655},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733443655,\"endTime\":1733443655},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"like, no, like teachers were like, no, I''m not doing it. You know, like I don''t \",\"startTime\":1733443655,\"endTime\":1733443659},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"want to slow down for for kids that, you know, like I''m used to teaching. We \",\"startTime\":1733443659,\"endTime\":1733443664},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"have kind of this, we have a, we have a very seasoned staff at this school and we strive for excellence. And that''s really hard to adjust for students that \",\"startTime\":1733443664,\"endTime\":1733443672},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"need that adjustment. So. Yeah, but. \",\"startTime\":1733443672,\"endTime\":1733443677},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Seeing some some great things with the people and I think the team of Gen. Ed \",\"startTime\":1733443678,\"endTime\":1733443682},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"teachers are the right people to be vocal about it, to try to recruit others next year, yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733443682,\"endTime\":1733443689},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Make such a difference when there''s that buy in and they can shift the culture naturally as a staff, there is nothing harder than when most everybody''s like, oh. \",\"startTime\":1733443690,\"endTime\":1733443698},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Not into it, so that sounds amazing. OK, I''m not. I''m going to break eye contact. \",\"startTime\":1733443700,\"endTime\":1733443704},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733443700,\"endTime\":1733443701},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"I''m going to like a heavy traffic. \",\"startTime\":1733443704,\"endTime\":1733443708},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"No, you''re fine. You''re actually you''re frozen on my screen, but you I can still \",\"startTime\":1733443709,\"endTime\":1733443713},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"hear you talking, so it''s OK. OK, sounds good. OK, so the question says why \",\"startTime\":1733443713,\"endTime\":1733443717},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh, no, OK, I''m in a bad. I''m in a bad part of town. You keep talking. Let''s \",\"startTime\":1733443714,\"endTime\":1733443717},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"go to the next question. Do you want to go first? \",\"startTime\":1733443717,\"endTime\":1733443720},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"do you think inclusion is essential in our schools today? Discuss the impact \",\"startTime\":1733443717,\"endTime\":1733443721},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"on students. \",\"startTime\":1733443721,\"endTime\":1733443725},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Since I''m being frozen.\",\"startTime\":1733443731,\"endTime\":1733443732},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Sure, sure. So I would say that this is actually a conversation I had with a \",\"startTime\":1733443733,\"endTime\":1733443737},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"student the other day who is a junior. And we were discussing him being evaluated \",\"startTime\":1733443737,\"endTime\":1733443741},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"for an IEP. And he had kind of that typical like, I don''t want to be one of \",\"startTime\":1733443741,\"endTime\":1733443745},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"those students. I don''t want to be in one of those classes. And I was talking \",\"startTime\":1733443745,\"endTime\":1733443750},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"to him and his mom and his counselor was there in our school psych. And I said, \",\"startTime\":1733443750,\"endTime\":1733443754},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"you know, you''re you''re the main character in your story. And I was like, who \",\"startTime\":1733443754,\"endTime\":1733443758},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"do you know? \",\"startTime\":1733443758,\"endTime\":1733443762},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"In one of those classes, and he was like, I don''t know anyone. I was like, I \",\"startTime\":1733443763,\"endTime\":1733443767},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"bet you know a lot. I bet you, you know a lot of students that are in classes \",\"startTime\":1733443767,\"endTime\":1733443771},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"that have like, I bet you are friends with kids that have Ieps. And I was like, \",\"startTime\":1733443771,\"endTime\":1733443775},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"nobody else is really paying attention to you. I was like, I hate to say it \",\"startTime\":1733443775,\"endTime\":1733443778},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"that way, but like you''re the one who thinks everybody''s looking at you and everybody like knows that you''re in that special class. Yeah. I was like, it''s. \",\"startTime\":1733443778,\"endTime\":1733443786},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"You''re not that special.\",\"startTime\":1733443785,\"endTime\":1733443786},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"It''s really not the case. And I was like, and you said school has been hard \",\"startTime\":1733443786,\"endTime\":1733443789},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"for like 11 years. I was like for. \",\"startTime\":1733443789,\"endTime\":1733443793},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"As long as you can remember, you have not liked school and it''s been difficult. \",\"startTime\":1733443794,\"endTime\":1733443798},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I was like, I want you to graduate and have loved your last few years. Like \",\"startTime\":1733443798,\"endTime\":1733443801},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''m sorry that it''s taken this long. But then I talked about our Co Top Model \",\"startTime\":1733443801,\"endTime\":1733443805},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"and his mom started like breaking down in tears and was like, I think this is exactly what he needs, you know? So I think the impact on students is so powerful \",\"startTime\":1733443805,\"endTime\":1733443812},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"and just the fact that they''re just like, no, that kids in my English class not. \",\"startTime\":1733443812,\"endTime\":1733443819},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''m, you know, like in a special English class.\",\"startTime\":1733443820,\"endTime\":1733443823},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yeah, right, right, which is sometimes really sad to like have kids so like separated that just need like resource support. Know some some it''s not even \",\"startTime\":1733443825,\"endTime\":1733443835},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"like the intensive IEP and that many minutes or services that I I love what you said about this. People don''t know and it''s so normalized anymore like when \",\"startTime\":1733443835,\"endTime\":1733443845},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1733443839,\"endTime\":1733443840},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"some old school parents you talk to think of special education like back in the maybe 90s where people would get. \",\"startTime\":1733443845,\"endTime\":1733443855},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Ton of and you were separated and normalized anymore and we have kids in our school where they''re like, are you pulling me out? Like they get excited like \",\"startTime\":1733443857,\"endTime\":1733443866},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"when when am I going to get pulled out? I want to go with you even with like \",\"startTime\":1733443866,\"endTime\":1733443870},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1733443870,\"endTime\":1733443870},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"our intervention. We''re like no, honey, you don''t qualify like you don''t need \",\"startTime\":1733443870,\"endTime\":1733443874},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"these extra support, but you know maybe one day we can play for something fun. \",\"startTime\":1733443874,\"endTime\":1733443878},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1733443876,\"endTime\":1733443877},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"So it''s it''s very accepted and love that. What was the other part when students. \",\"startTime\":1733443878,\"endTime\":1733443882},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733443879,\"endTime\":1733443879},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"It says discuss its impact on students and why do you think it''s Why do you think inclusion is essential in our schools? \",\"startTime\":1733443886,\"endTime\":1733443893},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh yes, I think the other thing I would say too is that everyone has needs and I think the more. \",\"startTime\":1733443896,\"endTime\":1733443901},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Individualized, we can make our educational systems, our processes, our, our teaching, all of those things are better. And so to me, it''s, it''s just how \",\"startTime\":1733443903,\"endTime\":1733443911},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"we should be approaching education. Do we have the resources? No, our schools \",\"startTime\":1733443911,\"endTime\":1733443915},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"aren''t built for that. Our systems aren''t built for that. But I think that''s \",\"startTime\":1733443915,\"endTime\":1733443919},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1733443918,\"endTime\":1733443919},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"a necessary shift that has to happen as a school system if we''re really honoring every child''s need and their whole self, right? Every, every kid is different \",\"startTime\":1733443919,\"endTime\":1733443927},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"and we have to stop labeling and boxing in. \",\"startTime\":1733443927,\"endTime\":1733443932},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"And to see. And I think it teaches kids that everyone''s different and that''s \",\"startTime\":1733443935,\"endTime\":1733443937},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"OK. \",\"startTime\":1733443937,\"endTime\":1733443939},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"And everyone gets what speed, and that''s OK, which is really important. Oh my \",\"startTime\":1733443939,\"endTime\":1733443942},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733443939,\"endTime\":1733443939},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"gosh. \",\"startTime\":1733443942,\"endTime\":1733443944},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''m hoping that with this, you know, I don''t know what your school kind of makeup looks like, but we have almost 2000 kids here and we have just this huge yeah, we have this huge increase of 504 plans. And I think a lot of teachers are realizing \",\"startTime\":1733443943,\"endTime\":1733443954},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"like I''m just going to make the use of a calculator, a universal support. Like \",\"startTime\":1733443954,\"endTime\":1733443958},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I don''t, I''m so sick of trying to figure out which kids need this and which kids don''t. So I''m kind of hoping the Co teach model is going to shift teachers \",\"startTime\":1733443958,\"endTime\":1733443965},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"thinking too, like this is just a best practice. Like I just need to do this \",\"startTime\":1733443965,\"endTime\":1733443969},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"for. \",\"startTime\":1733443969,\"endTime\":1733443973},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Exactly.\",\"startTime\":1733443974,\"endTime\":1733443975},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"All kids, you know, and so that''s where I''m really excited is that I''ve, I''ve seen some teachers that have been here for like 20 years and they''re like opening \",\"startTime\":1733443974,\"endTime\":1733443982},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"up to Co teaching and I think they''re just saying like, oh, that''s not that hard to differentiate that or oh, OK, like that''s how I reteach this, you know, in a different way, or that''s what manipulatives are for or whatever. So I''m \",\"startTime\":1733443982,\"endTime\":1733443994},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''m really excited about how it''s impacting the teachers as well. \",\"startTime\":1733443994,\"endTime\":1733443998},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"That''s awesome. And the more access points we can give kids, the better for \",\"startTime\":1733443998,\"endTime\":1733444001},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"them. That''s amazing. We move on to the next question. OK. \",\"startTime\":1733444001,\"endTime\":1733444005},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, sounds good. You know what? It''s it''s like frozen in between on \",\"startTime\":1733444002,\"endTime\":1733444008},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"my screen. I don''t want to put you in danger though, but I can''t see it. \",\"startTime\":1733444008,\"endTime\":1733444014},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh, there you go. Do you mind reading it? Sorry.\",\"startTime\":1733444009,\"endTime\":1733444011},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh my gosh. OK, let me get in a safe position here. What do you think is the \",\"startTime\":1733444019,\"endTime\":1733444023},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"hardest part of Co teaching? Share your thoughts and listen to what Mallory \",\"startTime\":1733444023,\"endTime\":1733444028},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"considers the question for you. That''s why I did it. Yeah, it''s for you. So \",\"startTime\":1733444028,\"endTime\":1733444032},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"maybe that''s why it''s a half halfway has your name. \",\"startTime\":1733444032,\"endTime\":1733444036},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh, is that what it says?\",\"startTime\":1733444033,\"endTime\":1733444035},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh, OK.\",\"startTime\":1733444038,\"endTime\":1733444039},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"That''s interesting, I wonder if mine has your name? Like I only see half of \",\"startTime\":1733444041,\"endTime\":1733444044},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"the questions and I think your name is on there too so. \",\"startTime\":1733444044,\"endTime\":1733444047},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Oh, that''s hilarious. OK, maybe. I don''t know.\",\"startTime\":1733444044,\"endTime\":1733444048},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK. I would say the hardest part is probably that beginning part and giving \",\"startTime\":1733444052,\"endTime\":1733444057},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"up, you know, what''s been your space and your, you know, like power, right? \",\"startTime\":1733444057,\"endTime\":1733444062},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"And really sharing that. But I also would say that I think after a year or two \",\"startTime\":1733444062,\"endTime\":1733444067},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"of doing it, you''re you''re going to see it''s really easier for you. \",\"startTime\":1733444067,\"endTime\":1733444072},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"But I think those initial things at the beginning of like remembering there''s another adult in there and like who, you know, trying to figure out, OK, who''s kind of more in charge this day and when do I take a backseat? I think it''s \",\"startTime\":1733444073,\"endTime\":1733444084},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"it''s been harder for the adults. And then just logistically for our students, \",\"startTime\":1733444084,\"endTime\":1733444087},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"we don''t have enough spots in our Co taught classes. So we''re having to be so \",\"startTime\":1733444087,\"endTime\":1733444091},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"picky about which kids we put in there because we want to stick to a certain ratio. And that''s been really hard too, because if we are seeing more kids could \",\"startTime\":1733444091,\"endTime\":1733444098},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"benefit from it and we don''t have enough space. \",\"startTime\":1733444098,\"endTime\":1733444102},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh yeah, right. And likely enough teachers as well. Like if you''re teaching, \",\"startTime\":1733444104,\"endTime\":1733444108},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"if you''re doubling up teachers on a class, that''s one last class during that period that can be taught by somebody else to put more kids in the class. Yeah, \",\"startTime\":1733444108,\"endTime\":1733444117},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733444116,\"endTime\":1733444118},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"that''s a hard bread to do. I would agree with your like the setting up the parameters \",\"startTime\":1733444117,\"endTime\":1733444121},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"and boundaries, like what''s my part with your part? How do we cope in real time? \",\"startTime\":1733444121,\"endTime\":1733444125},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"The other challenge with that goes on with that is when teachers are. \",\"startTime\":1733444125,\"endTime\":1733444130},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Fit with each other like how do you support them Co teaching when they''re having conflict because of their teaching style or because of their beliefs around kids or things like that. I think that is something that we can run into it. \",\"startTime\":1733444134,\"endTime\":1733444146},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Nova in the Co teaching model were some some teachers just it was also one of those stuff that works there forever and some of them did not get along and \",\"startTime\":1733444146,\"endTime\":1733444153},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"they would refuse to teach with each other and so then it was always the same teachers Co teaching and then the same that were kind of isolated not doing it so that. \",\"startTime\":1733444153,\"endTime\":1733444164},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"A little bit tricky, but I heard this year they''re doing better. I''m not there \",\"startTime\":1733444167,\"endTime\":1733444170},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"anymore, obviously, but I heard it''s got yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733444170,\"endTime\":1733444173},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right, Yeah, I think you bring up a really good point. We had a bad pairing \",\"startTime\":1733444172,\"endTime\":1733444175},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"last year and they''re not Co teaching at all this year. Like we didn''t feel \",\"startTime\":1733444175,\"endTime\":1733444179},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"like they''d be a good fit for anybody after the year that they had together and probably they were both turned off from teaching in the in the in the end, so. \",\"startTime\":1733444179,\"endTime\":1733444189},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Right. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733444186,\"endTime\":1733444188},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"All right, they taught just I think it was only one class that was like a Co taught math and. \",\"startTime\":1733444191,\"endTime\":1733444198},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Did they did they teach the entire year or just a couple of classes?\",\"startTime\":1733444193,\"endTime\":1733444198},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"It was they were paired together before I was in this building and I, I didn''t agree with the pairing once I found out the reason, But neither one of them were very strong teachers. And so the rationale was, well, let''s put them both \",\"startTime\":1733444205,\"endTime\":1733444216},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"together and together, maybe they could bring out each other''s like strengths. \",\"startTime\":1733444216,\"endTime\":1733444220},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"So I kind of understand that, but like, I think you need your very best teachers for a Co Top Model, not your ones that are struggling the most. And so I, I \",\"startTime\":1733444220,\"endTime\":1733444228},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yes.\",\"startTime\":1733444226,\"endTime\":1733444226},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"think if you got a math teacher who''s not that great at teaching math, and then you''ve got a special Ed teacher who just like. \",\"startTime\":1733444228,\"endTime\":1733444235},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Oh yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733444229,\"endTime\":1733444230},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Wants to do their own thing. You run into some real power dynamics, like with \",\"startTime\":1733444237,\"endTime\":1733444240},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"the with the. So yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733444240,\"endTime\":1733444244},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Yeah, that makes a lot of sense. And their own insecurities. So the things that \",\"startTime\":1733444245,\"endTime\":1733444249},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"they''re not good at that they''re working on are amplified at times. Oh yeah, \",\"startTime\":1733444249,\"endTime\":1733444253},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, and they were both very respectful to one another. But I think it was \",\"startTime\":1733444251,\"endTime\":1733444255},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"that''s, that''s hard. OK. \",\"startTime\":1733444253,\"endTime\":1733444256},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"pretty quickly, like our special Ed teacher kind of turned into a para in that space, and it was just kind of insulting, you know? So, alright. \",\"startTime\":1733444255,\"endTime\":1733444263}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.472548+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.472548+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 909, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:28.240Z", "session_title": "Coteaching improves inclusion", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "56", "name": "Coteaching improves inclusion", "tags": [{"name": "Inclusion"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('9b690a8f-92f1-4c66-945a-4b9319ff4174', 'a3d62eb9-a287-4962-83ad-36d2e6f079b3', '74412', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:40:26.988446+00', '2025-05-06 19:40:26.988446+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 201, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:40:26.933Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('d919123d-2864-45e5-b895-1ff5cf2a772b', '31f25266-25f6-40c6-b809-30b6e6bc2301', '134588', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"Hi, my name is Annie Parker. I am an elementary school principal and I guess \",\"startTime\":1732054415,\"endTime\":1732054420},{\"speaker\":\"11318\",\"text\":\"I''m hoping to learn more about effective leadership and how to support teachers and making sure that students are successful in school. \",\"startTime\":1732054420,\"endTime\":1732054430}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.468383+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.468383+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 19, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:40.254Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('eea7f16f-ac26-49aa-84bf-a6633c645bf9', '713b8455-cc3b-4ab1-bcfb-255f93bf56b0', '136665', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Good day, Jeff. How are you mate?\",\"startTime\":1738087298,\"endTime\":1738087299},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Wonderful. Good day to you too.\",\"startTime\":1738087298,\"endTime\":1738087301},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Happy Tuesday. Tuesday. Yes, Tuesday.\",\"startTime\":1738087303,\"endTime\":1738087305},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It is Tuesday, Yeah. So.\",\"startTime\":1738087306,\"endTime\":1738087308},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, we have a balmy 40 plus degrees day here in Madison, WI, which is glorious. \",\"startTime\":1738087308,\"endTime\":1738087314},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Nice, nice. It was 12 when I woke up this morning here. I think it it might \",\"startTime\":1738087316,\"endTime\":1738087320},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"get up to 35. I think is the high scheduled. \",\"startTime\":1738087320,\"endTime\":1738087324},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"OK, OK.\",\"startTime\":1738087323,\"endTime\":1738087324},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"I''ll, I''ll, I''ll take it. We''ve had some really cold days here, so I''m I''m enjoying \",\"startTime\":1738087325,\"endTime\":1738087328},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"this warmer week. \",\"startTime\":1738087328,\"endTime\":1738087331},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, way to go, Way to go.\",\"startTime\":1738087331,\"endTime\":1738087333},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Ice breaker today what''s what''s your favorite book or movie?\",\"startTime\":1738087334,\"endTime\":1738087338},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"You can''t use Dune, you use that last time.\",\"startTime\":1738087340,\"endTime\":1738087343},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, no, I, I.\",\"startTime\":1738087343,\"endTime\":1738087344},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Man, I love, I love like stupid comedies. I''ve got a there''s a place in my heart \",\"startTime\":1738087346,\"endTime\":1738087350},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"full. \",\"startTime\":1738087350,\"endTime\":1738087353},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Really stupid stuff like Will Farrow type stupid stuff. Yeah, like that type \",\"startTime\":1738087356,\"endTime\":1738087360},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"of genre. \",\"startTime\":1738087360,\"endTime\":1738087364},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Just makes me happy.\",\"startTime\":1738087365,\"endTime\":1738087366},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, I love it. I love it.\",\"startTime\":1738087367,\"endTime\":1738087369},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, what? What about you?\",\"startTime\":1738087369,\"endTime\":1738087370},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Umm, I have a place in my heart for that, to let go of the world and the seriousness too. \",\"startTime\":1738087374,\"endTime\":1738087378},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Umm, I think, uh, there''s something about The Hobbit as a kid, uh, reading it and my dad loved Token and. \",\"startTime\":1738087379,\"endTime\":1738087386},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"All of the things with it and then a reading so much of.\",\"startTime\":1738087386,\"endTime\":1738087390},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"The token book series and even the similarly in and all that stuff and.\",\"startTime\":1738087392,\"endTime\":1738087397},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I just find myself captivated by this other world where there''s other people fighting for life and what''s right and figuring it out and they''re all specially created and different and unique and. \",\"startTime\":1738087397,\"endTime\":1738087409},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087397,\"endTime\":1738087399},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yep, cool.\",\"startTime\":1738087410,\"endTime\":1738087411},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, something magical about that. But I do like that Will Ferrell, kind of. \",\"startTime\":1738087411,\"endTime\":1738087416},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087414,\"endTime\":1738087414},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Kind of laugh sometimes it makes my heart, makes my heart just let go of the seriousness that I need to at times. I like it. \",\"startTime\":1738087417,\"endTime\":1738087425},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, man.\",\"startTime\":1738087418,\"endTime\":1738087419},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087424,\"endTime\":1738087424},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh alright. Oh, do you know what GPT is?\",\"startTime\":1738087428,\"endTime\":1738087432},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"You know, I actually looked at this about a week ago and now I''m blanking on what it is. \",\"startTime\":1738087436,\"endTime\":1738087441},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"So no, I''m not even gonna guess because I know it''s wrong.\",\"startTime\":1738087442,\"endTime\":1738087446},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Under the Moor on mine it does tell us what it is.\",\"startTime\":1738087448,\"endTime\":1738087451},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Generative pre trained transformer. I remember. I remember it had generative \",\"startTime\":1738087451,\"endTime\":1738087456},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, that''s why Jenner and Tre.\",\"startTime\":1738087454,\"endTime\":1738087456},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and and training in it but I couldn''t remember the the. \",\"startTime\":1738087456,\"endTime\":1738087461},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Designation for it, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087463,\"endTime\":1738087465},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, that''s a good one. How do I remember that? Like what? Yeah, I need some \",\"startTime\":1738087465,\"endTime\":1738087468},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"word play on how to remember that. \",\"startTime\":1738087468,\"endTime\":1738087471},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, Why? Just look it up. We have it at our fingertips and then and you put \",\"startTime\":1738087471,\"endTime\":1738087474},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it back on anybody else. That''s the one best thing in my teaching I''ve ever \",\"startTime\":1738087474,\"endTime\":1738087478},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, true.\",\"startTime\":1738087475,\"endTime\":1738087476},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"done. \",\"startTime\":1738087478,\"endTime\":1738087481},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And high school kids are wonderful for it. I did my biggest stint at a high \",\"startTime\":1738087482,\"endTime\":1738087485},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"school and you just play dumb all the time because they think you''re dumb. And \",\"startTime\":1738087485,\"endTime\":1738087489},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087489,\"endTime\":1738087490},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"when you play dumb, they don''t know when you''re really dumb or when you''re hiding the answer. Even with adults, you''re like, Oh, I don''t know what is that? Or \",\"startTime\":1738087489,\"endTime\":1738087497},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''ll ask something like even the other day I totally blanked one of my good colleagues names. You know how it goes in the middle of the day and something \",\"startTime\":1738087497,\"endTime\":1738087504},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and just can''t replace it. So I just tossed it back out there and I go, you \",\"startTime\":1738087504,\"endTime\":1738087508},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087506,\"endTime\":1738087506},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"know, some people like I hear they and. \",\"startTime\":1738087508,\"endTime\":1738087511},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Describe the person and and I was just throwing it out there like a fishing line they snagged right on that Oh you mean Kristen Munson. I''m like yeah, Kristen \",\"startTime\":1738087511,\"endTime\":1738087518},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"isn''t she amazing? I''m like I totally couldn''t remember her name for the save \",\"startTime\":1738087518,\"endTime\":1738087522},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"my life for the moment, but. \",\"startTime\":1738087522,\"endTime\":1738087525},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That''s my new strategy and you''ll see me do it too many times I''m sure in the future. But. \",\"startTime\":1738087527,\"endTime\":1738087532},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"You just get them to think that you don''t know and they, they, they happy to, they''re happy to figure it out with you for you. \",\"startTime\":1738087534,\"endTime\":1738087539},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087539,\"endTime\":1738087539},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"What do you what do you think about when you like, even when I''m looking at those words generative pre trained transformer. What''s up you make you think \",\"startTime\":1738087540,\"endTime\":1738087548},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"about especially with your use because I know you''ve used the chat GPTA lot. \",\"startTime\":1738087548,\"endTime\":1738087552},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I think it it just means like pre trained. It''s more like.\",\"startTime\":1738087553,\"endTime\":1738087559},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"It''s it''s using using all the information they have which is the the Internet basically right to. \",\"startTime\":1738087564,\"endTime\":1738087573},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"To pre train your assistant your.\",\"startTime\":1738087574,\"endTime\":1738087578},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Support worker your tutor your.\",\"startTime\":1738087578,\"endTime\":1738087582},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Whatever you want to call your GPT.\",\"startTime\":1738087582,\"endTime\":1738087584},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"But it''s umm.\",\"startTime\":1738087585,\"endTime\":1738087586},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I''m not sure how Transformer fits into that, but.\",\"startTime\":1738087588,\"endTime\":1738087591},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"It certainly transforms the way that you.\",\"startTime\":1738087591,\"endTime\":1738087594},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Work and live but yeah I think just just like thinking about having a pre trained assistant ready to support you. \",\"startTime\":1738087595,\"endTime\":1738087605},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"With whatever you need.\",\"startTime\":1738087605,\"endTime\":1738087607},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"In an instant.\",\"startTime\":1738087607,\"endTime\":1738087609},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I like how you say that.\",\"startTime\":1738087609,\"endTime\":1738087611},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It''s made me think a lot more of GPTS as assistants. Like originally the first \",\"startTime\":1738087612,\"endTime\":1738087616},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"version of GPT was like getting a new college MIT type of graduate who came to your doorstep and wanted to work for you. And you''re like, yes, And you know, \",\"startTime\":1738087616,\"endTime\":1738087624},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"they''re all super eager about doing everything. And you''re like, yeah, yeah, \",\"startTime\":1738087624,\"endTime\":1738087628},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"just calm down a minute. I know you think you know the answers to everything, \",\"startTime\":1738087628,\"endTime\":1738087632},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"but. \",\"startTime\":1738087632,\"endTime\":1738087636},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"This is what we do here. These are called children and they need to be loved \",\"startTime\":1738087637,\"endTime\":1738087639},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"first. \",\"startTime\":1738087639,\"endTime\":1738087642},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"But in that notion of just losing my track with that, but but that as assistants, they become even more trained as we give them specialization and we give them that focus on what they should be doing. Like you mentioned last time about \",\"startTime\":1738087643,\"endTime\":1738087656},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"you were building out your own GPT specifically for task and helping to iteratively make them better and training them to be better at the process at what they''re doing. And I think. \",\"startTime\":1738087656,\"endTime\":1738087669},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"MMM.\",\"startTime\":1738087668,\"endTime\":1738087668},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"At least for me, it makes sense in my mind that the the biggest component about like ChatGPT is it''s built to chat. It''s built to have conversation. It wasn''t \",\"startTime\":1738087670,\"endTime\":1738087679},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"built on its surface level. \",\"startTime\":1738087679,\"endTime\":1738087683},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"To go in deep with things and even though we had the the plus version, which was like now having a whole fleet or a whole class of MIT graduates in your school just coming to help you out, you''re like, oh, this is awesome. You''re \",\"startTime\":1738087684,\"endTime\":1738087695},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"a specialist and everything. But even at that, having it even trained even more \",\"startTime\":1738087695,\"endTime\":1738087698},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"specifically because just being able to chat about a topic doesn''t mean that they''re able to help support you in in the needs that you have for the problems that you are working on and the solutions that you''re trying to find. I mean, \",\"startTime\":1738087698,\"endTime\":1738087710},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087709,\"endTime\":1738087711},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"they might be able to help you think it out loud. \",\"startTime\":1738087710,\"endTime\":1738087713},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And to work through those things, but when it comes to like an IEP situation for your students, it''s going to need a lot more knowledge. \",\"startTime\":1738087714,\"endTime\":1738087721},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And as you called it, an assistant, that makes my mind think so much.\",\"startTime\":1738087721,\"endTime\":1738087725},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087722,\"endTime\":1738087723},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"This metaphor of the GPT being like a new college graduate who comes in and I''ve been gung ho into this situation. I''ll help you and I''ll do all these things. \",\"startTime\":1738087726,\"endTime\":1738087733},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And Dale, have you thought about doing this? And you look at me and smile and \",\"startTime\":1738087733,\"endTime\":1738087737},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"you say. \",\"startTime\":1738087737,\"endTime\":1738087740},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Little grasshopper, you got a long ways to go, and I think that''s part of it is remembering. \",\"startTime\":1738087741,\"endTime\":1738087747},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087745,\"endTime\":1738087745},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And you''ve said it in different ways, but that these tools are trained on a knowledge base. \",\"startTime\":1738087747,\"endTime\":1738087752},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And if we''re not mindful of the knowledge base that they''re trained upon, then we''re not knowledgeable about what effectiveness they might really have or ineffectiveness that they might have. Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1738087753,\"endTime\":1738087763},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, agree. No, that''s fine.\",\"startTime\":1738087763,\"endTime\":1738087766},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh I like this conversation already. OK I''m ready for the next one. Did you \",\"startTime\":1738087767,\"endTime\":1738087770},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"have anything for me or is it the same back just till? \",\"startTime\":1738087770,\"endTime\":1738087774},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Not, not good.\",\"startTime\":1738087777,\"endTime\":1738087778},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Umm umm.\",\"startTime\":1738087783,\"endTime\":1738087784},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Oh, that''s a good question.\",\"startTime\":1738087785,\"endTime\":1738087787},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Umm.\",\"startTime\":1738087791,\"endTime\":1738087791},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"What do you call them by the way? Do you call them like a new thread or a new \",\"startTime\":1738087791,\"endTime\":1738087794},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"instance or? \",\"startTime\":1738087794,\"endTime\":1738087796},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Like, well, I just call it like a new GPT and then I give it a a certain name. \",\"startTime\":1738087797,\"endTime\":1738087802},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"And we we were joking about the names that we. \",\"startTime\":1738087802,\"endTime\":1738087807},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087805,\"endTime\":1738087807},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Not be used yet.\",\"startTime\":1738087808,\"endTime\":1738087809},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK. I think that''s the different things here. I think this question is asking \",\"startTime\":1738087808,\"endTime\":1738087811},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"like when you open up because you have a new question to ask about, do you just keep going in the same? \",\"startTime\":1738087811,\"endTime\":1738087817},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Waterfall of conversation that you already had and just ask another question Or do you open a new conversation with even the same GPT? \",\"startTime\":1738087818,\"endTime\":1738087826},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087827,\"endTime\":1738087828},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"That''s a good question. I think I grapple with this.\",\"startTime\":1738087831,\"endTime\":1738087833},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"A little bit like, oh should I be?\",\"startTime\":1738087834,\"endTime\":1738087836},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Should I be asking this this question in my speed assistant or should I be going back out and just using the the plain GPT? \",\"startTime\":1738087838,\"endTime\":1738087847},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Or should I be creating something new? Is this a focus area that''s worth me \",\"startTime\":1738087849,\"endTime\":1738087853},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"putting in time to create a new GPT? \",\"startTime\":1738087853,\"endTime\":1738087857},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Umm, so.\",\"startTime\":1738087859,\"endTime\":1738087860},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"I I think most of the time I remain in the one that I''m using. Umm.\",\"startTime\":1738087861,\"endTime\":1738087866},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So like in the same conversation with the same GPT?\",\"startTime\":1738087868,\"endTime\":1738087871},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yes.\",\"startTime\":1738087873,\"endTime\":1738087874},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Uh, you know, I say I''ve got 5 or 6 ones that are like my main.\",\"startTime\":1738087876,\"endTime\":1738087880},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"GPTS I I toggle between them if I''m trying to do a task associated to any of those, but I think my main special education assistant. \",\"startTime\":1738087881,\"endTime\":1738087891},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1738087886,\"endTime\":1738087887},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Is the one that I spend most of my time in.\",\"startTime\":1738087891,\"endTime\":1738087894},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Have you given it a name yet?\",\"startTime\":1738087895,\"endTime\":1738087896},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Well, I haven''t. It''s it''s my special Ed education assistant. I''ve just called \",\"startTime\":1738087897,\"endTime\":1738087902},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"it that. I haven''t given it any outlandish names. \",\"startTime\":1738087902,\"endTime\":1738087907},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Uh, yet, Umm.\",\"startTime\":1738087909,\"endTime\":1738087910},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah. And and yeah, I, I would say that I would probably do 75% of my time is \",\"startTime\":1738087913,\"endTime\":1738087919},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"on that particular. \",\"startTime\":1738087919,\"endTime\":1738087924},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"On that particular GPGPT and I''ve I''ve like, that was the first one I''ve created. \",\"startTime\":1738087927,\"endTime\":1738087932},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"So I''ve put a lot of time into that and I''m and I''m really happy with what that gives me. And I, I, I kind of trust that. \",\"startTime\":1738087932,\"endTime\":1738087940},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"That might sound strange, but I I kind of trust him for my.\",\"startTime\":1738087941,\"endTime\":1738087944},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Do you celebrate your anniversary dates with the with the GPT? Not quite.\",\"startTime\":1738087944,\"endTime\":1738087952},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Not quite, you know, that''s that''s the.\",\"startTime\":1738087948,\"endTime\":1738087950},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"That''s maybe another step we haven''t got to but.\",\"startTime\":1738087951,\"endTime\":1738087953},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"Yeah, certainly. I certainly have some faith in that. GPT put a lot of work \",\"startTime\":1738087955,\"endTime\":1738087957},{\"speaker\":\"11773\",\"text\":\"into it. \",\"startTime\":1738087957,\"endTime\":1738087959},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Uh, that''s cool. Umm. I I''ve been wondering about this question for a while \",\"startTime\":1738087960,\"endTime\":1738087965},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"because I noticed that at least in the past, if I keep just one thread going, I''ll I''ll call it a thread where I have a GPT open like on my computer scr