from other schools. So basically it''s around communication tools that we''re \",\"startTime\":1733842513,\"endTime\":1733842523},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"using. Liam, we just switched to a new tool called Thrill share that''s supposed \",\"startTime\":1733842523,\"endTime\":1733842528},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"to translate, but we we''re having a hell of a time getting it up and going. \",\"startTime\":1733842528,\"endTime\":1733842533},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Just because parents have to be able to log into it. And so how do you get the \",\"startTime\":1733842537,\"endTime\":1733842541},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"information pushed out and get parents signed into it and those sorts of things? \",\"startTime\":1733842541,\"endTime\":1733842545},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"That''s our big issue. But it''s supposed to translate good to almost all of our \",\"startTime\":1733842545,\"endTime\":1733842549},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"languages. \",\"startTime\":1733842549,\"endTime\":1733842552},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Do you have accurate data in your What''s your information system, power school, or? \",\"startTime\":1733842557,\"endTime\":1733842561},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Oh, what''s the other one?\",\"startTime\":1733842565,\"endTime\":1733842565},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"We''re switching to cumulative and it has been a giant disaster.\",\"startTime\":1733842566,\"endTime\":1733842570},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"It''s horrible. I I can''t even explain how it is.\",\"startTime\":1733842572,\"endTime\":1733842574},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733842575,\"endTime\":1733842575},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Awful.\",\"startTime\":1733842580,\"endTime\":1733842580},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"And the the didn''t over correctly and things are in the wrong fields and so right now. \",\"startTime\":1733842583,\"endTime\":1733842589},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yep.\",\"startTime\":1733842593,\"endTime\":1733842593},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"I''ve been, you know, I think things other than social media, but I''ve been trying to leverage my social media more and more with my Instagram account and my Facebook. \",\"startTime\":1733842597,\"endTime\":1733842606},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"That''s what I.\",\"startTime\":1733842597,\"endTime\":1733842598},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yep, we''re doing, we''re doing the 12 days of good attendance as Santa''s watching. \",\"startTime\":1733842610,\"endTime\":1733842613},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yep. \",\"startTime\":1733842613,\"endTime\":1733842617},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Increase. Oh, I love it.\",\"startTime\":1733842615,\"endTime\":1733842618},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Love it. Oh wow.\",\"startTime\":1733842620,\"endTime\":1733842622},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"My MTSS person made a whole 12 days with Flyers and then today is naughty or nice list for tardies. And if you have no tardies you''re getting a cookie delivered \",\"startTime\":1733842621,\"endTime\":1733842631},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"to a class. We have 686 kids with no tardies. \",\"startTime\":1733842631,\"endTime\":1733842636},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"So it''s all the little silly things is what we''re trying to leverage. But I \",\"startTime\":1733842641,\"endTime\":1733842644},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"don''t know if it makes a difference. Looks good on paper. \",\"startTime\":1733842644,\"endTime\":1733842648},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"I think we did. We had some friends of mine where we''re capstone doctorate program \",\"startTime\":1733842650,\"endTime\":1733842655},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"and they came in and study. \",\"startTime\":1733842655,\"endTime\":1733842660},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"I don''t have enough of those positive reinforcers, so that''s kind of cute. I \",\"startTime\":1733842666,\"endTime\":1733842669},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"like that. Oh, that''s fun. \",\"startTime\":1733842669,\"endTime\":1733842672},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yep, and then we''ll do March Madness attendance during basketball season.\",\"startTime\":1733842672,\"endTime\":1733842676},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"So about what? About once a quarter we run a positive attendance. You know, \",\"startTime\":1733842680,\"endTime\":1733842684},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"high schools, PBIS is a bad word, but PBIS ish, nerdy, cutesy, whatever you want to call it. \",\"startTime\":1733842684,\"endTime\":1733842693},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Because I I do happy texts so I can through our system text parents and I will pull just random lists of good data. And hey, your kid, you know, it has the \",\"startTime\":1733842695,\"endTime\":1733842707},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"GPA above this that''s awesome. Or your kid has this attendance or your on the \",\"startTime\":1733842707,\"endTime\":1733842713},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"list of kids that has straight A''s or just random data point. \",\"startTime\":1733842713,\"endTime\":1733842719},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"I do AI do a personal phone call to every straight A kid between now and Christmas break OK. \",\"startTime\":1733842720,\"endTime\":1733842726},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Oh.\",\"startTime\":1733842724,\"endTime\":1733842724},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"We do postcards at the Bath meet. Each staff member writes a postcard to a kid. \",\"startTime\":1733842729,\"endTime\":1733842735},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"We''re starting to collect student into our data system so that we can start texting students. \",\"startTime\":1733842735,\"endTime\":1733842745},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733842742,\"endTime\":1733842742},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Now you''re back.\",\"startTime\":1733842752,\"endTime\":1733842752},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Oh, we started calling the phone number students.\",\"startTime\":1733842753,\"endTime\":1733842757},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"All right, we''re ready for our next.\",\"startTime\":1733842762,\"endTime\":1733842765},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Yep, practical ways to involve.\",\"startTime\":1733842767,\"endTime\":1733842772},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Technology and virtual cultural relevant. What do you got for this one?\",\"startTime\":1733842784,\"endTime\":1733842790},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"So I think this is one of our holes like when we do our grade distribution pattern, our non dominant culture males are not passing at a disproportionately high rate because we don''t think they see the relevance in high school or post secondary. \",\"startTime\":1733842795,\"endTime\":1733842807},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"So we don''t have. \",\"startTime\":1733842807,\"endTime\":1733842810},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"I''m losing you. Yeah, we''re struggling with this as well. I mean, in terms of \",\"startTime\":1733842816,\"endTime\":1733842821},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"But we really see this as a hole in the unconvincing kids and parents about post secondary opportunities and lifelong impact. Good morning. \",\"startTime\":1733842819,\"endTime\":1733842829},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"we have the regular post secondary nights and curriculum nights and things like that. \",\"startTime\":1733842821,\"endTime\":1733842829},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Morning, Stephanie.\",\"startTime\":1733842833,\"endTime\":1733842834},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Virtual school tours we haven''t done that might be kind of cool. We do we''ve \",\"startTime\":1733842856,\"endTime\":1733842862},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"done parent nights utilizing some of our cultural liaisons we have we have culturally \",\"startTime\":1733842862,\"endTime\":1733842867},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"for some of our larger cultural groups and we go to our community for some of our like our King County Housing Authority development and do different things bring. \",\"startTime\":1733842867,\"endTime\":1733842884},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733842881,\"endTime\":1733842881},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Court cards, we did that last. Last. They delivered report cards. All right. \",\"startTime\":1733842891,\"endTime\":1733842894},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Want to move to the next? \",\"startTime\":1733842894,\"endTime\":1733842898},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Sure.\",\"startTime\":1733842904,\"endTime\":1733842904},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Consider tools. We have a college and career counselor that sits down with any \",\"startTime\":1733842931,\"endTime\":1733842935},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"of our families and will sit down and use translation or translation tools to work with our families one-on-one with everything from financial aid forms. \",\"startTime\":1733842935,\"endTime\":1733842944},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"We do our financial aid forms and our financial aid presentations in multiple languages. \",\"startTime\":1733842944,\"endTime\":1733842952},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Umm and we pair with like central Rendu to support our larger groups. And so \",\"startTime\":1733842961,\"endTime\":1733842966},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"in these particular cases, we would pair with like our culturally and our college and career counselor to support. \",\"startTime\":1733842966,\"endTime\":1733842978},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Our family with filling out the tool one-on-one. Oh.\",\"startTime\":1733842980,\"endTime\":1733842985},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"That I just read, Washington State Ledge is proposing no FAFSA, but you get all the financial aid from it. It broke yesterday because there''s such a low \",\"startTime\":1733842987,\"endTime\":1733842998},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"FAFSA completion rate. Ledge is looking at eliminating that barrier, guaranteeing \",\"startTime\":1733842998,\"endTime\":1733843004},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"that your sophomore year. \",\"startTime\":1733843004,\"endTime\":1733843009},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Oh, interesting.\",\"startTime\":1733843015,\"endTime\":1733843016},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733843017,\"endTime\":1733843017},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Well, you know what? For two kids this year and I''m college educated and I still \",\"startTime\":1733843018,\"endTime\":1733843021},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"cuss at the stupid thing. \",\"startTime\":1733843021,\"endTime\":1733843024},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Well, so I have.\",\"startTime\":1733843026,\"endTime\":1733843028},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"I don''t wanna over share but we have $60,000 a year in out of pocket college expenses this year and I don''t know how families would do it unless you have really good jobs because that is an entire job going to my kids. \",\"startTime\":1733843030,\"endTime\":1733843046},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I I have to put through college. I get it. Totally understand.\",\"startTime\":1733843050,\"endTime\":1733843055},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Yep, OK.\",\"startTime\":1733843056,\"endTime\":1733843057},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Next.\",\"startTime\":1733843057,\"endTime\":1733843058},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Thank you, partner.\",\"startTime\":1733843063,\"endTime\":1733843065},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Thank you. And I wrote down all sorts of ideas about your naughty and nice list \",\"startTime\":1733843064,\"endTime\":1733843069},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"and 12 days of attendance and March Madness and I like it. Oh, awesome. Which \",\"startTime\":1733843069,\"endTime\":1733843074},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"If you shoot me, if you shoot me an e-mail, I''ll send you our our 12 Days templates on Canva chris.shellin@ksd.org. \",\"startTime\":1733843071,\"endTime\":1733843082},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"school are you at? chrisksd.org. OK, got it. Thank you. \",\"startTime\":1733843074,\"endTime\":1733843080},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Kennewick School District. Yep, Yep.\",\"startTime\":1733843091,\"endTime\":1733843092},{\"speaker\":\"10899\",\"text\":\"Cool beans later.\",\"startTime\":1733843095,\"endTime\":1733843097}]"', '2025-05-08 03:17:44.154961+00', '2025-05-08 03:17:44.154961+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 762, "created_at": "2025-05-08T03:17:44.123Z", "session_title": "Family/Parental Involvement in Post-Secondary Access", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1428", "name": "Family/Parental Involvement in Post-Secondary Access", "tags": [{"name": "HSLC"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('edcb30d7-be9d-4d00-b72d-1845f0741deb', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '78010', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:40:27.163132+00', '2025-05-06 19:40:27.163132+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 303, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:40:26.947Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('b51482d3-be14-4a0d-8ab2-4a74b9798270', '6ff6d5f4-9cc6-4a8e-9c48-608201bb392d', '137087', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"I was a high school math teacher for 12 years and now I work and facilitate the professional growth of math teachers. \",\"startTime\":1739559895,\"endTime\":1739559901},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"I''m the author of The Imperfect and Unfinished Math Teacher. I''ve done a lot \",\"startTime\":1739559901,\"endTime\":1739559904},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"of lesson study and trying to get teachers to work together and be active partners in each other''s growth. \",\"startTime\":1739559904,\"endTime\":1739559910},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"And I also work for Peter Lilly Doll right now and.\",\"startTime\":1739559910,\"endTime\":1739559914},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"I''m not building thinking classrooms facilitator.\",\"startTime\":1739559915,\"endTime\":1739559917},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"Otherwise, I''m a full time nomad. I live on the road since 2020. I live out \",\"startTime\":1739559917,\"endTime\":1739559922},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"of a converted U-Haul box truck. That''s my tiny home on wheels, but it''s also \",\"startTime\":1739559922,\"endTime\":1739559927},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"a passion project of mine. It''s called the Traveling Stoop and it is a traveling \",\"startTime\":1739559927,\"endTime\":1739559932},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"porch and I like to go to gatherings and provide a space of community and storytelling. \",\"startTime\":1739559932,\"endTime\":1739559936},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"And gathering for us to be at our best as humans, which is?\",\"startTime\":1739559937,\"endTime\":1739559941},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"Listening to each other''s stories and learning from each other. Anyway, that''s \",\"startTime\":1739559942,\"endTime\":1739559945},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"a little bit about me. Thanks for listening. \",\"startTime\":1739559945,\"endTime\":1739559947},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"My thought on the role of the teacher is 2 things. It''s to understand content, \",\"startTime\":1739559982,\"endTime\":1739559985},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"but it''s also to help foster a child''s relationship with that content knowledge. \",\"startTime\":1739559985,\"endTime\":1739559989},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"Like so for example, with mathematics, we want them to learn math, but they need to be able to see themselves as math people and, and, and have a healthy relationship with mathematics, something I call a math story. And so as teachers, \",\"startTime\":1739559989,\"endTime\":1739560000},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"we work in a system that really sometimes only cares about content. And that''s \",\"startTime\":1739560000,\"endTime\":1739560004},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"something that gets in our way and needs to change. And as teachers, we need \",\"startTime\":1739560004,\"endTime\":1739560007},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"to learn to really focus on the human data. \",\"startTime\":1739560007,\"endTime\":1739560010},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"In our classrooms that.\",\"startTime\":1739560010,\"endTime\":1739560012},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"Tell us that our students are thriving and that requires us as teachers to as teachers to share authority with with our students. \",\"startTime\":1739560012,\"endTime\":1739560020},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"And elevate their voice and help them seem feel seen and valued for what they do have to offer. And the role of the learners, to be curious is to be engaged, \",\"startTime\":1739560022,\"endTime\":1739560029},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"to learn how to be patient, to learn about what they''re good at and what they need to work on. And learn about their social skills in addition to their academic \",\"startTime\":1739560029,\"endTime\":1739560036},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"skills. \",\"startTime\":1739560036,\"endTime\":1739560039},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"And they need to be as much as they can be, to be present and to be there in the moment and to be open. \",\"startTime\":1739560039,\"endTime\":1739560046},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"To learning.\",\"startTime\":1739560047,\"endTime\":1739560048},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"Yeah. So I think that''s, uh, wraps it up.\",\"startTime\":1739560050,\"endTime\":1739560053},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"My work puts me in slow. I love facilitating the learning of of adult learners \",\"startTime\":1739560074,\"endTime\":1739560078},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"and and also students like teaching puts me in the flow. \",\"startTime\":1739560078,\"endTime\":1739560082},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"Nothing, nothing makes time fly by than a good math lesson that I''m able to facilitate joy and thinking for for the humans that are in the room and so. \",\"startTime\":1739560082,\"endTime\":1739560093},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"Most of my work right now is with adult teachers and SO.\",\"startTime\":1739560093,\"endTime\":1739560096},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"And facilitating their learning. And I love that work. It puts me in the flow. \",\"startTime\":1739560100,\"endTime\":1739560104},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"Personally.\",\"startTime\":1739560104,\"endTime\":1739560105},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"Put me in the flow. I love to play chess.\",\"startTime\":1739560107,\"endTime\":1739560109},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"I will play chess a lot throughout the day, online and in person and solving puzzles and studying lessons. \",\"startTime\":1739560110,\"endTime\":1739560117},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"And so I think chess is a good example. I love driving. I would drive for countless \",\"startTime\":1739560118,\"endTime\":1739560122},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"hours and be. \",\"startTime\":1739560122,\"endTime\":1739560125},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"Pleasantly engage in my own thinking and reflection.\",\"startTime\":1739560126,\"endTime\":1739560129},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"Playing music also puts me on the flow.\",\"startTime\":1739560130,\"endTime\":1739560132},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"And playing sports and being outdoors and hiking and also.\",\"startTime\":1739560134,\"endTime\":1739560138},{\"speaker\":\"11873\",\"text\":\"Do a similar thing all right.\",\"startTime\":1739560138,\"endTime\":1739560140}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:27.847313+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:27.847313+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 207, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:27.790Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('eeffb94d-2e2d-43c4-b446-d81b49e7a5e8', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '136015', '"[{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"What a great morning.\",\"startTime\":1736261163,\"endTime\":1736261165},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Holy cow, doing the same thing you are right now. Driving. Driving somewhere. \",\"startTime\":1736261165,\"endTime\":1736261170},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Your friend driving to work.\",\"startTime\":1736261166,\"endTime\":1736261169},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Yeah, well, I''m lucky. I''m lucky because I get to have a dentist appointment \",\"startTime\":1736261170,\"endTime\":1736261174},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"this morning as I''m driving. Well, I don''t know if that''s lucky or not, but \",\"startTime\":1736261174,\"endTime\":1736261178},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"it works. It works. So happy New Year to you. \",\"startTime\":1736261178,\"endTime\":1736261182},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Isn''t that fun?\",\"startTime\":1736261178,\"endTime\":1736261179},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Same to you. I''ll tell you. Did you have a nice, nice new year, nice holiday? \",\"startTime\":1736261185,\"endTime\":1736261190},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1736261187,\"endTime\":1736261188},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Yeah. I put one on the road to college yesterday and I''m like, uh, piece of \",\"startTime\":1736261190,\"endTime\":1736261194},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You know what we did? We did. It was great when both the kids were home and \",\"startTime\":1736261192,\"endTime\":1736261197},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"my heart missing in the house again. \",\"startTime\":1736261194,\"endTime\":1736261198},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"and of course sad when they left, but we said for one of the people in our house, So actually both, actually both. But that was wonderful, wonderful time. \",\"startTime\":1736261197,\"endTime\":1736261206},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yep, Yep, we''re experiencing that now. So it''s all good, though we''ll, we''ll \",\"startTime\":1736261216,\"endTime\":1736261220},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"figure it out sooner or later, sooner or later. So you ready? That''s the next \",\"startTime\":1736261220,\"endTime\":1736261225},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, alright.\",\"startTime\":1736261225,\"endTime\":1736261226},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"one. \",\"startTime\":1736261225,\"endTime\":1736261229},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Hit next. There we go. Oh, no. Hit. Hit next. Hit next. Down below. There we \",\"startTime\":1736261232,\"endTime\":1736261237},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Ready. Alright, Favorite family?\",\"startTime\":1736261237,\"endTime\":1736261239},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"go. There we go. Awesome. This is so cool. I''m just so glad I''m getting Heidi \",\"startTime\":1736261237,\"endTime\":1736261243},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Mauer this morning. I love it, love it, love it. Hope you''re still there. You \",\"startTime\":1736261243,\"endTime\":1736261248},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"still there? OK, OK. I said no, that''s OK. I just said it''s, it''s so cool to \",\"startTime\":1736261248,\"endTime\":1736261253},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Uh, alright Valerie, I''m back. Yeah, yeah, I have a Internet dead zone on my \",\"startTime\":1736261248,\"endTime\":1736261252},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"way. How? \",\"startTime\":1736261252,\"endTime\":1736261257},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"have Heidi Meyer this morning. I''ll, I''ll read the question for you. \",\"startTime\":1736261253,\"endTime\":1736261259},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"How can schools bridge? How can schools bridge the knowledge gap for families \",\"startTime\":1736261277,\"endTime\":1736261281},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1736261279,\"endTime\":1736261279},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"unfamiliar with the high school to college or trade pipeline or pathway? \",\"startTime\":1736261281,\"endTime\":1736261285},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"We ironically, we''ve been having some conversations about we do the normal parent night and they''re inviting the the families in. But really what we''re finding \",\"startTime\":1736261297,\"endTime\":1736261307},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"is the kids get the majority of the information from the schools, not their parents. So we''re targeting the kids more than we are the families. \",\"startTime\":1736261307,\"endTime\":1736261317},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"And, you know, inviting the parents along for the ride, that really targeting the kids more than the families. \",\"startTime\":1736261322,\"endTime\":1736261328},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, right, right. Oh, I I don''t know either. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1736261324,\"endTime\":1736261331},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"I don''t know if that''s bad.\",\"startTime\":1736261330,\"endTime\":1736261331},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"But we''ve got some news. We have a weekly newsletter that goes out from our \",\"startTime\":1736261337,\"endTime\":1736261341},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"college to career counselor, and it has all the scholarships and deadlines and information. And the kids are just saying it''s so much information that it''s \",\"startTime\":1736261341,\"endTime\":1736261350},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"too much to digest. And they they were. \",\"startTime\":1736261350,\"endTime\":1736261354},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Getting it. I freeze again. I keep freezing. Internet around here is horrible. \",\"startTime\":1736261368,\"endTime\":1736261374},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Gotcha. No, we''re you''re in and out. That''s OK. Yeah. No, no, you''re Yeah, No, \",\"startTime\":1736261369,\"endTime\":1736261373},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I got that. The advisory, advisory programs. Yeah. And that and that makes sense, \",\"startTime\":1736261373,\"endTime\":1736261377},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"especially if it''s built, especially if it''s built into the school day. You \",\"startTime\":1736261377,\"endTime\":1736261382},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1736261378,\"endTime\":1736261378},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"know, I think about if if I was back in a building now and this knowledge gap for families and people unfamiliar. \",\"startTime\":1736261382,\"endTime\":1736261390},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"So so parent, so paranoid, but the kids wanted more advisory and stuff.\",\"startTime\":1736261382,\"endTime\":1736261386},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You know, it starts before high school. And how do you build a build a system \",\"startTime\":1736261399,\"endTime\":1736261404},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"that that that shares those opportunities, not just at the school setting, but community wide? How do you integrate into and use some community stakeholder \",\"startTime\":1736261404,\"endTime\":1736261414},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"organizations that interface with, with parents who may not know what''s possible for their kids? And yes, kids, kids get all the information at school and and \",\"startTime\":1736261414,\"endTime\":1736261424},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"like you said, feel inundated with some of that stuff, but is there? \",\"startTime\":1736261424,\"endTime\":1736261429},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Is there a different way to engage families, to provide some knowledge for them? \",\"startTime\":1736261429,\"endTime\":1736261433},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Because it is you''ve, you''re going through it. You''ll go through it here again. \",\"startTime\":1736261433,\"endTime\":1736261436},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"But even though I''ve worked in schools, you worked in schools, I didn''t even understand half the things that were available for my own kids. And so how do \",\"startTime\":1736261436,\"endTime\":1736261444},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"you. \",\"startTime\":1736261444,\"endTime\":1736261447},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Well, and what''s frustrating for me is the other 3 high schools have Gear up and they have College Success Foundation because they they have been granted those opportunities or they have Dream UW DreamWorks stuff and I don''t have any of that and it''s frustrating. So we just have to do it internally. \",\"startTime\":1736261447,\"endTime\":1736261468},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, right.\",\"startTime\":1736261468,\"endTime\":1736261470},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"How do they have access to that? You guys don''t? OK, gotcha, gotcha, gotcha. \",\"startTime\":1736261476,\"endTime\":1736261480},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Well at the time when district was allocating funds and stuff like that, all the other schools had lower free and reduced lunch rates and so they access to their grants and things but I didn''t have it at the time. Now I have a lower \",\"startTime\":1736261480,\"endTime\":1736261493},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Can we just say that again? It''s stupid. Should be everybody, everywhere, \",\"startTime\":1736261480,\"endTime\":1736261485},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"everything, all the time. So. \",\"startTime\":1736261485,\"endTime\":1736261489},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"free and reduced lunch rate than all the other schools except Meridian and but because of when things were allocated I don''t have access to it. Stupid. \",\"startTime\":1736261493,\"endTime\":1736261503},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, Dang it. Dang it. All right, let''s see, next question.\",\"startTime\":1736261514,\"endTime\":1736261518},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"I went back there. I went to park.\",\"startTime\":1736261523,\"endTime\":1736261524},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You went too far.\",\"startTime\":1736261525,\"endTime\":1736261526},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Partner ready. OK, so hit next again ''cause it looked like you went backwards. \",\"startTime\":1736261528,\"endTime\":1736261531},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"There we go. \",\"startTime\":1736261531,\"endTime\":1736261534},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Here we go practical ways to involve parent teacher meeting Taylor to explain post second. Oh, I got this one going on. So we have a college and career team \",\"startTime\":1736261537,\"endTime\":1736261547},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Good help me with this one.\",\"startTime\":1736261546,\"endTime\":1736261548},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"of teachers, counselors run by my assistant principal. And what we have, what \",\"startTime\":1736261547,\"endTime\":1736261552},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"we have done, we''ve done modeled it through the CCLI college Career Leadership Institute. I don''t know if you''re OK so. \",\"startTime\":1736261552,\"endTime\":1736261562},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, OK. Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1736261559,\"endTime\":1736261562},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"They they, they meet with them frequently and they they take the survey data. \",\"startTime\":1736261570,\"endTime\":1736261574},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"And then they plan everything out for the year through CCL Light using that data. They survey the kids with the kids and they use that data to plan our \",\"startTime\":1736261574,\"endTime\":1736261584},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"college career works for the year. And every staff meeting we have a college \",\"startTime\":1736261584,\"endTime\":1736261589},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1736261587,\"endTime\":1736261588},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"and career moment. And what it what it is intended to do is build a capacity \",\"startTime\":1736261589,\"endTime\":1736261594},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"of our teachers and our staff. So not just my teachers, the entire staff. So \",\"startTime\":1736261594,\"endTime\":1736261599},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"yeah, classified staff, para educators. \",\"startTime\":1736261599,\"endTime\":1736261604},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"The entire staff, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1736261604,\"endTime\":1736261605},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Everyone to understand financial planning pieces.\",\"startTime\":1736261609,\"endTime\":1736261615},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"All of everything in terms of post secondary education and it''s grounded in the data of what we know, what we don''t know, what kids need us to know, what kids are seeing and not seeing. So we have these CCLI moments and it can be \",\"startTime\":1736261616,\"endTime\":1736261631},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"everything from do you understand internships and apprenticeships? Do you know \",\"startTime\":1736261631,\"endTime\":1736261636},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"where to find information? Do you understand how to fill out the the financial \",\"startTime\":1736261636,\"endTime\":1736261640},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1736261639,\"endTime\":1736261640},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"aid form? And So what we''re finding is by giving small. \",\"startTime\":1736261640,\"endTime\":1736261645},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Pieces of information that are digestible consistently every staff meeting that we''re really building the capacity across the entire building around. \",\"startTime\":1736261648,\"endTime\":1736261658},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"People understanding information and then what we''re seeing is that they''re then passing that information on to parents, students and and building then their capacity to mentor the students and the parents. \",\"startTime\":1736261660,\"endTime\":1736261676},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"On the kids, yeah, right, right. I love that. I love that. You know, you think \",\"startTime\":1736261667,\"endTime\":1736261672},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"about I''ve heard this before 7 * 7 different ways and even though it''s a little different knowledge, but you''re ingraining the post secondary process or you know, I heard about that sometime I want to go talk to so and so I think they know a lot about that or, or whatever and, and. \",\"startTime\":1736261672,\"endTime\":1736261688},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That''s awesome. That''s awesome. How long have you guys been doing that?\",\"startTime\":1736261697,\"endTime\":1736261701},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"About six years now, yeah. And so we''re really building that, that capacity. \",\"startTime\":1736261705,\"endTime\":1736261710},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Six years now, OK.\",\"startTime\":1736261706,\"endTime\":1736261707},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"We talk about T4 that everyone needs to have graduate to something. \",\"startTime\":1736261710,\"endTime\":1736261715},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, right.\",\"startTime\":1736261713,\"endTime\":1736261715},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"And graduating to technical school two year, 4 year and those pieces. Where \",\"startTime\":1736261719,\"endTime\":1736261723},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"we''re really struggling, though, is getting kids to fill out the financial aid form. And I have my principal Advisory Council. The other day I shared with \",\"startTime\":1736261723,\"endTime\":1736261732},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right.\",\"startTime\":1736261730,\"endTime\":1736261730},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"my kids some data. I have the lowest secondary enrollment rate of all the schools \",\"startTime\":1736261732,\"endTime\":1736261736},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"in Kent. \",\"startTime\":1736261736,\"endTime\":1736261741},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"And I gave the data to my students. I said why? And it was really interesting. \",\"startTime\":1736261745,\"endTime\":1736261750},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"OK, Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1736261745,\"endTime\":1736261747},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"They said we''re poor and we can''t go to school and we don''t find out about financial aid until our junior, senior year. At that point in time, it''s too late. We''ve \",\"startTime\":1736261750,\"endTime\":1736261760},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"kind of written off college. And so if you gave us that information our freshman \",\"startTime\":1736261760,\"endTime\":1736261764},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"year, we won''t have written it out. It kind of predetermined our path so early \",\"startTime\":1736261764,\"endTime\":1736261769},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"in our high school career, and we think we would apply. \",\"startTime\":1736261769,\"endTime\":1736261774},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"And, and reroute our, our, our goals differently. And so it''s really important \",\"startTime\":1736261779,\"endTime\":1736261784},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right. Yeah. Aren''t kids awesome?\",\"startTime\":1736261782,\"endTime\":1736261785},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"information that they were sharing with me. I love them. Oh my God, My principal \",\"startTime\":1736261784,\"endTime\":1736261789},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Advisory Council is incredible. Yeah, exactly. \",\"startTime\":1736261789,\"endTime\":1736261794},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, aren''t they awesome? You know? Yeah. You know, if you gave this information \",\"startTime\":1736261794,\"endTime\":1736261798},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"to me sooner, I might know it was possible and I might do something about it. \",\"startTime\":1736261798,\"endTime\":1736261803},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh, gosh. Oh, all right.\",\"startTime\":1736261807,\"endTime\":1736261810},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Let''s see next one.\",\"startTime\":1736261811,\"endTime\":1736261812},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Read the scenario yeah here mentoring program.\",\"startTime\":1736261818,\"endTime\":1736261822},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That never happens.\",\"startTime\":1736261827,\"endTime\":1736261828},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Yeah, we don''t have a pure mentoring program. Well, we have an amazing individual \",\"startTime\":1736261840,\"endTime\":1736261844},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"from Central Rendu who is in our school full time and she she supports our Spanish speaking families. \",\"startTime\":1736261844,\"endTime\":1736261853},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"So the.\",\"startTime\":1736261845,\"endTime\":1736261846},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Parents, multilingual students feel overwhelmed by the information by that school post secondary options and financial aid like translation services. \",\"startTime\":1736261850,\"endTime\":1736261857},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Thinking you know that is it.\",\"startTime\":1736261862,\"endTime\":1736261864},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Huge obstacle, you know, unless you have the resources to. When I was in Centralia, \",\"startTime\":1736261864,\"endTime\":1736261867},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"we had. \",\"startTime\":1736261867,\"endTime\":1736261871},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"An individual that handled migrant families and, and, or our bilingual populations and we worked pretty hard to at the, at the high school level to, you know, translate resources and everything else like that. But that individual was, \",\"startTime\":1736261873,\"endTime\":1736261887},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"was the conduit to the families because of maybe some of the language barriers and, and, or being first Gen. to go and so. \",\"startTime\":1736261887,\"endTime\":1736261897},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"That''s where some of the other opportunities like College Success Foundation and and some other stakeholder groups have have some amazing resources to be able to help with that. But this is a, this is a tough one. This is a tough \",\"startTime\":1736261897,\"endTime\":1736261907},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"one. \",\"startTime\":1736261907,\"endTime\":1736261911},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"And so she''ll sit down and help them fill out the FAFSA or the WAFA. And I also \",\"startTime\":1736261924,\"endTime\":1736261930},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Yeah, OK.\",\"startTime\":1736261928,\"endTime\":1736261930},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"have communities and communities and schools and I''ve 2 liaisons, 1 is Afghani and one is Ukrainian. And those are two of my strongest new immigrant populations. \",\"startTime\":1736261930,\"endTime\":1736261941},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"And so they also are supporting in that work. So we have a lot of. \",\"startTime\":1736261941,\"endTime\":1736261947},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Affinity type. Is that the right term? Affinity type groups. We also have a \",\"startTime\":1736261951,\"endTime\":1736261954},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Right. Yeah, that work, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1736261954,\"endTime\":1736261956},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Native American liaison. \",\"startTime\":1736261954,\"endTime\":1736261958},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"So these liaisons are helping with specific populations of students. And so \",\"startTime\":1736261960,\"endTime\":1736261966},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1736261961,\"endTime\":1736261961},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"oftentimes we will connect students with these particular groups. But we also \",\"startTime\":1736261966,\"endTime\":1736261971},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"have 138 different languages. So I mean that can only go, yeah, 138. So that \",\"startTime\":1736261971,\"endTime\":1736261977},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"can only go, that only goes so far. So if we can, we connect with an affinity \",\"startTime\":1736261977,\"endTime\":1736261982},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Jeez, so far.\",\"startTime\":1736261979,\"endTime\":1736261982},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"or a liaison the other times our college and career. \",\"startTime\":1736261982,\"endTime\":1736261988},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Counselor will sit down with either our translation, our language line.\",\"startTime\":1736261994,\"endTime\":1736261998},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"On a regular basis or our translation services and we''ll sit one-on-one with a kid and a family on a regular basis and fill that out. That happens quite \",\"startTime\":1736261999,\"endTime\":1736262008},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"a bit. Our counselors do the same thing. I will use student leaders that will \",\"startTime\":1736262008,\"endTime\":1736262013},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"help as well. \",\"startTime\":1736262013,\"endTime\":1736262017},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Did I freeze again?\",\"startTime\":1736262024,\"endTime\":1736262025},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"OK, Yeah, good. I think the more you can get the students involved, maybe there''s \",\"startTime\":1736262025,\"endTime\":1736262029},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"past students that if you know where they are and if they''re kind of local to help bridge that gap for for some kids as well. \",\"startTime\":1736262029,\"endTime\":1736262036},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"But let''s see, I don''t want to rush, rush along here, but I''ve got to head into the dentist office right now, so we''ll go to the next. Oh, look at that. Thank \",\"startTime\":1736262037,\"endTime\":1736262044},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"you, partner. Gosh Dang it. You know what? This just puts a smile on my face. \",\"startTime\":1736262044,\"endTime\":1736262047},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Sorry.\",\"startTime\":1736262046,\"endTime\":1736262046},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Heidi Maurer, I''m not going to lie to you. Puts a big smile on my face seeing \",\"startTime\":1736262047,\"endTime\":1736262051},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"you this morning. \",\"startTime\":1736262051,\"endTime\":1736262054},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"That''s, hey, I gotta tell you, the last couple of Tuesdays I''ve started my morning with Chris Shellin and the two of us have really enjoyed, yes, starting our mornings on Tuesdays together. It''s been really insightful. It''s been awesome. \",\"startTime\":1736262054,\"endTime\":1736262068},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Oh yeah. Wait a minute. No, nobody ever says that about Chris. So I''m glad to \",\"startTime\":1736262064,\"endTime\":1736262067},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"hear that. You know, I''ve known him for a long time. Yep. No, I''ve known him \",\"startTime\":1736262067,\"endTime\":1736262071},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"for a long time and I''m glad he''s hopping on ''cause he was one of them. That \",\"startTime\":1736262071,\"endTime\":1736262075},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"Hey hey, I''ve been learning a lot.\",\"startTime\":1736262073,\"endTime\":1736262076},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"was like, I hate this technology stuff and staring at myself on the screen, I''m not doing this. So I''m glad he''s on. That''s awesome. \",\"startTime\":1736262075,\"endTime\":1736262083},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"He''s been on and then the conversations have actually spilled over into emails and sharing resources and things like that. So kudos to this little project \",\"startTime\":1736262086,\"endTime\":1736262094},{\"speaker\":\"10902\",\"text\":\"of yours is actually working really well. \",\"startTime\":1736262094,\"endTime\":1736262098},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Way cool.\",\"startTime\":1736262094,\"endTime\":1736262095},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Cool, cool. Well, you have a wonderful, wonderful day.\",\"startTime\":1736262100,\"endTime\":1736262104}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.203828+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.203828+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 958, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:28.141Z", "session_title": "Family/Parental Involvement in Post-Secondary Access", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1428", "name": "Family/Parental Involvement in Post-Secondary Access", "tags": [{"name": "HSLC"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('10262415-5946-4b48-a18d-c3a53c961ba9', 'f75f7f16-84b9-41ce-b842-2a77a9dd70b8', '54371', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:40:30.905713+00', '2025-05-06 19:40:30.905713+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 656, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:40:30.859Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('cdc91fe0-c65c-4ded-84b0-eb132898f353', '72766e2f-2bb1-4be6-85a2-718e55325f8a', '134636', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Hi, what?\",\"startTime\":1732054733,\"endTime\":1732054734},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Oh, there you go.\",\"startTime\":1732054734,\"endTime\":1732054735},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"That''s a really weird. OK, so a fun fact about myself.\",\"startTime\":1732054738,\"endTime\":1732054742},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"I run 2 marathons. Thank you. Thank you. OK, well, what''s a fun fact about you \",\"startTime\":1732054743,\"endTime\":1732054747},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Good job, good for you. I have not ran a marathon and I don''t plan on it, so \",\"startTime\":1732054746,\"endTime\":1732054749},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"then? \",\"startTime\":1732054747,\"endTime\":1732054750},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"that''s all. \",\"startTime\":1732054749,\"endTime\":1732054752},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Fun fact, let''s see, I''ve I''ve been to a lot of different islands on the Caribbean on cruise boats. Yeah, OK. \",\"startTime\":1732054756,\"endTime\":1732054767},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"Nice. OK, great. That''s way more fun than mine anyways. OK, so do we go next \",\"startTime\":1732054766,\"endTime\":1732054769},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"now? OK. \",\"startTime\":1732054769,\"endTime\":1732054772},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"I think so.\",\"startTime\":1732054772,\"endTime\":1732054772},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"All right, what makes you an effective leader?\",\"startTime\":1732054777,\"endTime\":1732054778},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Go for it, OK?\",\"startTime\":1732054781,\"endTime\":1732054782},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"I Oh, yeah, you go first. No, you go for it.\",\"startTime\":1732054781,\"endTime\":1732054784},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"I think I value relationships and.\",\"startTime\":1732054786,\"endTime\":1732054789},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Really care about my staff and my students. And so I listen. I''m patient.\",\"startTime\":1732054792,\"endTime\":1732054796},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I think that''s what it is.\",\"startTime\":1732054799,\"endTime\":1732054800},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I would say that, you know, we talked yesterday about the three different domains and I think that culture is something that comes super easy to me and learning is really the one that I lean into the most. And so I just think that \",\"startTime\":1732054801,\"endTime\":1732054812},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"I can relate to people, can understand people, can have empathy for people. \",\"startTime\":1732054812,\"endTime\":1732054816},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"And that''s really why I got into education and and what makes me effective at my job too. \",\"startTime\":1732054816,\"endTime\":1732054824},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Thanks. Excellent.\",\"startTime\":1732054827,\"endTime\":1732054828},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"All right, next. OK, so for me, I just moved districts this year. I''m not sure \",\"startTime\":1732054829,\"endTime\":1732054833},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Next.\",\"startTime\":1732054830,\"endTime\":1732054830},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"that I''m loving it. They have a lot of structures in place, which is great, \",\"startTime\":1732054833,\"endTime\":1732054837},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"The next goal in your leadership journey? OK, go ahead.\",\"startTime\":1732054833,\"endTime\":1732054838},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"but they also expect you to kind of operate like a Barbie within their system. \",\"startTime\":1732054837,\"endTime\":1732054841},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"And so truthfully, I don''t know. I am feeling like I know it''s only November, \",\"startTime\":1732054841,\"endTime\":1732054845},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"but I''m already at a crossroads. So it''s like, really, what comes next doesn''t \",\"startTime\":1732054845,\"endTime\":1732054850},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"mean moving levels to middle school to high school doesn''t mean moving districts going back to my district going to. \",\"startTime\":1732054850,\"endTime\":1732054858},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"Another district going to work with that guy who presented to us this morning. \",\"startTime\":1732054865,\"endTime\":1732054869},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"You know, like I don''t. I''m not really sure what my next step is. So crossroads. \",\"startTime\":1732054869,\"endTime\":1732054873},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Hey, that''s tough. That is tough. You know, I think my next goal is to improve \",\"startTime\":1732054873,\"endTime\":1732054880},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"on I think critical conversations more quickly and. \",\"startTime\":1732054880,\"endTime\":1732054888},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Taken advantage of of of the support that I have to really allow me to do that so. \",\"startTime\":1732054894,\"endTime\":1732054900},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"Yep. All right. Let''s see you next.\",\"startTime\":1732054905,\"endTime\":1732054908},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Good.\",\"startTime\":1732054907,\"endTime\":1732054908},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"OK, strength of your school''s culture. Well, this year we have put a huge emphasis \",\"startTime\":1732054911,\"endTime\":1732054917},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"on more celebrations and so we we celebrate our staff every Friday with Flamingo Friday. It''s kind of a weird, funky thing, but it started a couple years ago \",\"startTime\":1732054917,\"endTime\":1732054928},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"and we have just. \",\"startTime\":1732054928,\"endTime\":1732054933},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Kind of went overboard, maybe not overboard, but we''re definitely taking it up a couple notches. And so the kid, the parents are sorry. The staff really \",\"startTime\":1732054937,\"endTime\":1732054943},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"have a great time with that. \",\"startTime\":1732054943,\"endTime\":1732054945},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Umm, and then we''re also, we didn''t really have a good system on celebrating students a ton and intentional. So we doing student of the month and having \",\"startTime\":1732054947,\"endTime\":1732054956},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"assemblies and getting them little prizes and things like that. So, so yeah, \",\"startTime\":1732054956,\"endTime\":1732054961},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"I think our school culture is growing and not where it needs to be, but we''re we''re getting there. So pretty proud of that. \",\"startTime\":1732054961,\"endTime\":1732054971},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"Yeah. For us, I think like kind of like a reference before us, we have a lot \",\"startTime\":1732054973,\"endTime\":1732054977},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"of structures in place. So like teams, when they meet, no matter like what team \",\"startTime\":1732054977,\"endTime\":1732054981},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"it is, they''ll start with the purpose of their meeting and their norms and their norm facilitator and they have consensus voting and they have roles. And so \",\"startTime\":1732054981,\"endTime\":1732054989},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"like something about our culture that''s really strong is that we kind of know how it should operate, right, And whether that feels authentic or. \",\"startTime\":1732054989,\"endTime\":1732054997},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"Whatnot. That''s kind of, you know, where I struggle, but.\",\"startTime\":1732054999,\"endTime\":1732055002},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"Lots of structures in place to help support like what it should look like, what PLC should look like. Yeah, right. An area of work regarding school culture \",\"startTime\":1732055003,\"endTime\":1732055015},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055006,\"endTime\":1732055006},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Interesting.\",\"startTime\":1732055009,\"endTime\":1732055010},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1732055014,\"endTime\":1732055014},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"would probably just be like making that that''s like I said, make me more authentic, encouraging, more innovation, encouraging differences of thought, encouraging. \",\"startTime\":1732055015,\"endTime\":1732055026},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"Shared ownership.\",\"startTime\":1732055034,\"endTime\":1732055034},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"MMM yeah, I think for for me is trying to inspire people to.\",\"startTime\":1732055036,\"endTime\":1732055043},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Take a take an idea and roll with it. You know, they have a thought or an idea \",\"startTime\":1732055048,\"endTime\":1732055052},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"of what they would like to do and they, you know, they, they send it to us and we, it''s like, hey, that''s a great idea. Go for it. Like you go do that. That''s \",\"startTime\":1732055052,\"endTime\":1732055060},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"awesome. So I think it''s trying to. \",\"startTime\":1732055060,\"endTime\":1732055063},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Help support when staff bring those ideas forward and so that it''s not always coming from 1 area, it''s coming throughout the school. \",\"startTime\":1732055066,\"endTime\":1732055076},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055076,\"endTime\":1732055076},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"All right, let''s see last time. Oh, thank your partner. One thing you learned \",\"startTime\":1732055079,\"endTime\":1732055083},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"from him. I love the idea of Flamingo Friday and like celebrating like an intentional \",\"startTime\":1732055083,\"endTime\":1732055087},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"way every week, like having a repeated structure that you just come back to, but that is in there for positives and for celebrations. Thanks. I appreciate \",\"startTime\":1732055087,\"endTime\":1732055096},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah. Well, thank you. And I think you really trying to embed that authenticity \",\"startTime\":1732055096,\"endTime\":1732055100},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"that it doesn''t feel it feels awkward, especially being the new guy, but I''m like, you know what? I only am who I am so. \",\"startTime\":1732055096,\"endTime\":1732055104},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"into your, your everyday stuff is, is huge. I, I, I think the structures are \",\"startTime\":1732055100,\"endTime\":1732055104},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"there for a good reason, but I also think that it needs to be authentic and not just checking the box. And so I, I appreciate your courage and, and taking \",\"startTime\":1732055104,\"endTime\":1732055113},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"that on. \",\"startTime\":1732055113,\"endTime\":1732055118},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"You know I''m in a special against your system a little bit and see if we can continue to be a fit but. \",\"startTime\":1732055127,\"endTime\":1732055132},{\"speaker\":\"11337\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1732055129,\"endTime\":1732055129},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Oh well, it''s really nice to meet you. This is fun. OK, Have a good one. \",\"startTime\":1732055136,\"endTime\":1732055139},{\"speaker\":\"11319\",\"text\":\"Bye. \",\"startTime\":1732055139,\"endTime\":1732055142}]"', '2025-05-08 03:17:46.625637+00', '2025-05-08 03:17:46.625637+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 414, "created_at": "2025-05-08T03:17:46.596Z", "session_title": "School Leadership: Describing the Work(BEL LSL)", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1416", "name": "School Leadership: Describing the Work(BEL LSL)", "tags": [{"name": "BEL"}, {"name": "LSL"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('863ea133-f2a2-4aa9-9a29-56f71c327204', '760ebb56-9a35-4b72-8b73-bc98a5f056a3', '114736', '"[]"', '2025-05-08 03:18:04.539327+00', '2025-05-08 03:18:04.539327+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 15, "created_at": "2025-05-08T03:18:04.519Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('8b5cbc9a-307d-4687-8985-ed5d6b38c92d', '713b8455-cc3b-4ab1-bcfb-255f93bf56b0', '81186', '"[]"', '2025-05-06 19:40:26.974077+00', '2025-05-06 19:40:26.974077+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 282, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:40:26.915Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('ade72e21-9f1a-4a38-9c83-d88d0bc43920', '4734e9cf-74b7-4e89-b92c-8dc6f49c5b2a', '135593', '"[{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Really. Misplaced fears. Educators might have been using work AI tools. Yeah, \",\"startTime\":1733844741,\"endTime\":1733844744},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I think some of the misplaced fears are, are cheating. I mean, it''s a low, you \",\"startTime\":1733844744,\"endTime\":1733844748},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"know, think very hard about that one, you know, cheating. \",\"startTime\":1733844748,\"endTime\":1733844752},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You know, skating on assignments and bunch of other things like that. The real \",\"startTime\":1733844758,\"endTime\":1733844760},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"fears. \",\"startTime\":1733844760,\"endTime\":1733844763},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I don''t know I I truly don''t and maybe that''s just because I feel so confident and or positive about it. \",\"startTime\":1733844766,\"endTime\":1733844772},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I think maybe some of the real fears can be found in.\",\"startTime\":1733844774,\"endTime\":1733844778},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"I don''t know, using it for not good purposes. So, so there''s some, you know, \",\"startTime\":1733844782,\"endTime\":1733844786},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"there could be some fears around that like some of the real fears around around taking positions or jobs away from people. I think that''s misplaced as well. \",\"startTime\":1733844786,\"endTime\":1733844795},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It''s if you don''t use it, yeah, you''re going to be misplaced or or not very efficient find something. But I think overall. \",\"startTime\":1733844795,\"endTime\":1733844804},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You can mitigate all of all of those pieces.\",\"startTime\":1733844808,\"endTime\":1733844810},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"In terms of research, it hasn''t been like research project or anything else like that has just been reading that I''ve done listening to other people talk, listening to keynote people, so on and so forth. So we talk about the bias that \",\"startTime\":1733844833,\"endTime\":1733844846},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"they have models and ChatGPT or just GPTS in general. Yes, they''re they''re clear \",\"startTime\":1733844846,\"endTime\":1733844850},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"and they''re evident. If you''re not careful in terms of crafting a prompt, you \",\"startTime\":1733844850,\"endTime\":1733844854},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"can certainly get information back that. \",\"startTime\":1733844854,\"endTime\":1733844859},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Is slanted one way, slanted another way.\",\"startTime\":1733844860,\"endTime\":1733844862},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Does not take into account race or equity.\",\"startTime\":1733844863,\"endTime\":1733844866},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Kind of access and opportunity pieces.\",\"startTime\":1733844868,\"endTime\":1733844870},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"It''s it. It is gotten better over time, but I think it''s more about a human \",\"startTime\":1733844871,\"endTime\":1733844877},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"engagement interaction and inquiry piece where you have to be cognizantly aware of a prompt and how it might lean into some of the biases that can be demonstrated and shown in GPT answers. \",\"startTime\":1733844877,\"endTime\":1733844893},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"You know, I think the, the most important thing here in terms of content that shows bias in your classroom is, is calling it and naming it, recognizing it and utilize it as a, as a teaching opportunity for kids. And how would you respond? \",\"startTime\":1733844918,\"endTime\":1733844930},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"How could you do something differently? How can we change the results up so \",\"startTime\":1733844930,\"endTime\":1733844934},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"we can remove the bias? I just think it''s critically important that we that \",\"startTime\":1733844934,\"endTime\":1733844938},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"we respond to those things when we see them and we give them permission as teachers or school leaders. \",\"startTime\":1733844938,\"endTime\":1733844946},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"To respond when we recognize inherent bias, or especially explicit bias, that just pops up. It''s just there. We have to name it, talk about it. \",\"startTime\":1733844949,\"endTime\":1733844961},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"Because that will better equip our kids, but it also better equip ourselves to handle the conversations. Along with this, again, it''ll better equip our \",\"startTime\":1733844963,\"endTime\":1733844971},{\"speaker\":\"8437\",\"text\":\"kids to be able to recognize and respond appropriately when they''re not in the classroom and have dialogue and discussion and be open about it, be civil about it. So anyway, just those pieces. \",\"startTime\":1733844971,\"endTime\":1733844983}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.023285+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.023285+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 223, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:27.964Z", "session_title": "Navigating AI Responsibly", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1320", "name": "Navigating AI Responsibly", "tags": [{"name": "AI in Education"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('d066bf66-6c03-4412-be90-1e4ab8440574', '0c6c53a9-c040-411d-a09e-ba80b8419d9e', '135591', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Good morning. Good. How are you?\",\"startTime\":1733844518,\"endTime\":1733844520},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Hi, how are you? Good. I''m gonna try this on my way to work. We''ll see how this \",\"startTime\":1733844518,\"endTime\":1733844521},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"goes. \",\"startTime\":1733844521,\"endTime\":1733844523},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''ve done this twice and the last time somebody was driving too so.\",\"startTime\":1733844523,\"endTime\":1733844527},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"I mean, it told me not to drive, but it''s not very far.\",\"startTime\":1733844527,\"endTime\":1733844530},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''m sure you''ll be fine.\",\"startTime\":1733844532,\"endTime\":1733844532},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"My name is Mallory Wilson. I am an assistant principal at Olympia High School. \",\"startTime\":1733844535,\"endTime\":1733844539},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh, cool. OK. \",\"startTime\":1733844539,\"endTime\":1733844542},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Oh, I''m Sarah Rubenstein and I''m a principal at AK12 school in Port Townsend. \",\"startTime\":1733844542,\"endTime\":1733844547},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"All right. Should we move on to the next one?\",\"startTime\":1733844552,\"endTime\":1733844553},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"All right. So do you want me to read the questions as you''re driving, like once \",\"startTime\":1733844563,\"endTime\":1733844565},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"you start driving, OK. \",\"startTime\":1733844565,\"endTime\":1733844568},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Yeah, that''d be good.\",\"startTime\":1733844568,\"endTime\":1733844569},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Let''s see here. What systems do you have in place to help students pursue post \",\"startTime\":1733844571,\"endTime\":1733844573},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"secondary education? \",\"startTime\":1733844573,\"endTime\":1733844576},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Then ask your partner, do you want to go first?\",\"startTime\":1733844577,\"endTime\":1733844580},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I''ll go first while my car is warming up and clearing the windshield. \",\"startTime\":1733844580,\"endTime\":1733844584},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"I would say it''s something that we''re really like working on. \",\"startTime\":1733844584,\"endTime\":1733844587},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Like my school''s like an alternative high school. So like I would say we, you \",\"startTime\":1733844589,\"endTime\":1733844593},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"know, we have a counselor who does some counseling with them, but we just started. \",\"startTime\":1733844593,\"endTime\":1733844597},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"A grant program with College Success Foundation and so they are going to be able to be in our school a few days a month and I think we really want to like work on students who like want to try some, you know, not just like 4 year, 2 year college kind of post secondary things like. \",\"startTime\":1733844599,\"endTime\":1733844613},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"You know, for my students, so I''m, you know, hopeful to see how that will work and someone who''s a little bit more connected and knowing what all those programs are for a student based on their interest. \",\"startTime\":1733844614,\"endTime\":1733844624},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, this is only my second year in high school, so I feel like everything last year was like new and I was learning. One of the great things that I oversee \",\"startTime\":1733844624,\"endTime\":1733844634},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"though is our counseling team. And so we''ve got 5 counselors cause we''ve got \",\"startTime\":1733844634,\"endTime\":1733844640},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"about 2000 students and so. \",\"startTime\":1733844640,\"endTime\":1733844645},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I think that there''s been in our enrollment luckily went up this year. We were \",\"startTime\":1733844647,\"endTime\":1733844652},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"in, we were in a budget crisis last year and then we were told like except everybody. \",\"startTime\":1733844652,\"endTime\":1733844656},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"So we are like keeping our district afloat right now. Our high school is, but \",\"startTime\":1733844657,\"endTime\":1733844661},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"one of the things that we''re seeing an uptick in is number of kids that want to go to trade programs, you know, next year. And so we''ve got a really great \",\"startTime\":1733844661,\"endTime\":1733844669},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"college and career counselor who''s incredibly like connected to the students and. \",\"startTime\":1733844669,\"endTime\":1733844677},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"She really highlighted at graduation last year the number of students that received scholarships for programs kind of after. \",\"startTime\":1733844678,\"endTime\":1733844686},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"After high school that were more into the trades. So we also partner with the \",\"startTime\":1733844687,\"endTime\":1733844691},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Tumwater School District and send our students to Newmarket Skill Center. And \",\"startTime\":1733844691,\"endTime\":1733844695},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"so a lot of students can get like apprenticeships right out of out of high school if they choose to do that. I feel like it''s a little daunting though ''cause \",\"startTime\":1733844695,\"endTime\":1733844704},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"some students that just have like no idea what they want to do until they are gone. So that kind of bums me out, ''cause I don''t I don''t know that we''re doing \",\"startTime\":1733844704,\"endTime\":1733844713},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"much of A service to them, but. \",\"startTime\":1733844713,\"endTime\":1733844717},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Umm, yeah. I don''t, I don''t think that we have a ton of options other than two \",\"startTime\":1733844718,\"endTime\":1733844723},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"year, 4 year, and then kind of a trade program. I was talking to our special \",\"startTime\":1733844723,\"endTime\":1733844727},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Ed director yesterday though, about how if I was ever a special Ed director, which I do not want to be, but I would really want to do like a para Academy so that students could receive like credit if they wanted it to. \",\"startTime\":1733844727,\"endTime\":1733844740},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"College credit if they wanted, but then they could graduate from high school with their para certificate and have passed the skills test. And then we could \",\"startTime\":1733844743,\"endTime\":1733844750},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"hire them right out of high school because we were, we have such a Paris shortage. \",\"startTime\":1733844750,\"endTime\":1733844754},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Oh, that''s, that''s such a smart idea. No, like I had a couple students who graduated \",\"startTime\":1733844754,\"endTime\":1733844758},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"last year and they were kind of interested in like childcare and they did like a senior project like in our kindergarten classrooms. And I like, I know they \",\"startTime\":1733844758,\"endTime\":1733844766},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"had no plan. And I''m like, why didn''t we get this student ready to be a parent \",\"startTime\":1733844766,\"endTime\":1733844770},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm. Yeah. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733844770,\"endTime\":1733844773},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"educator for us so that that''s a smart idea. Like, could we just help them be \",\"startTime\":1733844770,\"endTime\":1733844774},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"ready to pass that skills test? Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733844774,\"endTime\":1733844778},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right. Exactly. And then like guarantee them an interview, like maybe not guarantee \",\"startTime\":1733844777,\"endTime\":1733844781},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"them a job, but guarantee them an interview and part of their you know like internship their senior year could be working with students in resource or like the early childhood or things like that. So. \",\"startTime\":1733844781,\"endTime\":1733844792},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Yeah, no, that''s a fun idea. I''m like, well, if you can make it to an interview \",\"startTime\":1733844793,\"endTime\":1733844796},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"for our pair of jobs, we usually give you the job. \",\"startTime\":1733844796,\"endTime\":1733844798},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, same. Sometimes we''re like, hey, pending references, do you want this \",\"startTime\":1733844799,\"endTime\":1733844802},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"position like before they leave? \",\"startTime\":1733844802,\"endTime\":1733844805},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Right, right.\",\"startTime\":1733844806,\"endTime\":1733844806},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"All right, should we go to the next one?\",\"startTime\":1733844807,\"endTime\":1733844809},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733844809,\"endTime\":1733844809},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"All right, take turn sharing. What challenges do you face in assisting your \",\"startTime\":1733844811,\"endTime\":1733844816},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"students with post secondary goals And then press more for ideas. \",\"startTime\":1733844816,\"endTime\":1733844820},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Well, I think that the like high school and beyond plan has good intentions. \",\"startTime\":1733844825,\"endTime\":1733844829},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I just think that I mean, I personally, I, I went to a four year college right after high school and I didn''t feel like I knew what I wanted to do and I ended up majoring in something that I had nothing to do with. \",\"startTime\":1733844829,\"endTime\":1733844842},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"In the end, you know, my parents were like just graduate, get the diploma and then figure it out after. So hopefully the high school and beyond plan is helping \",\"startTime\":1733844843,\"endTime\":1733844853},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"students because I didn''t have that when I was went through the system. But \",\"startTime\":1733844853,\"endTime\":1733844858},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"if if nothing else, it like works on you building your resume and thinking about it before it''s happened. So other than that, though, I''m not really, I''m not \",\"startTime\":1733844858,\"endTime\":1733844868},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"really sure I think if if a kid has a plan. \",\"startTime\":1733844868,\"endTime\":1733844873},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"We do a much better job of trying to assist them and whatever that that plan or goal is, it''s harder for the kids that are just like, I don''t know or aren''t really motivated to figure it out. \",\"startTime\":1733844873,\"endTime\":1733844883},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Yeah, and I think here in Port Townsend, like all of that is true for us too. \",\"startTime\":1733844884,\"endTime\":1733844888},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"So I guess that''s pretty universal. But like here in Port Townsend, I also feel \",\"startTime\":1733844888,\"endTime\":1733844891},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"like just like the sense of what your opportunities are feels pretty limited for high school students. Like, like the only jobs they really know like that \",\"startTime\":1733844891,\"endTime\":1733844897},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"they can imagine are all service industry jobs, because that''s like that''s those are the only jobs really teens. \",\"startTime\":1733844897,\"endTime\":1733844904},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Get around here at all like and like even working at Safeway sometimes it''s like out of reach for some of our teens. Like so like, I think just really that''s \",\"startTime\":1733844906,\"endTime\":1733844913},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"our biggest challenge is like helping them see some spectrum of jobs beyond like just what they can see here in our little town. And there''s like, right, \",\"startTime\":1733844913,\"endTime\":1733844921},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733844919,\"endTime\":1733844920},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"there''s lots of jobs you can do, but you might not do them in Port Townsend. \",\"startTime\":1733844921,\"endTime\":1733844924},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"So how do we help them like have that sense of outside of this community a little bit? \",\"startTime\":1733844924,\"endTime\":1733844932},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"And like, I feel like, how do we help them see what like the differences between a job that offers like some like opportunity for growth for them maybe with only minimal training versus like required. You know, it''s going to like, you \",\"startTime\":1733844938,\"endTime\":1733844951},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"know, top out at 25 an hour or something, not have an opportunity to like move to the next step because that sounds great when you''re 18, right? But like, \",\"startTime\":1733844951,\"endTime\":1733844959},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"that''s not the, you''re not going to raise your family on that. \",\"startTime\":1733844959,\"endTime\":1733844963},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right. Well, and I feel like it''s so like, you know, we''ve got this perspective \",\"startTime\":1733844967,\"endTime\":1733844970},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"that students don''t. And so when they''re like, oh, just get a job and I''ll, \",\"startTime\":1733844970,\"endTime\":1733844973},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"you know, and I''m like, I just don''t think you understand how easy that is sometimes, you know? \",\"startTime\":1733844973,\"endTime\":1733844979},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733844974,\"endTime\":1733844974},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"OK, right.\",\"startTime\":1733844979,\"endTime\":1733844980},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"All right, Let''s see. Yeah. Are you already at work? That''s amazing.\",\"startTime\":1733844983,\"endTime\":1733844988},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"You''re ready for the next one.\",\"startTime\":1733844984,\"endTime\":1733844985},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"I mean, I live like a mile from work. I only, I only drive because like I, I \",\"startTime\":1733844990,\"endTime\":1733844992},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"mean, I dropped my daughter at the bus stop and then my son''s with me in the car. \",\"startTime\":1733844992,\"endTime\":1733844997},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"There''s nice parts of living in Port Townsend.\",\"startTime\":1733844999,\"endTime\":1733845001},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah. I used to live 5 minutes from my school and I loved it until I like \",\"startTime\":1733845001,\"endTime\":1733845005},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"had the trick or treaters show up at my house and I was like, no, everybody knows where I live. It''s like, I don''t love this. \",\"startTime\":1733845005,\"endTime\":1733845012},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Oh yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733845008,\"endTime\":1733845010},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Oh, yeah. Like I like, I went to the grocery store the other day and like a \",\"startTime\":1733845011,\"endTime\":1733845014},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"mom like, sees me there and like she burst into tears about how can I help her daughter And yeah, like. \",\"startTime\":1733845014,\"endTime\":1733845020},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Like set up a meeting with me.\",\"startTime\":1733845023,\"endTime\":1733845024},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"You know.\",\"startTime\":1733845023,\"endTime\":1733845024},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Yeah. I was like, could you try emailing or calling me? I understand you work \",\"startTime\":1733845025,\"endTime\":1733845028},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"here at Safeway, but like I''m not currently available. \",\"startTime\":1733845028,\"endTime\":1733845031},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1733845032,\"endTime\":1733845032},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"All right.\",\"startTime\":1733845035,\"endTime\":1733845035},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"How it says I have to share first?\",\"startTime\":1733845036,\"endTime\":1733845037},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"OK perfect, mine says use your second.\",\"startTime\":1733845037,\"endTime\":1733845039},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"What do you care for students as the greatest reason they are not pursuing or thinking about enrolling in a post secondary program? Well it''s funny, I''m like, \",\"startTime\":1733845041,\"endTime\":1733845049},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"I don''t really even know if I hear from them. I mean I think that they can''t \",\"startTime\":1733845049,\"endTime\":1733845053},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"even imagine like most post secondary programs are an hour from here. \",\"startTime\":1733845053,\"endTime\":1733845057},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh, OK.\",\"startTime\":1733845059,\"endTime\":1733845060},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"I guess like live at home and commute an hour but like it just feels so far away for our students. I think like so. \",\"startTime\":1733845063,\"endTime\":1733845070},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I think that can you? Are you still there?\",\"startTime\":1733845072,\"endTime\":1733845075},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Are you still there? You''re frozen on my screen.\",\"startTime\":1733845087,\"endTime\":1733845090},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"There you go.\",\"startTime\":1733845110,\"endTime\":1733845111},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh, good. I was like, you''re frozen. I don''t know.\",\"startTime\":1733845112,\"endTime\":1733845115},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Well, I told you everything, but you probably didn''t get any of it. Yeah. Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1733845115,\"endTime\":1733845119},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I did not I The last thing I heard was that like, everything''s kind of an hour away. \",\"startTime\":1733845118,\"endTime\":1733845122},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"So I mean, that''s just a huge barrier. And then. \",\"startTime\":1733845119,\"endTime\":1733845122},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"And just like, even if they want to go to college, I feel like the affordability issue for my students, like my high school students, like, you know, they''re like 70% free and reduced lunch. So just like, you know, very few of them have \",\"startTime\":1733845128,\"endTime\":1733845141},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"parents who went to college, like, you know, getting through all just those barriers and imagining it is pretty hard for them. \",\"startTime\":1733845141,\"endTime\":1733845149},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I think that we serve, for the most part a pretty privileged population. And \",\"startTime\":1733845148,\"endTime\":1733845152},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"so we''re kind of on the other end of the spectrum. We''ve got a lot of really \",\"startTime\":1733845152,\"endTime\":1733845156},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"high achieving students who know exactly what they want to do and their parents know what they should be doing and you know, they get all the pressure. But \",\"startTime\":1733845156,\"endTime\":1733845165},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I''m just seeing this like hidden population kind of. \",\"startTime\":1733845165,\"endTime\":1733845169},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"In the middle of like, you know, some kids, they definitely know they want to go straight into the workforce or things like that. But then there''s kind of \",\"startTime\":1733845170,\"endTime\":1733845178},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"this group of kids that I don''t think we''re doing a very good job of capturing that definitely have the potential. But like maybe they''re the 1st in their \",\"startTime\":1733845178,\"endTime\":1733845185},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"family to graduate or they just don''t, they don''t really know what their options are. And as much as we try to present that stuff to them, it feels overwhelming \",\"startTime\":1733845185,\"endTime\":1733845193},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"or like, where do we even start? Or you know, just kind of not maintainable. \",\"startTime\":1733845193,\"endTime\":1733845197},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Because we have a whole group of students that are just figuring it out where they''ve got the support system to really guide them through that. \",\"startTime\":1733845198,\"endTime\":1733845205},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Well, at home so.\",\"startTime\":1733845205,\"endTime\":1733845207},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"All right, let''s see here.\",\"startTime\":1733845210,\"endTime\":1733845211},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Oh.\",\"startTime\":1733845215,\"endTime\":1733845215},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Well, thank you. I think something, I mean, that last question actually, I''d \",\"startTime\":1733845217,\"endTime\":1733845220},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"like to like all of your interest before that, I was like, oh, those are just like my students. And so it''s really interesting that you''re like, oh, well, \",\"startTime\":1733845220,\"endTime\":1733845226},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"our student populations are kind of really different, like, you know, demographically in some ways, right? But it''s like, oh, it''s still the same barriers. I just \",\"startTime\":1733845226,\"endTime\":1733845232},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"think that''s really like, I kind of have this feeling of like, well, that''s just kind of my alternative Ed students who like just feel lost and don''t know what they''re doing. And I''m like, no, it''s like, sounds like there''s a more \",\"startTime\":1733845232,\"endTime\":1733845241},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"global problem. \",\"startTime\":1733845241,\"endTime\":1733845244},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Right. Yeah. Well, I think it''s also just becoming more normal to like live \",\"startTime\":1733845242,\"endTime\":1733845246},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"at home later. And some of these goals just like owning a house and things like \",\"startTime\":1733845246,\"endTime\":1733845250},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"that just don''t seem achievable. So, you know, working to go back to school \",\"startTime\":1733845250,\"endTime\":1733845254},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"to maybe earn more of a paycheck, to not get anything out of it in the, you know, I mean, not tangible things that you''re like, OK, like I can graduate from a four year school, get a really great job and own a house within five years. Like that''s really. \",\"startTime\":1733845254,\"endTime\":1733845269},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Depending on where you live or the community, you know, and how much prices of everything are. So yeah, I think that''s it''s tricky. Things are not like \",\"startTime\":1733845270,\"endTime\":1733845280},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"they, they definitely aren''t like they were when my parents were growing up. \",\"startTime\":1733845280,\"endTime\":1733845285},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"And then it''s changed even since, you know, I was a teenager. One thing I learned \",\"startTime\":1733845285,\"endTime\":1733845290},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"is just you gave me perspective on how far some things are. Like we have, we \",\"startTime\":1733845290,\"endTime\":1733845295},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"have about 2000 students on paper, but about 300 of them. \",\"startTime\":1733845295,\"endTime\":1733845300},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"To our Community College and do running start and then a lot of them just kind of trickle straight into either Community College or go to UW or you know, some, some closer colleges. And we have a lot of colleges that are close by. So that \",\"startTime\":1733845301,\"endTime\":1733845316},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"that does present more opportunities than some other places for sure. So I guess \",\"startTime\":1733845316,\"endTime\":1733845321},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"you gave me perspective feeling a little bit lucky about our location. \",\"startTime\":1733845321,\"endTime\":1733845326},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"It''s not so bad.\",\"startTime\":1733845326,\"endTime\":1733845327},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"Well, also it was really nice to talk to you and meet you.\",\"startTime\":1733845329,\"endTime\":1733845332},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"Yeah, it was lovely to meet. Yeah, maybe I''ll see you another time.\",\"startTime\":1733845331,\"endTime\":1733845335},{\"speaker\":\"11476\",\"text\":\"I hope you have a good day. Yeah, All right. Have a good day. Bye.\",\"startTime\":1733845333,\"endTime\":1733845337},{\"speaker\":\"10903\",\"text\":\"OK, bye.\",\"startTime\":1733845337,\"endTime\":1733845338}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.561129+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:28.561129+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 826, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:28.349Z", "session_title": "Uncovering Student Post-Secondary Access Realities", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1323", "name": "Uncovering Student Post-Secondary Access Realities", "tags": [{"name": "HSLC"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('2c5706ed-b95a-4055-9909-8348e9858d14', 'f75f7f16-84b9-41ce-b842-2a77a9dd70b8', '134299', '"[{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"I look forward to having this chat with you. This is a this is a topic near \",\"startTime\":1731963872,\"endTime\":1731963875},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"and dear to my heart and just, you know, this was one requested by the Columbia Selkirk team. \",\"startTime\":1731963875,\"endTime\":1731963881},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, fun. I can''t wait. OK, we got an icebreaker.\",\"startTime\":1731963884,\"endTime\":1731963888},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"All right, I see you. I hear you''re coming in loud and clear. How about me?\",\"startTime\":1731963891,\"endTime\":1731963895},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, you''re coming in. Good. I am trying to do Bluetooth, but whatever, we''ll \",\"startTime\":1731963895,\"endTime\":1731963899},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"skip it. OK, Icebreaker. You could travel anywhere in the world. Where would \",\"startTime\":1731963899,\"endTime\":1731963902},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"you want to go, Mr. Mike? \",\"startTime\":1731963902,\"endTime\":1731963906},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Today I would go to no, today I''m going to absolutely nowhere. I''m staying right \",\"startTime\":1731963907,\"endTime\":1731963911},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"here in my in my new digs. It''s going to be hard for me in the next I''ve I''ve \",\"startTime\":1731963911,\"endTime\":1731963915},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"chosen to live where I wanted to travel to. And so now I don''t want to go anywhere. \",\"startTime\":1731963915,\"endTime\":1731963919},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"But if I had to go somewhere, it would be to go to Italy to drink some good coffee. How about you? \",\"startTime\":1731963919,\"endTime\":1731963927},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"There are a lot of places I do want to travel in the world, but right now I really do want to go to Tahoe and be with you and work and get some of our programming stuff done and go play in the ski and the snow stuff. And I''m, I''m excited for \",\"startTime\":1731963931,\"endTime\":1731963942},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"that and I''m ready to just get stuff done right now. \",\"startTime\":1731963942,\"endTime\":1731963946},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So that part is exciting, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1731963946,\"endTime\":1731963949},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"That''s cool. Those are two non obvious answers that we we both kind of don''t \",\"startTime\":1731963949,\"endTime\":1731963953},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"need to go anywhere except maybe where we are and have a helicopter to be in the same space. Sometimes we want to travel in time and not travel in location. \",\"startTime\":1731963953,\"endTime\":1731963962},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1731963956,\"endTime\":1731963956},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, alright. A standard is a measurement to see where you are in growth or \",\"startTime\":1731963961,\"endTime\":1731963967},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Jeff and your in your own words, what''s the difference between curriculum and a standard? Yeah, I think you and I share an understanding. \",\"startTime\":1731963962,\"endTime\":1731963970},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"in process or in skill level. Whereas curriculum is a thoughtful intentional \",\"startTime\":1731963967,\"endTime\":1731963974},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"plan to get you to growth, which may be towards standards or not are measured by lived or not. \",\"startTime\":1731963974,\"endTime\":1731963986},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"The hints I have under here share that curriculum. It says it''s just one tool \",\"startTime\":1731964000,\"endTime\":1731964004},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"which can be used to help students achieve a standard. So that it''s it''s an \",\"startTime\":1731964004,\"endTime\":1731964007},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"approach, it''s a thoughtful approach as you described it. \",\"startTime\":1731964007,\"endTime\":1731964011},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"But it''s also not the end all.\",\"startTime\":1731964013,\"endTime\":1731964015},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And it''s interesting, mine says consider why it''s essential to distinguish these elements. \",\"startTime\":1731964017,\"endTime\":1731964022},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"I think it''s important to distinguish them because if I, if I''m a, if my job is to be a teacher and follow a policy, is the policy to stay in lockstep with the curriculum or is my responsibility to guide each learner to the standard? \",\"startTime\":1731964022,\"endTime\":1731964036},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"And what I know after having have had this reflection is the goal is to teach to to, to move the learners from can''t to can against the standards through whatever means necessary. \",\"startTime\":1731964036,\"endTime\":1731964049},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"And I think it''s freeing for teachers to know that they''re not stuck to the curriculum, but they are usually stuck to the standards. And then it gets, it''s \",\"startTime\":1731964055,\"endTime\":1731964062},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"more motivating. I think it''s worth mentioning that when you look at high school \",\"startTime\":1731964062,\"endTime\":1731964066},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"math standards, which is my domain, they''re really thoughtful. So I have some \",\"startTime\":1731964066,\"endTime\":1731964069},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"buy in for the standards. I don''t see it as someone is telling me you have to \",\"startTime\":1731964069,\"endTime\":1731964073},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"do this because some bureaucrat told me to like they''re, they''re kind of beautiful. \",\"startTime\":1731964073,\"endTime\":1731964077},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"And so I have I, I have developed a respect for the standards. I don''t have \",\"startTime\":1731964077,\"endTime\":1731964080},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"as much of respect for someone else''s curriculum. And maybe that''s. \",\"startTime\":1731964080,\"endTime\":1731964084},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"The personality quirk for me.\",\"startTime\":1731964087,\"endTime\":1731964088},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Very interesting, your take on that. That resonated with me. And that difference \",\"startTime\":1731964092,\"endTime\":1731964096},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"is the standards and curriculum. It''s important to know the difference because \",\"startTime\":1731964096,\"endTime\":1731964101},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"the curriculum is what we get to choose to adapt or to use as a tool along the way with our students. \",\"startTime\":1731964101,\"endTime\":1731964109},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And inherently, I think we don''t trust it because it''s not written by our students, teacher or teachers or the ones who know our students. And we know our students \",\"startTime\":1731964113,\"endTime\":1731964120},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"better than anybody. \",\"startTime\":1731964120,\"endTime\":1731964124},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So how can these people who don''t know my students have written this curriculum and tell me how to raise my kids? \",\"startTime\":1731964125,\"endTime\":1731964132},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1731964127,\"endTime\":1731964128},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Is the idea and, and yet really well written curriculum today honours that choice that we get to make as the facilitator. And it''s based on sound curricular decisions \",\"startTime\":1731964134,\"endTime\":1731964142},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"around who we are as human beings and what''s good for our thinking and, and what''s developmentally correct and, and challenging us to think in multiple ways and all of that. And so it can be much broader and richer and deeper than \",\"startTime\":1731964142,\"endTime\":1731964155},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"what I would be able to bring as a as the teacher or the guide. But I think \",\"startTime\":1731964155,\"endTime\":1731964159},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it''s important to know the difference between. \",\"startTime\":1731964159,\"endTime\":1731964164},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"The two because curriculum you''re gonna flex it or lean on it harder we adapt it all the time, especially math it''s hilarious as math teachers, we whine about \",\"startTime\":1731964166,\"endTime\":1731964174},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"this and that with the standards and the curriculum and then we go right 40 worksheet practice things in a row for the next 50 days ''cause some of them \",\"startTime\":1731964174,\"endTime\":1731964183},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"might take more than one day, Mike like seriously, the amount of worksheets and practice sheets that we create as high school math teachers to help our kids is ridiculous we pretend that we''re amazing curriculum authors by doing. \",\"startTime\":1731964183,\"endTime\":1731964195},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Worksheet right there. You got something you made because we''re going to make \",\"startTime\":1731964197,\"endTime\":1731964201},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it better. And I think there''s something to be said about the curriculum is \",\"startTime\":1731964201,\"endTime\":1731964205},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"is made to be flexed or bent or used or adapted and we should have that that freedom to do so, but the standards not so much. I should know what it means \",\"startTime\":1731964205,\"endTime\":1731964214},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"for developmentally appropriate student at this grade level to be thinking or mindful of this kind of work and that I should be pushing my kids and showing them more of the things that should be. \",\"startTime\":1731964214,\"endTime\":1731964227},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Appropriately addressed at that time. Yeah, yeah, yeah. Oh, that makes me think \",\"startTime\":1731964229,\"endTime\":1731964234},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"With deep thought across the entire economy and things that are changing. Like \",\"startTime\":1731964231,\"endTime\":1731964234},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"of a lot. All right, I''m ready for the next one. Wait till we get that. Yeah, \",\"startTime\":1731964234,\"endTime\":1731964239},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"I can''t being one local teacher and one local in one classroom know what what what the bar is to hit for precalculus. \",\"startTime\":1731964234,\"endTime\":1731964241},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"we got that. Take turns sharing with Mikey. Give an example of how you have \",\"startTime\":1731964239,\"endTime\":1731964244},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"tailored your have to scroll. Little mini scroll bar. It''s like big for ants. \",\"startTime\":1731964244,\"endTime\":1731964249},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"We might have a responsibility so and and you and I work like we''re thinking maybe about curriculum and pedagogy on mathematics, but writing the standards for AI and education is still an unknown. \",\"startTime\":1731964244,\"endTime\":1731964255},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m scrolling. Have you tailored your teaching method to meet a standard? \",\"startTime\":1731964249,\"endTime\":1731964254},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"An unfinished job like What should people know? I think isn''t quite articulated \",\"startTime\":1731964256,\"endTime\":1731964258},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"yet. \",\"startTime\":1731964258,\"endTime\":1731964260},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, let me read again. Give an example of how you''ve tailored your teaching \",\"startTime\":1731964288,\"endTime\":1731964291},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"method to meet a standard. \",\"startTime\":1731964291,\"endTime\":1731964293},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Would you like me to go first since I''m like capital T teaching math at the moment so I''m more in it. We''re studying trig and the standard I should I like \",\"startTime\":1731964294,\"endTime\":1731964301},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1731964296,\"endTime\":1731964296},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"If I were on right now, I''d I''d tell you the standard that I was teaching towards, but something along the lines of I can model and make predictions from things that are cyclical. \",\"startTime\":1731964301,\"endTime\":1731964312},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"And so my modification was around taking that you and I did you and I hiked on recently that waterfall gets drier and drier and drier and then fills back up and fills back up and fills back up and they get dry and dryer and drier. \",\"startTime\":1731964316,\"endTime\":1731964330},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"So I told the the story of that. I developed a sinusoidal equation to model \",\"startTime\":1731964330,\"endTime\":1731964335},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"it. It was the day that it just started snowing again. So it went from dry, \",\"startTime\":1731964335,\"endTime\":1731964340},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1731964337,\"endTime\":1731964337},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"it went from zero water flow to not 0 water flow and its characteristics. \",\"startTime\":1731964340,\"endTime\":1731964345},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Like looked like it did in November. So I was like drying out and now it''s wetting \",\"startTime\":1731964346,\"endTime\":1731964351},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"up, which isn''t the right word, but it feels and looks the same. So you can \",\"startTime\":1731964351,\"endTime\":1731964355},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"see the two sides under the little sine wave. Are they they''re similar to each \",\"startTime\":1731964355,\"endTime\":1731964359},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"other. And that was interesting. So I like had videos of it at different times \",\"startTime\":1731964359,\"endTime\":1731964363},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"in the in the year and then had them do math around it. When will it be 12 cubic \",\"startTime\":1731964363,\"endTime\":1731964368},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"feet per minute or second? I don''t remember the units that we were playing with, \",\"startTime\":1731964368,\"endTime\":1731964372},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"but. \",\"startTime\":1731964372,\"endTime\":1731964376},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Local problem, A place they had been, a phenomenon that was timely. It was happening \",\"startTime\":1731964379,\"endTime\":1731964382},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"at the moment, but the math was sound. \",\"startTime\":1731964382,\"endTime\":1731964385},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I love it, I love it.\",\"startTime\":1731964385,\"endTime\":1731964387},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"How about you thinking back and we might have to call after this card because I''ve got a 1115 amazing. And I think like we can talk about this through the \",\"startTime\":1731964389,\"endTime\":1731964396},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I can.\",\"startTime\":1731964392,\"endTime\":1731964392},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, OK. I''m thinking of two different ones. One was Hunter''s profits. I rewrote \",\"startTime\":1731964394,\"endTime\":1731964399},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"lens of like you and I are in the the 3 1/2 or the four against this learning target. We both understand the difference between curriculum standards. We''re \",\"startTime\":1731964396,\"endTime\":1731964404},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"a worksheet the next day because this kid who''s from a family that owns a bunch of farmland and knew he was going to be making money owning and running the farm, I just made the next day''s worksheet content right from his farm and was called Hunter. That was his name, Prophets, and it was about being on a farm. \",\"startTime\":1731964399,\"endTime\":1731964415},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"probably also both getting excited about what it means to build personalized curriculum using modern tooling in ways that were previously impossible. And \",\"startTime\":1731964404,\"endTime\":1731964411},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"it makes me think of like if you were to deliver a curricular product to a teacher today. \",\"startTime\":1731964411,\"endTime\":1731964418},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And then the linear questions were all in context around making profits at his farm and. \",\"startTime\":1731964415,\"endTime\":1731964424},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So that was one that was fun to match right to them, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1731964426,\"endTime\":1731964430},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Knowing that they get to personalize it, what would it look like? What would \",\"startTime\":1731964453,\"endTime\":1731964458},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"the what would the levers and dials be for that feature? How cool would that \",\"startTime\":1731964458,\"endTime\":1731964463},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"For me, Mike, that would be my superstar 11 star experience for a teacher is to provide for them their curriculum builder tool that they could talk to me \",\"startTime\":1731964460,\"endTime\":1731964469},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"be? Yeah, Yeah. Cool. Good to know. Let''s stay in it. \",\"startTime\":1731964463,\"endTime\":1731964468},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and I would be like building out and giving them all of the things to build the curriculum or adapt the curriculum to be epic to their own, authored with their own name on it. \",\"startTime\":1731964469,\"endTime\":1731964484},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Better and better. That would be a dream to do that with with teachers, A reflection \",\"startTime\":1731964486,\"endTime\":1731964490},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"questions. It''s 114. \",\"startTime\":1731964490,\"endTime\":1731964494},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Doesn''t apply to us. I think we should skip it, but you can read a second just \",\"startTime\":1731964502,\"endTime\":1731964505},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"to see what I had hoped everyone would get before your last Salkirk adventure. \",\"startTime\":1731964505,\"endTime\":1731964508},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, yeah, yeah, there we go. There we go. And I did. I did listen to anybody \",\"startTime\":1731964506,\"endTime\":1731964511},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"Alright. \",\"startTime\":1731964508,\"endTime\":1731964512},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"who had gotten on on Tuesday this week. All right, dude, you got to run. The \",\"startTime\":1731964511,\"endTime\":1731964515},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"other one I will say is my favorite adoption, and that was when I learned Geogebra and on Friday, Thursday, whatever it was when I learned about it, or Friday when I was gone all day teaching or whatever. Yeah, Thursday I learned about \",\"startTime\":1731964515,\"endTime\":1731964528},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it. Friday I was giving tests and thought it should be grading the next class \",\"startTime\":1731964528,\"endTime\":1731964532},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"period test from last period and just played on Geogebra all day long. \",\"startTime\":1731964532,\"endTime\":1731964536},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Ditched my Lesson plan late Sunday night that I had for Monday morning and gave him some prompts in a note file notebook file of AB CS how to open up Geogebra and do some graphs and tangent curves and drag along and introduce them to the integral symbol. By the end of two days of playing in Geogebra, I had a student \",\"startTime\":1731964540,\"endTime\":1731964557},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"describing to me the fundamental theorem of calculus without having done any more than plain because I gave him some tools and showed him how to do the stuff and visualize what they had learned about. \",\"startTime\":1731964557,\"endTime\":1731964570},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And introduce this new thing called the integral and did nothing. Then show \",\"startTime\":1731964571,\"endTime\":1731964575},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"that it provides a value and the graphical interface of what it looks like. \",\"startTime\":1731964575,\"endTime\":1731964580},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"What that tells me like, like highlights for me is how you as a teacher would refuse to walk in on Monday and give not the right thing for students so much you rewrite what you had planned on Sunday night. Like we as teachers care so \",\"startTime\":1731964581,\"endTime\":1731964593},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"much about showing up with the right thing for the for the actual kids in front of you at the right time based on our best thinking that we won''t accept anything else. So curriculum creators have it really cut out for them. That''s a hard \",\"startTime\":1731964593,\"endTime\":1731964606},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1731964603,\"endTime\":1731964604},{\"speaker\":\"262\",\"text\":\"job. How could you possibly? \",\"startTime\":1731964606,\"endTime\":1731964610},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"How could you know? But you know what? You know what the best was, is because \",\"startTime\":1731964612,\"endTime\":1731964616},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I had done what I had done personally, and it couldn''t stop playing with jojoba. \",\"startTime\":1731964616,\"endTime\":1731964619},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I had to embrace the reality as being a human being that that''s what I wanted to do. More than the other stuff, more than grading papers, more than hanging \",\"startTime\":1731964619,\"endTime\":1731964627},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"on the other meetings. I wanted to play with it. And why not give the kids that \",\"startTime\":1731964627,\"endTime\":1731964630},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"same joy? And how could I curate that space for them? That''s what I came down \",\"startTime\":1731964630,\"endTime\":1731964634},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"to. \",\"startTime\":1731964634,\"endTime\":1731964638},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"All right, you can have.\",\"startTime\":1731964641,\"endTime\":1731964642}]"', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.363908+00', '2025-05-06 19:02:40.363908+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 775, "created_at": "2025-05-06T19:02:40.305Z", "session_title": "Standards vs. Curriculum", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "250", "name": "Standards vs. Curriculum", "tags": [{"name": "Cothinking Classrooms"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
